{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical","id":1530343,"title":"How do you do your Traditions? Good, Bad, or Hypocritical?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-08T22:41:34-08:00","id":1530343,"title":"How do you do your Traditions? Good, Bad, or Hypocritical?","content":"What the title says. Lots of people have OPINIONS on the Technocracy and whether they're the Star Trek utopians or fascist Warhammer 40K in the making. However, we rarely see the Traditions debated with as much fervor when it's very often the case that I believe they're just as confusing in their status for the world.<br /> <br /> For me, I think whether you believe the Traditions are the good guys versus the Technocracy is distilled to one question that even fans can't agree on.<br /> <br /> Do you believe the Traditions have actually learned to have their paradigms live in harmony and want to build a new utopian world where everyone can use whatever magic they want.<br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> Do you believe it's an alliance of convenience and as soon as the Union is done, it's every Tradition for themselves.<br /> <br /> The answer is not clear even in the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T03:56:05-08:00","id":1530359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical#post1530343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer is not clear even in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends when you mean. Like, I think <i>Revised</i> absolutely does lean towards the former pretty overtly. Much of the fiction is precisely about mages coming to mutual understandings across lines of Tradition. Additionally, I think <i>Revised</i> is clear that the second option isn't available. The alliance of convenience was what the old masters were trying, and it failed, and they all (more or less) died.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T04:46:58-08:00","id":1530363,"title":"","content":"What I know about MAGE inclines me to depict the Technocracy as - on the whole - a Good Idea which at some point became a Harsh Reality that grows harsher and harsher by the day.<br /> <br /> Put simply the Traditions - whether as a band of brothers or as an alliance of convenience - demand that one reach an accommodation with your rivals and cooperate for mutual benefit: the Technocracy demands conformity, not mutual consensus, and must therefore crush it\u2019s rivals.<br /> <br /> This wasn\u2019t always the case and most likely will not always be the case, but for the moment the Technocracy is not only the heavy of the piece, it\u2019s budding Tyranny - so when asked to chose between Pluralism and a Monoculture, don\u2019t expect me to chose those who insist that there can be only One.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T04:55:43-08:00","id":1530366,"title":"","content":"I used to think the Technocracy was cool and sleek and the Traditions were lame. In 2024, I'm more inclined to go full First Edition.<br /> <br /> Traditions: Marginalized peoples and the oppressed<br /> <br /> Technocracy: Fascist Western hegemony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T05:30:43-08:00","id":1530372,"title":"","content":"My Traditions are deeply flawed but honorably striving towards worthy goals. Although those on the ground could be forgiven for a hostile view.<br /> <br /> My Technocracy is profoundly flawed and rotting from within but still has idealists and a few honorable members. <br /> <br /> My Desperates are a wildly mixed bag falling apart. Some like the Wu-lung and the Batini are corrupt but unaware of it. Some are to narrow in their focus. Others are beginning to see their mistakes, but unwilling to face them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-09-2024, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T08:07:28-08:00","id":1530378,"title":"","content":"For me, the Traditions have learned how to have their paradigms harmonize, which is what distinguishes them from the Disparates, who at best exist in an alliance of convenience that's likely to fall apart just as soon as the Technocracy is vanquished.<br /> <br /> But that's got nothing to do with \u201cGood, Bad, or Hypocritical\u201d, as you put it in the title. There are, to me, more important factors for what qualifies as \u201cgood\u201d or \u201cbad\u201d than \u201chow well do you work with other mages?\u201d In particular, I tend to view the question of ethics more in terms of \u201chow do you treat Sleepers\u201d? And <i>that's</i> something that <i>everyone</i> (organization-wise) fails on, albeit in different ways. Which gets back to the essential nature of the game: each faction (Technocracy, Traditions, and Disparates) can point to the failings of the other factions and say, \u201cwe don't do that, so we're better than them!\u201d And be half right.<br /> <br /> The failing of the Technocracy is that it tries to force its way of doing things on the Masses. The Traditions claim superiority here in that they view their own way of doing things as promoting freedom; but often, that's just a talking point and the truth is that they only care about the Sleepers in terms of whether and how they can be Awakened. The Disparates, meanwhile, are very good at taking care of their people; but if you're not part of whatever protected class a given Craft takes responsibility for, tough. This contrasts with the Technocracy, which at least in theory tries to take care of <i>everyone </i>\u2014 albeit in their aforementioned \u201cmoral busybodies\u201d way.<br /> <br /> So again, everyone has dirty hands; nobody gets it right, and everyone \u2014 Traditions, Technocracy, and Disparates, can do better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-09-2024, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T09:04:24-08:00","id":1530380,"title":"","content":"By the way, we've discussed something <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1385487-confession-time-i-just-can-t-get-into-the-traditions\">very similar to this</a> before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-09T09:09:31-08:00","id":1530383,"title":"","content":"I'm going full First Edition with Mage<br /> <br /> Traditions are flawed Chaotic Good heroic rebels<br /> <br /> Technocracy are Lawful Evil totalitarian communist despots<br /> <br /> The Disparate Alliance flat out does not exist. Hollow Ones are an orphan craft that's on the verge of becoming the Tenth Tradition","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T08:01:42-08:00","id":1530443,"title":"","content":"I have nearly an opposite approach to Matt here. My Traditions are flawed in concept and in execution. Any good done by them is done by individuals or by accident. Good is never done by the organization itself, as they are deeply out of touch and fundamentally reactionary groups, at least at the top. My Technocratic Union is correct in concept and flawed in execution. No theoretically perfect organization can survive contact with reality, as we have ego and ambition. For every genius doctor and noble crusader for human enlightenment, there is a mad scientist and a power hungry White-suit. Of course, not every convention is as corrupt as every other, same as the Traditions. As for the Crafts, they don't come up much, if they did, I'd portray them as similar to the various Traditions, just far less influential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28099-cardassianartistry","name":"CardassianArtistry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28099_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T09:04:13-08:00","id":1530454,"title":"","content":"Note that what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28099-cardassianartistry\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28099_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28099\" data-vbnamecard=\"28099\">CardassianArtistry</a> is describing doesn't really have much to do with how well or poorly the Traditions' various styles of Magick interact with each other. You can have the Traditions operating within a common framework of Magickal beliefs that allows their various approaches to harmonize with each other, and <i>still</i> have each Tradition be flawed in both concept and execution. <br /> <br /> In that regard, I view the Traditions as having learned to have their paradigms coexist in harmony, as distinct from the Disparates who are at best an alliance of convenience. But that doesn't make the Traditions \u201cgood\u201d or the Disparates \u201cbad\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T13:53:27-08:00","id":1530475,"title":"","content":"1st and 2nd Edition seemed to have the idea that paradigm is something that everyone is aware is just a crutch. The difference between Hedge Magic and True Magic is clear.<br /> <br /> A Hedge Mage Theruge believes his powers come from angels. A Celestial Choirster knows his powers come from within....but angels certainly help.<br /> <br /> Revised is that the Mages all ignorant of this even at Arete 5.<br /> <br /> Which massively changes the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> Because it adds a massive layer of hypocrisy to the Technocracy and other groups that are murdering people because they wear a different brand of clothing but you know is still fundamentally the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T17:29:42-08:00","id":1530504,"title":"","content":"Personally, I find the notion that one's deeply held beliefs should be thought of \u201cwhich brand of clothing do you wear?\u201d to be problematic \u2014 which could be part of the failing of the Traditions: by embracing the notion that \u201cit's all just Willworking anyway; your convictions are something you just need to get over\u201d, they're potentially undermining the essence of Magick. <br /> <br /> In short, yes; MRev <i>did</i> fundamentally change the nature of the Ascension War; but I think it was a change for the better, as the result is more nuanced and meaningful that 1e/2e's comparatively bland \u201cthe Traditions are right and everyone who disagrees with them is wrong\u201d. Though to be fair, it wasn't until M20 that the Traditions stopped being the default heroes of the game, and are now as much fair game for critique as anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T17:33:11-08:00","id":1530506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530504#post1530504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I find the notion that one's deeply held beliefs should be thought of \u201cwhich brand of clothing do you wear?\u201d to be problematic \u2014 which could be part of the failing of the Traditions: by embracing the notion that \u201cit's all just Willworking anyway; your convictions are something you just need to get over\u201d, they're potentially undermining the essence of Magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>By contrast, I feel like Mage is anti-fundamentalism and pro-tolerance. If you believe that a Dreamspeaker is awful and wrong because of his paradigm, you aren't Ascending.<br /> <br /> Mass Ascension is built on mutual respect.<br /> <br /> But I think that got lost in all editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T17:36:43-08:00","id":1530507,"title":"","content":"Mutual respect is one thing; \u201cin order to progress, you must give up your beliefs\u201d is something else entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T18:06:30-08:00","id":1530513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530507#post1530507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mutual respect is one thing; \u201cin order to progress, you must give up your beliefs\u201d is something else entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it depends on how you define it because in Revised, they're still WRONG.<br /> <br /> You can absolutely believe in the One, Do, and Ether but there is a common origin of magics and that isn't changed. Revised just mages ignorant of how their powers worked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T18:23:43-08:00","id":1530518,"title":"","content":"MRev also leaned <i>heavily </i>into the notion that the Traditions agree that they're all doing the same thing with different window dressing; which, if you buy the notion that the beliefs <i>are</i> merely window dressing, clashes with the idea that mages don't know what they're doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T18:44:17-08:00","id":1530521,"title":"","content":"fair point. You have me there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T00:36:08-08:00","id":1530539,"title":"","content":"I like shades of gray and I\u2019m fine with depicting both Traditions and the Technocracy as well intentioned yet flawed heroes. I\u2019m also fine with a game that has Traditions as heroes and the Technocracy as oppressive villains. <br /> <br /> As for the goodness of the Traditions, I like to have them lean in the good direction, keeping in mind that power corrupts and when you\u2019re in an alliance against an oppressive authority, every member of the alliance can honestly claim to oppose oppression and value tolerance and coexistence. If one of those factions rose to dominance themselves - they may be the ones doing the oppression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T01:54:34-08:00","id":1530541,"title":"","content":"Everyone portrays the traditions differently. As a general rule, I believe that both organizations have good intentions but are deeply flawed in their execution due to arrogance and pride, just like the very mages that form them. Good or bad is something that, to me, applies only on an individual level for each mage. The organizations as a whole try to do good, but more often than not get mixed results and always cause some harm, either intended or unintended. <br /> For something more specific, I represent the traditions as having a deep rift between the younger mages on Earth and the out-of-touch elders in the horizon realms. The avatar storm alleviated the problem a bit (by basically killing or making most elders disappear), but it still persists, and it's reaching a breaking point.<br /> Most young mages reject the violent conflict or &quot;crusader&quot; mentality against the technocracy. There's no denying the horrible things they have done and they must be opposed when they do wrong, but there's also no denying the good they have brought. Also, let's be honest, they may not have won the ascension war, yet, but they are the ones on the top right now. Just how realistic it is to confront them directly?<br /> As such, most younger mages see the technocratic paradigm not as something to destroy, but as something to make it their own and integrate into their paradigms. Their ultimate objective is to stretch it and make it more flexible, creating a world of wonder and possibility. The old guard of the traditions are mostly stuck in their old ways and don't like this attitude at all, their answer ranges from scolding to outright declaring many of these mages traitors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T05:27:33-08:00","id":1530546,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the official stance of <b>Lore of the Traditions</b> is that the Traditions had problems in the past, but have seen the errors of their ways and are each undergoing a reformation that returns them to the role of \u201cdefault good guys\u201d. <br /> <br /> It's <i>not</i> how I do things in my Mage setting, because it involves a lot of whitewashing of the more problematic elements of each Tradition. My go-to example of this is how the writer of the Verbena chapter decided to base her take on the Verbena on real-world Wicca, but deviated from that on the trans issue: \u201cSo, there is some very weird transphobia that pops up in witchcraft spaces, and I really wanted to push back on that.\u201d<a href=\"https://youtu.be/DLwE03kvdYM?si=OsOc6akQYMxWI8st\" target=\"_blank\"><sup>4:54</sup></a>. So the Verbena are based on real-world witchcraft, except when that clashes with trans rights. Similar issues crop up in <i>every</i> Tradition, with the book deviating from the real-world inspirations for each of them to provide a more rosy picture. In general, the \u201cRose-colored Glasses\u201d Flaw isn't specific to the Technocracy; but it's not something that the <i>writers</i> should succumb to. <br /> <br /> And again, the issue of whether they're good, bad, or hypocritical isn't determined by how well the Traditions get along with each other; it's determined by matters such as whether witches are transphobic \u2014 issues internal to each Tradition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T06:09:44-08:00","id":1530548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530546#post1530546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, the official stance of <b>Lore of the Traditions</b> is that the Traditions had problems in the past, but have seen the errors of their ways and are each undergoing a reformation that returns them to the role of \u201cdefault good guys\u201d.<br /> <br /> It's <i>not</i> how I do things in my Mage setting, because it involves a lot of whitewashing of the more problematic elements of each Tradition. My go-to example of this is how the writer of the Verbena chapter decided to base her take on the Verbena on real-world Wicca, but deviated from that on the trans issue: \u201cSo, there is some very weird transphobia that pops up in witchcraft spaces, and I really wanted to push back on that.\u201d<a href=\"https://youtu.be/DLwE03kvdYM?si=OsOc6akQYMxWI8st\" target=\"_blank\"><sup>4:54</sup></a>. So the Verbena are based on real-world witchcraft, except when that clashes with trans rights. Similar issues crop up in <i>every</i> Tradition, with the book deviating from the real-world inspirations for each of them to provide a more rosy picture. In general, the \u201cRose-colored Glasses\u201d Flaw isn't specific to the Technocracy; but it's not something that the <i>writers</i> should succumb to.<br /> <br /> And again, the issue of whether they're good, bad, or hypocritical isn't determined by how well the Traditions get along with each other; it's determined by matters such as whether witches are transphobic \u2014 issues internal to each Tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Random aside but this shows up in the recent Krakoan X-men Excalibur that has always had a pagan mystical tradition bent and association with the RL version. Tini Howard (who helped wrote WINTER'S TEETH) made it a point that a lot of the British witches were extremely bigoted against Mutants. Justifying it with the same nonsense that, well, real racist and transphobic nonsense of RL pagan groiups that the idealized past treatment of British magical groups sometimes glossed over.<br /> <br /> It was absolutely deliberate on her part and from a similar school of thought as you.<br /> <br /> I don't have any problem with the idea that the &quot;good guys&quot; don't have to platform bigotry. The Black Furies can absolutely have no problem with trans issues nor any other RL prejudice.<br /> <br /> Why? Because you can do whatever you want with your fictional groups. However, you should acknowledge the RL concerns. The Celestial Choir makes NO SENSE if they're not ecumenists as the &quot;big tent&quot; for all religious monotheistic or monist (not the same thing) mages but you better explain why that came about and how it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 02-11-2024, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T06:46:39-08:00","id":1530549,"title":"","content":"Again though, you're coming from the <i>assumption</i> that the Traditions are the \u201cgood guys\u201d; and that <i>therefore</i> it makes sense to purge them of the more offensive negative qualities. I don't make that assumption, any more than I assume that the Technocrats are the \u201cbad guys\u201d. <i>Everyone</i> gets their virtues and failings, whether they be individuals or factions; and the players then decide which if any of those factions the protagonists align with, why, and to what extent.<br /> <br /> And one option that's available is \u201cI align with faction X because I agree with enough of what they believe to work with them; but they have problems, and I'm going to try to reform them to fix those problems.\u201d In the Verbena example, it's entirely possible for the Verbena as a whole to be transphobic, but for the Verbena <i>protagonist</i> to be the exception who pushes back on it. <br /> <br /> Since you mentioned the Celestial Chorus, my problem with how <i>they're </i>presented isn't that they're ecumenical; it's that they're pseudo-Theosophic with monotheistic trappings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T12:46:11-08:00","id":1530576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530549#post1530549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again though, you're coming from the <i>assumption</i> that the Traditions are the \u201cgood guys\u201d; and that <i>therefore</i> it makes sense to purge them of the more offensive negative qualities. I don't make that assumption, any more than I assume that the Technocrats are the \u201cbad guys\u201d. <i>Everyone</i> gets their virtues and failings, whether they be individuals or factions; and the players then decide which if any of those factions the protagonists align with, why, and to what extent.</div> </div> </div> </div>To explain why I put the Traditions as the good guys as an assumption, I feel like there's a bad look to both sidings what the factions immediately invoke:<br /> <br /> 1. Western capitalism and the Military Industrial Complex.<br /> 2. The oppressed peoples of the world and their traditional culture.<br /> <br /> A lot of fans see the Ascension War as very much a kind of &quot;these are not related to the current struggles and oppressions of RL, Mages are whining over magic while real people are suffering&quot; (and this is essentially the tact that MAGE: REVISED took when describing the Ascenison War).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And one option that's available is \u201cI align with faction X because I agree with enough of what they believe to work with them; but they have problems, and I'm going to try to reform them to fix those problems.\u201d In the Verbena example, it's entirely possible for the Verbena as a whole to be transphobic, but for the Verbena <i>protagonist</i> to be the exception who pushes back on it.<br /> <br /> Since you mentioned the Celestial Chorus, my problem with how <i>they're </i>presented isn't that they're ecumenical; it's that they're pseudo-Theosophic with monotheistic trappings. </div> </div> </div>My concern with this is that if most Verbena are transphobic, this platforms hate speech. It's sort of the Swords of Heimdall problem over in Woof-Woof: The Barking. The Swords of Heimdall were ALWAYS meant to be a repulsive villain faction for the PCs to oppose. However, it permanently tainted the tribe with association in a lot of fans minds and actually appealed to white supremacists who showed up to LARPS playing SoH characters.<br /> <br /> Basically, I worry if you say, &quot;Yes, most Verbena are Transphobes&quot; then that will filter down into characters and possibly even get coopted.<br /> <br /> I suppose it's something to ask at tables as part of lines and discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T14:03:45-08:00","id":1530588,"title":"","content":"By Uno, I hope not, because this subject is already leaving me with post-traumatic stress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T16:43:27-08:00","id":1530594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CT Phipps</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of fans see the Ascension War as very much a kind of \u201cthese are not related to the current struggles and oppressions of RL, Mages are whining over magic while real people are suffering\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes; and others see the division as occurring along other lines. And these are all caps ways to look at it; singling out one (such as the one you single out) as fundamentally being more valid than the others largely undercuts the stated purpose of this topic, as it attempts to shut down our minimize alternate takes. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> On the Verbena thing:<br /> <br /> In the 80s, there was a big \u201cDungeons and Dragons\u201d scare, with reports about kids doing insane things after playing the game and intimations that the game was messing with children's minds and making them behave irrationally. That turned out not to be the case; the few instances where kids <i>did </i>behave irrationally after playing D&amp;D, it was later shown that they were <i>already </i>mentally unstable before they ever cracked open a book. <br /> <br /> In a similar way, the Swords of Heimdall aren't responsible for turning people into skinheads. The people that you described <i>already were</i> skinheads. <br /> <br /> In particular, <b>Mage</b> isn't <b>Werewolf</b>. At its finest, <b>Mage</b> promotes a level of maturity and introspection that <b>Werewolf</b> doesn't. A core theme of <b>Mage</b> is to encourage its players to think for themselves and to take responsibility for their own, personal choices. When you sugarcoat things and try to push a simplistic \u201cus good; them evil\u201d narrative onto the <b>Mage</b> gamers, you undercut that. <br /> <br /> And there's evidence that \u201call of the factions are f'd up; it's up to you to decide for yourself\u201d has been part of <b>Mage</b> from the very beginning: the very first supplement, <b>Book of Chantries</b>, deliberately portrayed <i>every</i> Chantry in the book as screwed up in its own unique way; the Traditions were not spared from this treatment. Brucato is on record stating that that was a deliberate choice, specifically <i>because</i> he didn't want any of the factions to hold a monopoly on ethics. And likewise, from the very beginning he was working to add nuance to the Technocracy so that it wouldn't merely be an oppressive monolith: in <b>Book of Shadows</b>, we were shown how an agent of the New World Order could be a good guy while a Cultist of Ecstasy could be a bad guy, with both of them playing their respective factions more or less straight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T19:44:47-08:00","id":1530601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530594#post1530594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes; and others see the division as occurring along other lines. And these are all caps ways to look at it; singling out one (such as the one you single out) as fundamentally being more valid than the others largely undercuts the stated purpose of this topic, as it attempts to shut down our minimize alternate takes.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> On the Verbena thing:<br /> <br /> In the 80s, there was a big \u201cDungeons and Dragons\u201d scare, with reports about kids doing insane things after playing the game and intimations that the game was messing with children's minds and making them behave irrationally. That turned out not to be the case; the few instances where kids <i>did </i>behave irrationally after playing D&amp;D, it was later shown that they were <i>already </i>mentally unstable before they ever cracked open a book.<br /> <br /> In a similar way, the Swords of Heimdall aren't responsible for turning people into skinheads. The people that you described <i>already were</i> skinheads.<br /> <br /> In particular, <b>Mage</b> isn't <b>Werewolf</b>. At its finest, <b>Mage</b> promotes a level of maturity and introspection that <b>Werewolf</b> doesn't. A core theme of <b>Mage</b> is to encourage its players to think for themselves and to take responsibility for their own, personal choices. When you sugarcoat things and try to push a simplistic \u201cus good; them evil\u201d narrative onto the <b>Mage</b> gamers, you undercut that.<br /> <br /> And there's evidence that \u201call of the factions are f'd up; it's up to you to decide for yourself\u201d has been part of <b>Mage</b> from the very beginning: the very first supplement, <b>Book of Chantries</b>, deliberately portrayed <i>every</i> Chantry in the book as screwed up in its own unique way; the Traditions were not spared from this treatment. Brucato is on record stating that that was a deliberate choice, specifically <i>because</i> he didn't want any of the factions to hold a monopoly on ethics. And likewise, from the very beginning he was working to add nuance to the Technocracy so that it wouldn't merely be an oppressive monolith: in <b>Book of Shadows</b>, we were shown how an agent of the New World Order could be a good guy while a Cultist of Ecstasy could be a bad guy, with both of them playing their respective factions more or less straight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fantastic post.<br /> <br /> +1 smiley face.<br /> <br /> BUT I feel it could go too far.<br /> <br /> Because, really...it's WRONG to teach that fascists are morally equivalent to the people who oppose them. Not just wrong ethically but just dumb from a philosophical standpoint.<br /> <br /> And I feel like the Technocracy can't be divorced from the fact its ideology is what causes wealth inequality, global warming, and so much.<br /> <br /> Individuals may be good but I think it might be best to make it so the Technocracy....should go for the betterment of the world.<br /> <br /> The question then becomes whether the Traditions are worth keeping with this stance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T03:09:44-08:00","id":1530624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530601#post1530601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fantastic post.<br /> <br /> +1 smiley face.<br /> <br /> BUT I feel it could go too far.<br /> <br /> Because, really...it's WRONG to teach that fascists are morally equivalent to the people who oppose them. Not just wrong ethically but just dumb from a philosophical standpoint.<br /> <br /> And I feel like the Technocracy can't be divorced from the fact its ideology is what causes wealth inequality, global warming, and so much.<br /> <br /> Individuals may be good but I think it might be best to make it so the Technocracy....should go for the betterment of the world.<br /> <br /> The question then becomes whether the Traditions are worth keeping with this stance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand what you mean. However, I think it's all about how you present it. Showing shades of gray is not the same as moral equivalency. It's important to show how flawed each organization is and call it when they do something wrong, even if individual members are good and ethical. <br /> <br /> In my games, I always let my players know in unambiguous terms that the technocracy, by their admission, <b>does not believe in democracy</b>. They are an authoritarian organization fully committed to having an elite group rule over the rest. I always point at China to see what the world would become if they could take over, only it would be much more extreme. That the technocracy is changing its ways to a kinder, gentler, and more open-minded organization doesn't change the fact that this belief is deeply ingrained and still present, a good tyrant is still a tyrant. They may have, for the most part, abandoned the colonizer and imperialist mindset of their forefathers, but they have substituted it for a paternalistic and condescending view in which they still believe they have to &quot;guide&quot; sleepers to the correct path. The methodology has changed, but not the main objective. <br /> <br /> Regarding the traditions, one thing that the books have pointed out and that I've seen very few people mention (except here) is this: <b>many in the traditions still adhere to outdated and harmful social conventions</b>. It is pretty clear that some traditions have strict social and gender roles as part of their paradigms, their underdog status does not make them immune to some type of bigotry. In fact, it is pointed out right that the technocracy can be much more accepting of transgender and other LGBtQ communities. The traditions are changing their approach, sure, but it is also important to not forget that their name includes tradition in it and there are plenty of mages who take it as gospel not to be questioned or challenged. That's why one of the central conflicts in my games is between the younger mages trying to reconcile their cultural traditions with the modern world and old mages trying to preserve the &quot;purity&quot; of tradition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T11:23:15-08:00","id":1530657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530576#post1530576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To explain why I put the Traditions as the good guys as an assumption, I feel like there's a bad look to both sidings what the factions immediately invoke:<br /> <br /> 1. Western capitalism and the Military Industrial Complex.<br /> 2. The oppressed peoples of the world and their traditional culture.<br /> <br /> A lot of fans see the Ascension War as very much a kind of &quot;these are not related to the current struggles and oppressions of RL, Mages are whining over magic while real people are suffering&quot; (and this is essentially the tact that MAGE: REVISED took when describing the Ascenison War).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> My concern with this is that if most Verbena are transphobic, this platforms hate speech. It's sort of the Swords of Heimdall problem over in Woof-Woof: The Barking. The Swords of Heimdall were ALWAYS meant to be a repulsive villain faction for the PCs to oppose. However, it permanently tainted the tribe with association in a lot of fans minds and actually appealed to white supremacists who showed up to LARPS playing SoH characters.<br /> <br /> Basically, I worry if you say, &quot;Yes, most Verbena are Transphobes&quot; then that will filter down into characters and possibly even get coopted.<br /> <br /> I suppose it's something to ask at tables as part of lines and discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a WEREWOLF man, I just want to say \u2026 that should be \u2018Wolf-woof: The Yelping\u2019. Wolves don\u2019t bark and neither do we.\ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T12:36:14-08:00","id":1530663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530601#post1530601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fantastic post.<br /> <br /> +1 smiley face.<br /> <br /> BUT I feel it could go too far.<br /> <br /> Because, really...it's WRONG to teach that fascists are morally equivalent to the people who oppose them. Not just wrong ethically but just dumb from a philosophical standpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the situation is one where one side has gone full fascist and the other has gone full opposition, I agree. That's not Mage though.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy has not cornered the market on fascism, totalitarianism, authoritarianism, or any of the other tyrannical isms. There are quite a few in the Traditions with proclivities in that direction as well. There are also key Traditions characters who are explicitly terrorists. Well intentioned extremism (and also not-so-well intentioned extremism) are common elements of Mage. Nor has any faction completely fallen completely down the fascism hill either, at least not by default (though depending on how far you push the authoritarian Technocracy slider, it may not be very long). It oversimplifies Mage to depict the Technocracy that way, or to lionize the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Also, I think its very important to keep at least some focus on how any mage or faction of mages can fall down that path. Most of what makes the Technocracy bad comes not from what they want to accomplish but how they are willing to do to accomplish it. The Traditions are not insulated from that, and their goal for the world - a place where myriad paradigms can be true at the same time - could be its own brand of dystopian nightmare. A very common question most mage's face sooner or later is: &quot;How far are you willing to go when you know you are right?.&quot; Fewer ask the important follow up questions like &quot;How sure are you that you are right?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I feel like the Technocracy can't be divorced from the fact its ideology is what causes wealth inequality, global warming, and so much. </div> </div> </div>The metaphysics of Mage do not play well with global warming, to the point that trying to put the blame for it on a faction (any faction) ends up opening a whole bunch of questions that make Mage uncomfortable for some. I've seen threads where this issue spoils the game for people. Same for vaccines. Unsurprisingly, a game about subjective reality breaks down when we look at it closely and this is one of those places.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T13:31:06-08:00","id":1530753,"title":"","content":"In my vision and the picture of MtA story and setting that is used by me, the Nine Magical Traditions are unified, and these woman, girls, man, and boys have clear and honest intentions, and reasonable goals. The average Cabal - including single Tradition Cabals and Fellowships - is schooled and aware of both wider politics and also the various magical theories and approaches. The Traditions and individual Mage still have their own hypocrisies and problems, but overall they are oriented towards goodness and responsibility to at least some considerable extent, no matter the circumstances.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T04:12:40-08:00","id":1530798,"title":"","content":"As far as i am concerned, the average tradition mage, to put it mildly, is affected, in terms of morality, by having so much power without drawbacks.<br /> <br /> Let us say that the average, using the mathematical definition of the word, mage of the Traditions, not counting nephandi infiltrators!, has a humanity of around 6, to put it in vampire terms.<br /> <br /> By way of comparison, the average vampire, rounding down literally everyone, has a humanity of 5, in my own view anyway. (even ignoring those on paths of enlightenment)<br /> <br /> In short, the average mage is better than bloodsucking fiends, but not by that much. Of course, the answer would vary, with regard to individual tradition<br /> <br /> Of course hypocrisy is a natural part of humanity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T07:39:17-08:00","id":1530814,"title":"","content":"I'm racking my brain here and a question comes to mind: What differentiates good from evil in this case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T09:19:40-08:00","id":1530826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530814#post1530814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm racking my brain here and a question comes to mind: What differentiates good from evil in this case?</div> </div> </div> </div>The readers own values.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T17:22:38-08:00","id":1530854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530814#post1530814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm racking my brain here and a question comes to mind: What differentiates good from evil in this case?</div> </div> </div> </div>In all honesty, i am interpreting from two perspectives? a) their relative amorality compared to the most basic stuff (still kill lie, abuse), b) what they are willing to do for the sake of ideology. Which still comes out with the above list.<br /> <br /> Mind you,i highly doubt mine is the canon interpretation. This is just my own view, for which i said, simplistically, &quot;humanity 6 for the 50th percentile&quot;<br /> <br /> Alternatively: I interpret them based on how they would be seen by most people of their era and location","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T23:58:07-08:00","id":1530874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530814#post1530814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm racking my brain here and a question comes to mind: What differentiates good from evil in this case?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask 10 mages and you will get 10 different answers, different ideologies imply different moralities. That said, my baseline for a &quot;moral&quot; mage depends on the following factors: How much do they care about sleepers, how much do they care about the consequences of their actions, and how much do they care about pursuing their ideology regardless of the means. A good mage is selfless, responsible, and cares about how things are done, and not just the objective. An evil mage is a selfish person with no regard for the common person and how their actions hurt others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 02-15-2024, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T01:33:46-08:00","id":1530878,"title":"","content":"A good mage will work to achieve their goals with minimal collateral damage. So will a shrewd one even if they are evil. In this case the difference would be in what would be needed for the Mage to throw caution to the winds. <br /> <br /> Even the 3rd season Star Trek show with Lincoln and the rock monster got that difference right. The decent folk were motivated by community and responsibility. The Villains by personal gain. Of course in Mage: the Ascension you also have to decide if your community of Mages is working on a worthwhile goal. Or as they said in the 1960s &quot;Justice, or Just Us?&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T04:20:02-08:00","id":1530889,"title":"","content":"I also think it largely depends on how much you think<b> Self-Determination</b> is a thing. The binary between Freedom versus Security doesn't actually exist as recent decades have proven. It is, however, used as an excuse by the powers that be to oppress people in the name of the latter. It is the Technocracy's big argument, though, and the one they use the most against the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Basically, how much does a choice between a life of comfort and safety versus being able to do what you want, believe what you want, and live how you want matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T07:45:29-08:00","id":1530902,"title":"","content":"Simple political binaries rarely present perfectly anyways. Even if side A is intrinsically evil and side B contains ways of being good, that doesn't mean every way of being on side B is good. Plenty of evil can be done in the name of fighting evil, and much more can be done when fighting something that isn't wholly evil.<br /> <br /> Usually the real issues are the underlying reasons behind the discussion, which makes things much more complicated. A worthwhile conversation about freedom vs security, for instance, will not place either Freedom or Security as objectively good ends in their own right, and will instead focus on the deeper goods, like human value and dignity, that both sides (hopefully) are trying to uphold. <br /> <br /> Which touches on one of the frequent tragedies of the Technocracy (and to a lesser extent the Traditions): they do fight for humanity, but they're always at risk of forgetting of why humanity is important. That's why the Syndicate often focuses on human statistics rather than individual wants, and the NWO often tries to manipulate humanity into more controllable forms. Indeed one of the classic principles of the villainous Technocracy is: Humanity is so important that all threats to it must be destroyed, including humanity.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T09:00:03-08:00","id":1530906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530902#post1530902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple political binaries rarely present perfectly anyways. Even if side A is intrinsically evil and side B contains ways of being good, that doesn't mean every way of being on side B is good. Plenty of evil can be done in the name of fighting evil, and much more can be done when fighting something that isn't wholly evil.<br /> <br /> Usually the real issues are the underlying reasons behind the discussion, which makes things much more complicated. A worthwhile conversation about freedom vs security, for instance, will not place either Freedom or Security as objectively good ends in their own right, and will instead focus on the deeper goods, like human value and dignity, that both sides (hopefully) are trying to uphold.<br /> <br /> Which touches on one of the frequent tragedies of the Technocracy (and to a lesser extent the Traditions): they do fight for humanity, but they're always at risk of forgetting of why humanity is important. That's why the Syndicate often focuses on human statistics rather than individual wants, and the NWO often tries to manipulate humanity into more controllable forms. Indeed one of the classic principles of the villainous Technocracy is: Humanity is so important that all threats to it must be destroyed, including humanity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that in this case it is more like the prerogative that society is not capable of taking responsibility for its own choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T09:51:43-08:00","id":1530908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530902#post1530902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which touches on one of the frequent tragedies of the Technocracy (and to a lesser extent the Traditions): they do fight for humanity, but they're always at risk of forgetting of why humanity is important. That's why the Syndicate often focuses on human statistics rather than individual wants, and the NWO often tries to manipulate humanity into more controllable forms. Indeed one of the classic principles of the villainous Technocracy is: Humanity is so important that all threats to it must be destroyed, including humanity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The hubris of mages is that they claim that Mass Ascension can only come from above as a gift handed down versus a hand up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-15T13:16:15-08:00","id":1530924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530908#post1530908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The hubris of mages is that they claim that Mass Ascension can only come from above as a gift handed down versus a hand up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally i tone down the whole ascension thing and treat it like wraiths treat Transcendence. That is, some very much seek it, other do not, some may not believe it is a thing.<br /> I treat mass Ascension as the same. Some genuinely want to give it to the masses, others use it as propaganda because it sounds better than &quot;damnit i just don't want paradox&quot; but by and large i also tone it down. Even if it comes to just helping sleepers you can do so with any number of ways without invoking ascension","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T02:45:32-08:00","id":1531181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530908#post1530908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The hubris of mages is that they claim that Mass Ascension can only come from above as a gift handed down versus a hand up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, is it hubris if it's true? <br /> Most of humanity is not awakened, they're metaphysically blind, and mages have peeked beyond the platonic cave, even if they ended with massively different views of what it means, they still understand more than 99.9% of people. <br /> <br /> How could humanity achieve mass ascension on it's own while it does not even understand that it is a possibility? <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> On that matter, the answer of the traditions is the less hubris-y one, since they want for mankind to accept the reality of magic and the possibilitied it allows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T09:35:02-08:00","id":1531201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1531181#post1531181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, is it hubris if it's true?<br /> Most of humanity is not awakened, they're metaphysically blind, and mages have peeked beyond the platonic cave, even if they ended with massively different views of what it means, they still understand more than 99.9% of people.<br /> <br /> How could humanity achieve mass ascension on it's own while it does not even understand that it is a possibility?<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> On that matter, the answer of the traditions is the less hubris-y one, since they want for mankind to accept the reality of magic and the possibilitied it allows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. I feel that mage the awakening is more realistic than Ascension in this regard (and the others that I already mentioned)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T14:26:00-08:00","id":1531216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530908#post1530908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The hubris of mages is that they claim that Mass Ascension can only come from above as a gift handed down versus a hand up.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is your distinction between a hand down vs a hand up? Are we talking about the way mages go about Mass Ascension, or that they try at all?<br /> <br /> I think there are ways mages could pursue Mass Ascension that are less arrogant than others. All of them run into a serious problem built in to Mage, though, which is that the very idea of Consensual Reality pushes mages to objectify people.<br /> <br /> Trying to alter the Consensus means treating regular people's beliefs, desires, perceptions, and lived experiences as pieces on a game board. The Technocracy exemplifies this, but the Traditions aren't that far behind. To change the world, even for the benefit of the people, they have to override the desires of the people.<br /> <br /> Of course, in many situations it is good to challenge people's beliefs, desires, perceptions, or lived experiences. Teaching comes to mind. But teachers, ideally, are teaching things they themselves believe to be true and beneficial. Mages are on much shakier ground.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1531181#post1531181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, is it hubris if it's true?<br /> <br /> Most of humanity is not awakened, they're metaphysically blind, and mages have peeked beyond the platonic cave, even if they ended with massively different views of what it means, they still understand more than 99.9% of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>But is it true? Mages have gained insight into the nature of reality. They haven't gained any special insight into morality or the nature of humanity. At best they have the ability to see additional ways the world could be, but they have no additional authority to determine what should be.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-21T18:32:23-08:00","id":1531262,"title":"","content":"The Maudaders are insane, the Fallen are evil, the Union is a fascist state, and the Traditions are ideological terrorists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T20:00:02-08:00","id":1531332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1531262#post1531262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Maudaders are insane, the Fallen are evil, the Union is a fascist state, and the Traditions are ideological terrorists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not how I interpret it but is certainly fun. But who is the lighter shade of black? Fascists or the Bolsheviks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T20:02:40-08:00","id":1531333,"title":"","content":"Doesn't matter, if you're not with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T20:24:55-08:00","id":1531334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1531332#post1531332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not how I interpret it but is certainly fun. But who is the lighter shade of black? Fascists or the Bolsheviks?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say always choose the non-fascists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T06:36:43-08:00","id":1531353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1531334#post1531334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say always choose the non-fascists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree, but also point out that it is academic. It is quite possible to oppose both with a clear conscience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-23T18:31:00-08:00","id":1531397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1531332#post1531332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not how I interpret it but is certainly fun. But who is the lighter shade of black? Fascists or the Bolsheviks?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more of a Fascists v. Stalinist situation, where one is catastrophically evil, and the other is worse. This is the World of Darkness, and there are no heroes. Except, possibly the PCs themselves. Only they can be the good the players want to see in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T03:58:01-08:00","id":1531458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1531216#post1531216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> But is it true? Mages have gained insight into the nature of reality. They haven't gained any special insight into morality or the nature of humanity. At best they have the ability to see additional ways the world could be, but they have no additional authority to determine what should be.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is entirely true. <br /> The morality of mages is the same as sleepers, but as they know far more, their position is akin to an adult about children. <br /> <br /> And I would disagree that awakened have no greater insight into the nature of humanity. <br /> <br /> Many have access to mind magic. While sleepers must rely on each other's claims and fragile psychological models, awakened can read someone's minds, knowing them for what they actually are. <br /> <br /> By doing so in repetition, a mind mage has an understanding of humans greater than any one of us could hope to achieve. <br /> <br /> Magic gives the answer to many fundamental. Questions of philosophy and morals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T03:58:44-08:00","id":1531459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1531262#post1531262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Maudaders are insane, the Fallen are evil, the Union is a fascist state, and the Traditions are ideological terrorists.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are the traditions &quot;ideological terrorists&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T04:32:42-08:00","id":1531461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1531459#post1531459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are the traditions &quot;ideological terrorists&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he's going along the line that since they &quot;know&quot; a possible future where everything went &quot;right&quot;, this supposedly gives them the right to do whatever is necessary to achieve that future, a dangerous thought that depending on the circumstances could be qualified as terrism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T04:48:04-08:00","id":1531464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1531459#post1531459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are the traditions &quot;ideological terrorists&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>They haven't bowed down to the greater good of the perfect Union!<br /> <br /> And insist on fighting back!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T10:10:07-08:00","id":1531477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1531458#post1531458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is entirely true.<br /> The morality of mages is the same as sleepers, but as they know far more, their position is akin to an adult about children.<br /> <br /> And I would disagree that awakened have no greater insight into the nature of humanity.<br /> <br /> Many have access to mind magic. While sleepers must rely on each other's claims and fragile psychological models, awakened can read someone's minds, knowing them for what they actually are.<br /> <br /> By doing so in repetition, a mind mage has an understanding of humans greater than any one of us could hope to achieve.<br /> <br /> Magic gives the answer to many fundamental. Questions of philosophy and morals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. So the NWO should be running everything, because they're masters of Mind. <br /> <br /> Oh, wait; are philosophy and morals <i>really</i> in the purview of <i>Mind</i>? Sure, it addresses the question of \u201cwhat are people thinking?\u201d But does that translate to questions of good and evil?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T08:42:21-08:00","id":1531519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1531477#post1531477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. So the NWO should be running everything, because they're masters of Mind.<br /> <br /> Oh, wait; are philosophy and morals <i>really</i> in the purview of <i>Mind</i>? Sure, it addresses the question of \u201cwhat are people thinking?\u201d But does that translate to questions of good and evil?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They indeed fall under mind. <br /> For philosophy and morals starts with axioms on the nature of existence and minds. <br /> Something mages can actually verify. <br /> <br /> Take Marx's axioms that man's nature is socialist (over simplification I know), rousseau's view that man is fundamentally good, and that it's society that corrupts him, or hobbies' opposed claims that man is evil. <br /> <br /> These can be verified by mind's mage, henceforth forcing axiomatic claims of philosophies under empirical verification. <br /> <br /> Same for many concepts, such as the notion of philosophical zombies. How can I know that I' m not the only conscious humans and all others are not just things lacking qualia, just mimicking consciousness Ness? Well, mind magic can check it out. <br /> <br /> It's chat GPT conscious? Let's check with mind magic. Are plants conscious? Mind magic. <br /> <br /> Add to that the ability of mages to go to the high umbra, offering them the ability to face the very incarnation of morals and philosophies rather than their vulgarised versions on earth, and you'll have a population far more able to understand them than even the most well versed sleeper philosopher. <br /> <br /> <br /> Following that, pages, at the opposite of sleepers, can actually anticipate the effectiveness of philosophies and policies. <br /> <br /> Can communism actually work or is it doomed to caused misery? Let's use time magic to scrupulously observe potential futures. <br /> <br /> Are criminals the product of their environment? Time +mind magic to see their mind across their lives. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Magic simply wipe out most philosophical and political questionment. <br /> <br /> To use again my previous metaphor, mages are to sleepers what adults are to children with the sheer breadth of their insight. <br /> <br /> As to your mention of the NWO, it's issue is that the NWO is in denial of it's own insight. As shown even in technocracy, reloaded, humanity don't behave as the union wished it would be. <br /> <br /> Something evident to every other faction that isn't under tech ocratic dogma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T15:30:05-08:00","id":1531552,"title":"","content":"You're assuming the conclusion in your premise: you're presuming that issues of morality are mental constructs, and jumping from that to the conclusion that they must therefore fall under the purview of Mind. But the idea that good and evil are mental constructs is <i>itself</i> a paradigmatic tenet, and <i>shouldn't </i>be assumed.<br /> <br /> I could see \u201cDetect Evil\u201d being a Telos rote, but not a Mind rote. Heck, I could even see something very much like it as a Prime rote, as part of \u201cidentify Resonance\u201d: one of the difficulties that the Nephandi have is that their corrupt natures tend to be given away by the Resonance that follows them around. Though that's not technically \u201cDetect Evil\u201d <i>either</i>, because there are Euthanatoi who tend to develop very similar Resonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T16:09:58-08:00","id":1531556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1531519#post1531519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They indeed fall under mind.<br /> For philosophy and morals starts with axioms on the nature of existence and minds.<br /> Something mages can actually verify.<br /> <br /> Take Marx's axioms that man's nature is socialist (over simplification I know), rousseau's view that man is fundamentally good, and that it's society that corrupts him, or hobbies' opposed claims that man is evil.<br /> <br /> These can be verified by mind's mage, henceforth forcing axiomatic claims of philosophies under empirical verification.<br /> <br /> Same for many concepts, such as the notion of philosophical zombies. How can I know that I' m not the only conscious humans and all others are not just things lacking qualia, just mimicking consciousness Ness? Well, mind magic can check it out.<br /> <br /> It's chat GPT conscious? Let's check with mind magic. Are plants conscious? Mind magic.<br /> <br /> Add to that the ability of mages to go to the high umbra, offering them the ability to face the very incarnation of morals and philosophies rather than their vulgarised versions on earth, and you'll have a population far more able to understand them than even the most well versed sleeper philosopher.<br /> <br /> <br /> Following that, pages, at the opposite of sleepers, can actually anticipate the effectiveness of philosophies and policies.<br /> <br /> Can communism actually work or is it doomed to caused misery? Let's use time magic to scrupulously observe potential futures.<br /> <br /> Are criminals the product of their environment? Time +mind magic to see their mind across their lives.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Magic simply wipe out most philosophical and political questionment.<br /> <br /> To use again my previous metaphor, mages are to sleepers what adults are to children with the sheer breadth of their insight.<br /> <br /> As to your mention of the NWO, it's issue is that the NWO is in denial of it's own insight. As shown even in technocracy, reloaded, humanity don't behave as the union wished it would be.<br /> <br /> Something evident to every other faction that isn't under tech ocratic dogma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that Time magic is meant to be an imperfect science. Especially when you try to apply it on a cosmic scale. You will get vague answers at best. <br /> <br /> Also, you can only use mind to verify if a man is good according to *your* standards. Even then, you'd have to target a lot of humans to see how well communism works on them.<br /> <br /> Remember, ideologie oftentimes fail to work due to practicalities rather than &quot;Evil&quot;. For instance, small communes have indeed lives in a communist lifestyle. Complexity is a factor that can not really be detected with mind. Let alone on a massive scale","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T08:18:14-08:00","id":1531623,"title":"","content":"As said, before trying to detect if something it's &quot;good&quot; or &quot;works&quot; one needs to set some basic premises that give meaning to those words. The devil it's in the details. And these precede any use of the Spheres<br /> <br /> For instance: We could say that &quot;goodness&quot; it's inherently part of the pattern of the human soul (Mind?, Spirit?,Prime?, 10th Sphere? a combination?), but if there's something mages know it's that reality can be changed (even on a basic level?): If someone has been &quot;corrupted by society&quot; it's reasonable to think you won't be able to &quot;detect good&quot;.<br /> <br /> Moreover, assuming &quot;reincarnation&quot; exists (does the soul reincarnate?, or it's an Avatar thing, and we deny the Avatar it's the soul or part of it?) even scanning a baby would be insufficient to determine if good it's inherent because this inheritance could be been tarnished by the karma of a previous life. Rather, you will have to find a &quot;blank slate soul&quot; to scan (do these exist?, how would you recognize one?)<br /> <br /> ... Wouldn't that be an interesting research? ...<br /> <br /> ... just for that Etherite over there to disagree with any of those questions, or maybe even just because they disagree on how some moral principles should work :P <hr /><br /> ...That being said, I do think that mages have more tools on their belts than Joe Average to make choices...<br /> <br /> If I can see your health with Life, and *know* how your choice of food affected it. Analize a building with Matter/Forces or Entropy, and *know* it's structurally unsafe. When I can throw a coin and predict if it's going to be &quot;face&quot; 10 times out of 10 (either by prediction, or by changing the results), and regularly do the same for a lot fo things that normal people see as &quot;random&quot; ... and also know how you *feel* about it...<br /> <br /> ... yeah, of course I'm going to believe &quot;I know better&quot;. Up to some extent, it's true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T09:03:44-08:00","id":1531625,"title":"","content":"Yep. \u201cUp to some extent.\u201d Which gives the mage <i>just enough </i>rope to hang himself. There's <i>enough</i> truth to the idea that mages are better equipped than Sleepers to make important decisions that it's understandable when they decide to tell you how to live your life. But unlike<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a>'s assertion earlier, mages aren't omniscient; and they frequently overreach. It's easy for them to think that their access to the Spheres means that they have all the answers; but they <i>don't</i>. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> just pointed out, there are answers that the Spheres can't easily provide, and that they may not be able to provide <i>at all</i>.<br /> <br /> And even when Spheres <i>can</i> provide answers, not every mage has access to every Sphere. Let's assume for the moment that one <i>can</i> use an appropriate combination of Spheres to, say, Detect Evil: not every mage is going to have that combination of Spheres; and the ones who don't are going to be no better off than the average Sleeper when it comes to judging whether something is evil. Should <i>they</i> bow down to the mages who <i>do</i> have the correct combination of Spheres? <br /> <br /> Or is turning your agency over to someone else <i>itself</i> a moral lapse? And if it is, isn't that just as true of Sleepers as it is of the Awakened? And conversely, wouldn't <i>taking someone's agency from them</i> be a moral lapse? <br /> <br /> It's a messy thing, all told; but the important point is that <i>even if the Awakened as a whole have better tools, </i>that doesn't inherently put them on the moral high ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T09:59:01-08:00","id":1531896,"title":"","content":"The moral of the story is, every faction and each subgroup of Mages thinks they are right, every group thinks they are the 'good guys', and every (sub)group, even if they cooperate, ultimately would love for their point of view to become the norm.<br /> <br /> They are very human like that. And all of them are flawed in human ways. This is nothing special at all. That's the point.<br /> <br /> *Any* kind of human can awaken. The most gentle soul and the most deranged bastard. And when humans organize large groups, shit goes wrong on *some* level or other.<br /> <br /> Nobody actually thinks they are a 'bad guy'. This applies to both Mages and RL folks that do abhorrent things. They might lack empathy and understanding, but they do not think they are 'the bad guy'.<br /> Even those Mages that push some actions and consequences to extremes consider it essentially to be 'the end justifies the means'.<br /> <br /> In the end, Mage asks the personal question <i>'If you were a powerful reality-bending being, how far would you go for what you think is right?'</i>, to every character, as well as the followup question <i>'And how would you treat normal, unaware people? What if they get in the way? What if you want them to see things your way? Just what would you do to win this war?'</i><br /> <br /> <br /> The only exception are the Nephandi. Which is what differentiates them from simple, sociopath murder Mages that naturally also exist out there. The Nephandi went through the Cauls, the Avatar got inverted, and they absolutely know they are pure Evil. They simply think they are either a necessary evil, or really don't care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-03-2024, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T14:55:23-08:00","id":1532198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1530601#post1530601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fantastic post.<br /> <br /> +1 smiley face.<br /> <br /> BUT I feel it could go too far.<br /> <br /> Because, really...it's WRONG to teach that fascists are morally equivalent to the people who oppose them. Not just wrong ethically but just dumb from a philosophical standpoint.<br /> <br /> And I feel like the Technocracy can't be divorced from the fact its ideology is what causes wealth inequality, global warming, and so much.<br /> <br /> Individuals may be good but I think it might be best to make it so the Technocracy....should go for the betterment of the world.<br /> <br /> The question then becomes whether the Traditions are worth keeping with this stance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fascists and Communists oppose each another, yet they are morally equivalently disgusting, deplorable and inhuman.<br /> <br /> So I think your point is a moot one.<br /> <br /> Also, no SERIOUS class of ethics in the world would ever teach you about &quot;how to be good&quot;. Anyone who isn't a psychopath or that don't follow those murderous ideologies already knows what is good and what is evil. The study of ethics is about how to make the best decisions given difficult situations upon which the best course of action is not clear. Mage therefore isn't a game about black and white morality of &quot;good vs evil&quot;. It is set in the freaking WORLD OF DARKNESS, not in &quot;my favorite unicorn utopia&quot;. One of the great questions it asks is one that all societies implicitly (and non verbally) make: what is best, safety or freedom? Would you be willing to give up some freedom for safety?<br /> <br /> I hear your buzz words about &quot;capitalism&quot; while talking about the Technocracy, cute, but let me ask you: would you rather starve to death, but be free, or having food as a slave?<br /> <br /> And before you thrown tamper tantrums at my question, I would like you to look at China, and realize that the population there has clearly chosen tyranny over freedom, as long as that gives them some food on their bellies. Oh, and they aren't a &quot;capitalist&quot; nation by the way.<br /> <br /> Can I blame the Chinese people for that choice? Well, I guess it is very easy for me who have always had at least 3 meals a day from birth to preach about how much I value my freedom, but let's be honest here, I never lived in a reality where I had to eat grass and rodents to survive while watching my parents and siblings and children starving to death, so we can see that morality has its breaking points under extreme conditions.<br /> <br /> And that's how I like to see my games of Magic. Not from the viewpoint of a spoiled western snowflake worried about not triggering other people, but as an in-depth look at morality from many hard perspectives.<br /> <br /> Imagine a Technocrat that fought off against Things-Man-Was-Not-Meant-To-Know. Imagine knowing that your worst existential dread is real - a mix of boogiemen with Nazis and demons, and that they are such an existential threat that there's nothing this guy wouldn't do to keep those things at bay.<br /> <br /> Is such an individual justified in his actions?<br /> <br /> Let's put in a more grounded example: imagine you captured a terrorist that placed a nuclear bomb somewhere in our fictional country of Perfectland, and that bomb is powerful enough the blow up the entire country, killing millions.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm against torture, and I'm sure you are too. But... And now comes the harsh choices... Would you torture that guy in order to get the information that can save millions? And if even under torture he doesn't break, would you torture his children? Remember, MILLIONS will die if you do nothing.<br /> <br /> Now, THAT'S a real question about morality. <br /> <br /> Would you sacrifice one life to save millions? If yes, then let's imagine another scenario: we have 5 people in a hospital needing organs. If you do nothing, they all die. Would you kill a healthy person to save 5? If not, what's the difference between saving millions or saving 5 at the cost of only 1? It's just a matter of numbers?<br /> <br /> You see, the world is much more nuanced than your simplistic and honestly, intellectually poor view of &quot;oppressors vs oppressed&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T15:44:42-08:00","id":1532199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532198#post1532198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You see, the world is much more nuanced than your simplistic and honestly, intellectually poor view of &quot;oppressors vs oppressed&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really no.<br /> <br /> Because the only person who wins when you don't stand up to oppression is the oppressor and the person who says otherwise is usually selling something.<br /> <br /> Plus, Stalin may be as bad as Hitler but the Nazis were infinitely worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T16:05:21-08:00","id":1532202,"title":"","content":"This has the potential to veer off into real world belief systems, which I'm leery of: it has the potential to get rather heated and to ruin my enjoyment of the thread. So I'm going to tread lightly here. With that in mind, \u201coppressor vs. oppressed\u201d is all well and good once you've properly identified the oppressor and the oppressed; that's why punching Nazis is such a popular choice in recent RPGs. You get into nuance when you try to make the determination of who is oppressing whom, or even if any oppression is happening. You cannot, for instance, assume that whoever has power is an oppressor and whoever the powerful is going after is oppressed. If a poor man brutalizes a rich man's daughter, and the rich man uses his wealth to track down and punish the poor man, it's not \u201cthe rich man is oppressing the poor man\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T16:06:13-08:00","id":1532203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532199#post1532199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really no.<br /> <br /> Because the only person who wins when you don't stand up to oppression is the oppressor and the person who says otherwise is usually selling something.<br /> <br /> Plus, Stalin may be as bad as Hitler but the Nazis were infinitely worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you're going towards a rather childish simplistic world. &quot;The Romans were oppressors&quot;. Yes sure, I have no doubt about it. They enslaved and slaughtered millions throughout their &quot;path to greatness&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's a shallow view of the world however. Were the &quot;barbarians&quot; any better than the Romans? Barbarians - Aka Gauls, Germanics, Iberians, Slavs and many others.<br /> <br /> Were they thou? Well, those people also practiced slavery, also slaughtered their enemies, and if they could, they would obliterate the Romans just like the Romans did to them.<br /> <br /> None of that is justifiable, despite you implicitly trying to say that I am &quot;trying to sell something&quot;, which is a very intellectual dishonest way of calling me a &quot;Nazi&quot;. * If you don't agree with me, you are 'trying to sell something' - aka you're trying to apologize for all of those evil things, aka you're a Nazi.<br /> <br /> In short, let's resume your argument as: if you don't agree with me, you're a Nazi.<br /> <br /> Which is a very childish way of looking at the world. As is childish to think that things either are done by the enlightened anti capitalistic angels of purity, or by evil fascists.<br /> <br /> Looking at history by such lenses is childish. The Romans were as barbaric and violent an abhorrent as the Zulus or as the Chinese or the Arabs or any others.<br /> <br /> We like to think that nowadays we are different, and this is good; I would NOT want to live in a world such as ancient Rome or ancient China or ancient anything.<br /> <br /> But moral judgements of our ancestors is just silly. Our ancestors were little more than beasts, and it would be silly to judge a lions morality for eating the gazelle.<br /> <br /> Also, like I said, it's easy to have a &quot;white men's burden&quot; towards the &quot;minorities&quot; when we have garanteed 3 meals per day throughout our entire lives. If you were living in a tribe starving to death in the savannas and crossed a tribe filled with food, I would really like to know if you would stick to your high western morals (that you despise by the way) or if you would slaughter them all and take the food you need to survive.<br /> <br /> About the Nazis being &quot;infinitely worse&quot; than the communists, there were 100 million people that would disagree with you - if they were alive today.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T16:16:21-08:00","id":1532205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532202#post1532202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has the potential to veer off into real world belief systems, which I'm leery of: it has the potential to get rather heated and to ruin my enjoyment of the thread. So I'm going to tread lightly here. With that in mind, \u201coppressor vs. oppressed\u201d is all well and good once you've properly identified the oppressor and the oppressed; that's why punching Nazis is such a popular choice in recent RPGs. You get into nuance when you try to make the determination of who is oppressing whom, or even if any oppression is happening. You cannot, for instance, assume that whoever has power is an oppressor and whoever the powerful is going after is oppressed. If a poor man brutalizes a rich man's daughter, and the rich man uses his wealth to track down and punish the poor man, it's not \u201cthe rich man is oppressing the poor man\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong but a larger matter that often gets ignored is that canon is flexible enough that a lot of it is up to the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T16:41:06-08:00","id":1532208,"title":"","content":"Going back to the topic, a game about &quot;Ze evil Technocrats&quot; vs &quot;the angelic oppressed Traditions&quot; would not be a game I would like to play. And it's not because some &quot;good vs evil&quot; very black and white game wouldn't be fun - when I play D&amp;D, it is strictly &quot;boy scouts&quot; heroic deeds (I absolutely dislike all of the disfunctional tables with &quot;Chaotic Evil&quot; Clerics shoehorned into it). But I think that Mage the Ascension can explore things with so much more depth to it than just that. And even if I want to make some non Nephandi as a clear cut and outright villain, that can be done with so much more depth than just &quot;evil for evil's sake&quot;. My example of the Technocrat that &quot;fights Things-men-were-not-meant-to-know&quot; is because I once used such a villain at my tables. He was a war veteran from deep space, and there was no atrocities that he would not commit for the sake of the Union - but there was a purpose to it, a motif. And his reason was that, in face of what awaited on the other side should the Union fail, ANYTHING else was secondary. This was an extreme view of &quot;trading safety for freedom&quot;. And that's the sort of moral analysis that I like my players to indulge into. It's not unlike primitive tribes of the Paleolithic exterminating one another over food. When pushed to the extremes for survival, moral considerations are thrown out the window. And that was the worldview of this villain, a &quot;barbarians at the gate&quot; mindset that is able to justify anything.<br /> <br /> That's also the dangers of ideology. When you are certain that you are on &quot;the right side of history&quot;, you can justify ANYTHING. Do you think that the Nazis though of themselves as villains? Of course not, in their lunatic worldview they were waging a spiritual war to save the world. The Chinese youth under Mao also thought that were on the &quot;right side of history&quot; when they were denouncing millions to die under the Cultural Revolution. But they were the &quot;righteous ones&quot;. And when you believe yourself to be &quot;righteous&quot;, it's very easy to become a tyrant and commit unspeakable atrocities.<br /> <br /> Even when you believe to be standing against the &quot;oppressors&quot; on behalf of &quot;the oppressed&quot; (which by the way, both the Nazis and the Communists also firmly believed to be doing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T16:48:17-08:00","id":1532210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532208#post1532208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going back to the topic, a game about &quot;Ze evil Technocrats&quot; vs &quot;the angelic oppressed Traditions&quot; would not be a game...</div> </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned, the one thing I disagreed with Onyx Path Publishing's writers on was the constant attempts at Technocracy rewriting. They tried to justify it in-universe and it was very well-written but I just think it was a bad idea all round. Basically, the Technocracy as depicted in first and second edition with its brainwashing, genocide, colonialism, forced labor, and propaganda is nothing remotely ridiculous. They are exactly like a lot of authoritarian governments in the real world and none of these groups require a &quot;misunderstood idealistic motivation.&quot; I could name five or six dictators who just care about power and think that people who are for the people are either lying or stupid.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy Reloaded suddenly acts like the kind of people who murder Traditionalists for the crime of using magic to heal sick patients are the kind of people who will suddenly care about the rain forest.<br /> <br /> And I feel that's actually the less realistic take. Graying up reality is actually the more unrealistic and naive take. In any punk game, a bunch of people are just greedy evil assholes and that's the kind of people who would be ruling the world behind the scenes in the WoD.<br /> <br /> Seers of Thrones is just more believable and grounded than the Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T17:02:46-08:00","id":1532212,"title":"","content":"This is going to be very out of place, but I had a similar internal dilemma while reading MTC, just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T17:20:34-08:00","id":1532214,"title":"","content":"The main drive, as I see it, for adding gray to the Technocracy is that they have a near-monopoly on Enlightened Science; and a lot of people love the idea of playing Enlightened Scientists. There are basically two possible solutions to this: make the Technocracy something that people can stomach playing when they don't want to play evil characters, or break the monopoly. <br /> <br /> Both have been tried. Guide to the Technocracy and the Revised Convention Books try for a \u201ckinder, gentler Union\u201d, and M20 introduces the possibility of groups like Navalon, which practice Enlightened Science but loathe technocracy (lower-case \u201ct\u201d). The former approach operates on the premise that the Dimensional Singularity and the subsequent loss of Control was a shock to the system for the Technocracy and made them take stock and get introspective, cleaning up their act to an extent. The latter approach takes a faction that was inside the Union but was always uneasy about what the Union was doing, and recently decided to jump ship. <br /> <br /> But this thread isn't really about the Technocracy; it's about the Traditions. And even if the Technocracy was as bad as the Nephandi, it doesn't mean that the Traditions are good guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T18:58:03-08:00","id":1532220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532212#post1532212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is going to be very out of place, but I had a similar internal dilemma while reading MTC, just saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>MTC?<br /> <br /> Sorry, I'm terrible with lingo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T19:00:42-08:00","id":1532221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532220#post1532220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> MTC?<br /> <br /> Sorry, I'm terrible with lingo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am too, Mummy the Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T20:52:36-08:00","id":1532228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532221#post1532221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am too, Mummy the Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to know a bit more about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T08:49:20-08:00","id":1532242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532228#post1532228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd love to know a bit more about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, before reading I had an overview of what the game was about, but I didn't know that much about the backstory and giving a summary of my impression vs. reality. I thought it would be similar to &quot;Resurrection&quot; and it is in a way, but the origin is very different, &quot;Resurrection&quot; is more about redemption or second chances if you stop to think about it, while &quot;The Curse&quot; are about people who did part of Irem's kingdom that would be almost like a Rome in Egypt and received the blessing/curse of the deathless to better serve their masters and their kingdom, may seem commendable act, but not as much as you think Irem's well-being was made through of the conquest and slavery of other kingdons, and things get worse when you know that they only perfected the deathless ritual after several experiments with slaves, in fact they became antagonists. Not that this made me dislike the game or anything like that, but it is something to relate to MTA where each tradition tries to reach its definition of what the ideal kingdom/world would be, as far as I know none enslave others, but the question remains, How far are you willing to go for what you believe in? Pretty uncomfortable to think about, right? But we tolerate it because it's a game. I also take myself thinking about similar things with Werewolf and the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T15:37:41-08:00","id":1532300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532198#post1532198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fascists and Communists oppose each another, yet they are morally equivalently disgusting, deplorable and inhuman.<br /> <br /> So I think your point is a moot one.<br /> <br /> Also, no SERIOUS class of ethics in the world would ever teach you about &quot;how to be good&quot;. Anyone who isn't a psychopath or that don't follow those murderous ideologies already knows what is good and what is evil. The study of ethics is about how to make the best decisions given difficult situations upon which the best course of action is not clear. Mage therefore isn't a game about black and white morality of &quot;good vs evil&quot;. It is set in the freaking WORLD OF DARKNESS, not in &quot;my favorite unicorn utopia&quot;. One of the great questions it asks is one that all societies implicitly (and non verbally) make: what is best, safety or freedom? Would you be willing to give up some freedom for safety?<br /> <br /> I hear your buzz words about &quot;capitalism&quot; while talking about the Technocracy, cute, but let me ask you: would you rather starve to death, but be free, or having food as a slave?<br /> <br /> And before you thrown tamper tantrums at my question, I would like you to look at China, and realize that the population there has clearly chosen tyranny over freedom, as long as that gives them some food on their bellies. Oh, and they aren't a &quot;capitalist&quot; nation by the way.<br /> <br /> Can I blame the Chinese people for that choice? Well, I guess it is very easy for me who have always had at least 3 meals a day from birth to preach about how much I value my freedom, but let's be honest here, I never lived in a reality where I had to eat grass and rodents to survive while watching my parents and siblings and children starving to death, so we can see that morality has its breaking points under extreme conditions.<br /> <br /> And that's how I like to see my games of Magic. Not from the viewpoint of a spoiled western snowflake worried about not triggering other people, but as an in-depth look at morality from many hard perspectives.<br /> <br /> Imagine a Technocrat that fought off against Things-Man-Was-Not-Meant-To-Know. Imagine knowing that your worst existential dread is real - a mix of boogiemen with Nazis and demons, and that they are such an existential threat that there's nothing this guy wouldn't do to keep those things at bay.<br /> <br /> Is such an individual justified in his actions?<br /> <br /> Let's put in a more grounded example: imagine you captured a terrorist that placed a nuclear bomb somewhere in our fictional country of Perfectland, and that bomb is powerful enough the blow up the entire country, killing millions.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm against torture, and I'm sure you are too. But... And now comes the harsh choices... Would you torture that guy in order to get the information that can save millions? And if even under torture he doesn't break, would you torture his children? Remember, MILLIONS will die if you do nothing.<br /> <br /> Now, THAT'S a real question about morality.<br /> <br /> Would you sacrifice one life to save millions? If yes, then let's imagine another scenario: we have 5 people in a hospital needing organs. If you do nothing, they all die. Would you kill a healthy person to save 5? If not, what's the difference between saving millions or saving 5 at the cost of only 1? It's just a matter of numbers?<br /> <br /> You see, the world is much more nuanced than your simplistic and honestly, intellectually poor view of &quot;oppressors vs oppressed&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#8B0000\"><b>Please tone it down a little. We can have a spirited debate without dipping into examples of torture, child harm, or putting words into one another's mouths. </b></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T21:00:33-08:00","id":1532313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532210#post1532210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I mentioned, the one thing I disagreed with Onyx Path Publishing's writers on was the constant attempts at Technocracy rewriting. They tried to justify it in-universe and it was very well-written but I just think it was a bad idea all round. Basically, the Technocracy as depicted in first and second edition with its brainwashing, genocide, colonialism, forced labor, and propaganda is nothing remotely ridiculous. They are exactly like a lot of authoritarian governments in the real world and none of these groups require a &quot;misunderstood idealistic motivation.&quot; I could name five or six dictators who just care about power and think that people who are for the people are either lying or stupid.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy Reloaded suddenly acts like the kind of people who murder Traditionalists for the crime of using magic to heal sick patients are the kind of people who will suddenly care about the rain forest.<br /> <br /> And I feel that's actually the less realistic take. Graying up reality is actually the more unrealistic and naive take. In any punk game, a bunch of people are just greedy evil assholes and that's the kind of people who would be ruling the world behind the scenes in the WoD.<br /> <br /> Seers of Thrones is just more believable and grounded than the Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... For that, the Technocracy would have to be a lot more like the Illuminati. In that case, why even having the Nephandi if all they care about is power. <br /> <br /> In First Edition yes, that's what the techies were, but first edition is like an introduction, it was the same for VtM where you had the Camarilla as the &quot;playable characters&quot; and the Sabbath was like the &quot;Book of Monsters&quot; for D&amp;D - aka the NPCs that the &quot;Dungeon Master&quot; throws at you.<br /> <br /> But again, if they're just as evil as Nephandi, why not having them being Nephandi all the way...<br /> <br /> I rather have it as any other human institution: something good at first, that gets corrupted over time. A good example would be the Catholic Church for instance. Christianism was a HUGE moral improvement over the debauchery that was the Roman culture, but power corrupts. So, over time, they had people like the Borgias and many petty squabbles over power, but you still had highly moral men amongst it. We can't judge an institution such as the Catholic Church as &quot;good&quot; or &quot;evil&quot;, but rather as something flawed and with mixed achievements. Just the same holds true for a realistic approach of the Union.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-09T21:57:26-08:00","id":1532315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532313#post1532313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm... For that, the Technocracy would have to be a lot more like the Illuminati. In that case, why even having the Nephandi if all they care about is power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh, the Nephandi aren't &quot;generically evil.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Nephandi don't care about power. They don't care about wealth. They don't care about nation states or even religion. They want to unmake existence. They've looked into the darkest heart of the universe and discovered that there is nothing good in it and only destroying everything will make it right, living and dead. There's a lot you can do with that kind of ideology in a game like Mage. People who argue that this world is an awful sick joke and we should just end it.<br /> <br /> The Seers, by contrast, just are people who don't give a shit how many children die if it gets them another mansion. The Union zig-zags between those guys and guys who keep arguing that all their actions are for the greater goodTM.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"800\" height=\"600\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://rhianhousingjourney.files.wordpress.com/2020/01/hotfuzzgreatergood.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://rhianhousingjourney.files.wordpress.com/2020/01/hotfuzzgreatergood.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://rhianhousingjourney.files.wordpress.com/2020/01/hotfuzzgreatergood.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> My point is that maybe we need to remember those mansion guys are way more common than someone stating that X number of children dying in the sweatshops we saw in Blade Runner 2049 is somehow necessary to save humanity.<br /> <br /> Mage kind of lacks a faction for people who are given godlike power and decide...you know, fuck everyone else. I've got mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-10-2024, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T06:23:23-07:00","id":1532323,"title":"","content":"Well then, in that case, go for it. It is essentially a different Technocracy from what is portrait in the game, but it is your game.<br /> <br /> I would still go for a vision of it being more or less like the Catholic Church. You DO have the &quot;sacrifice little children to get a new mansion&quot; type of people inside of the CC - heck, the church has countless cases of scandals about priests who molested children. I mean, it really is staggering how many of those have occured.<br /> <br /> It's a matter of power attracting psychopaths. &quot;Power is dangerous. It attracts the worse and corrupts the best&quot;.<br /> <br /> But the Catholic Church ain't just simply a club of pedophiles, and the majority of their priests are highly devotional and empathetic humans who dedicate their lives towards taking care of others.<br /> <br /> And yes, for &quot;The Greater Good&quot; usually leads on to tyranny and atrocities. Nazi/fascism and communism, all of those were done for the sake of &quot;The Greater Good&quot;, and millions paid the price of it. So yes, I absolutely agree that the Union is tyrannical and atrocious, but I disagree with this view that they are just psychopaths that are only interested in getting a new villa no matter how many little children they have to throw at the meat grinder for that. Sure, many MAY be like that, specially at the top, but I wouldn't think that ALL of them would be like this, and even those who are, still have &quot;some&quot; regards about humanity.<br /> <br /> I mean, think about such nice fellows such as Putin or Xi Jinping... Maybe those are the models to follow. Sure, they want their winter palaces stuffed with the best food and the best prostitutes that only true power can buy, and they want to keep their power above all else, but they still want their nations to thrive. It's only that they don't see their &quot;subjects&quot; as &quot;citizens&quot; with individual rights, but rather as eggs to be broken according to the needs of the nation.<br /> <br /> Are they evil? Oh yes, absolutely. But it's still not the same type of evil as North Korea for instance, upon which the subjects of Kim Jong Un are just his personal slaves and nothing more; that would be more likely to what you're proposing the Union to be, which I think is an exaggeration","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T11:32:10-07:00","id":1532342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532323#post1532323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well then, in that case, go for it. It is essentially a different Technocracy from what is portrait in the game, but it is your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it's a different portrayal from some editions but absolutely the portrayal in a lot of versions.<br /> <br /> It's like asking whether the Decepticons are well-intentioned extremists or Space Nazis.<br /> <br /> That depends on if you're an IDW comic reader or cartoon fans.<br /> <br /> We're discussing OOC after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T05:33:35-07:00","id":1532368,"title":"","content":"The Decepticons are heroes who hide as toys and defend children from evil aliens. Everything since then is alien propaganda. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T05:51:49-07:00","id":1532369,"title":"","content":"Odd how these threads always end up being about the Technocracy, even when they start out being about the Traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T09:25:42-07:00","id":1532379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532369#post1532369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odd how these threads always end up being about the Technocracy, even when they start out being about the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a theory - Giles voice<br /> <br /> Essentially, it's impossible to discuss the nature of the Traditions in these sort of things because so much of what they're justified in doing and what they're up to is in response to the situation. You need to define what exactly they're the RebellionTM against in order to talk about any sort of moral ambiguity or evil they may be. The Traditions also have a weird sense of where the fans can't agree on fundamental facts about what the Traditions goals, methods, and ideology is other than &quot;Techno-Illuminati bad.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which leads me to four separate Tradition views:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>High Contrast</b>: The Traditions are in a state similar to the Matrix. Once you are awakened, the Technocracy will track you down and proceed to force you to join them. They will black bag you over the head, kill and replace your family with clones, and torture you into compliance. Maybe you'll get the stock options and cloned sex slave/trophy spouse offer first. However, you must prove your loyalty first and repudiate anything other than total belief in the Union. Players are always on the run and the Union will frame them for being pedophiles, serial killers, terrorists, and otherwise turn everything as well as everyone against them. You're the Incredible Hulk and must constantly be on the move unless you're part of a chantry and even then, the Union will hunt that down to sanitize.<br /> <br /> <b>Clash of Ideologies</b>: The Union's ideology doesn't actually matter weirdly, nor does the Traditions. It's really too much of a fight for survival to get into the subject of naval gazing over God or communism. There's your side and their side and never the twain shall meet.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Low Contrast</b>: The Technocracy and Traditions are in a state of Cold War. The Traditions have huge chantries and other dimensional palaces while the Technocracy have their Death Stars and Enterprises. Big moves are fairly rare but do happen on occassion. Instead, this is all about the two elites fighting for rulership of humanity. Outcasts like the Hollow Ones may be in a fight for survival but your Tradition determines who you're supporting for when you rule the world. Foci are probably best thought of as tools rather than paradihm as the difference between both sides is just who signs your pay checks.<br /> <br /> <b>Clash of Ideologies</b>: A lot of naval gazing and debate but at the end of the day, it's about who rules what. The Order of Hermes will eventually turn against everyone else or the Celestial Choir but we're allies today. A lot of questioning of whether any of this is helping anyone as you ALL live in Ivory Towers.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Evil vs. Evil</b>: The Technocracy are fascists and the Traditions are fundamentalist terrorists. The Traditions blow up buildings full of cancer cures and the Technocracy gases minority churches. Both sides are complete scum and there's absolutely no value to siding with either of them save as a matter of survival. The Nephandi may have an appeal because it seems Awakening just makes you a fanatic who thinks that GOD is behind your magic and SATAN behind everyone else's or some variation thereof.<br /> <br /> <b>Clash of Ideologies</b>: Everyone you're allied with today is an enemy tomorrow because there's only one true way of magic.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Good vs. Good</b>: This is the one I hate the most and weirdly what I think Revised wanted to do. Basically, the Technocracy and Traditions both want to make the world a better place for Sleepers and their continued fight against one another is a waste of resources. The Technocrats want to cure all disease and make a utopian future where the environment is pristine and everyone eats while the Traditions want to make a similar magitech Utopian future where prayer does cure cancer and you can visit the stars with astral projection. There's no Enrons or vaccine deniers and it's only really belief the other side is a bunch of evil psychopaths that keep peace from happening.<br /> <br /> <b>Clash of Ideologies</b>: Both sides see the other as way more extreme than they actually are and frequently throw out accusations like, &quot;The Traditions want to throw us back to the Dark Ages&quot; and &quot;The Technocracy wants to eliminate human free will&quot; which is about as accurate as saying Hollywood vampire pedophile rings for both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T14:10:48-07:00","id":1532392,"title":"","content":"I can say that in Technocracy Reloaded and Lore of the Traditions we tried to pose an &quot;Ascension Truce&quot; option in which the Traditions and the Technocracy tentatively try working together to curtail the damage Sleepers have inflicted on the planet. (Both sides realize no one wants to control consensus on a lifeless cinder) I thought it was an interesting alternative to the normal interactions between those groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T06:59:20-07:00","id":1532435,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=CTPhipps;n1532379]<br /> 2. <b>Low Contrast</b>: The Technocracy and Traditions are in a state of Cold War. The Traditions have huge chantries and other dimensional palaces while the Technocracy have their Death Stars and Enterprises. Big moves are fairly rare but do happen on occassion. Instead, this is all about the two elites fighting for rulership of humanity. Outcasts like the Hollow Ones may be in a fight for survival but your Tradition determines who you're supporting for when you rule the world. Foci are probably best thought of as tools rather than paradihm as the difference between both sides is just who signs your pay checks.[quote]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TravisLegge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532392#post1532392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can say that in Technocracy Reloaded and Lore of the Traditions we tried to pose an &quot;Ascension Truce&quot; option in which the Traditions and the Technocracy tentatively try working together to curtail the damage Sleepers have inflicted on the planet. (Both sides realize no one wants to control consensus on a lifeless cinder) I thought it was an interesting alternative to the normal interactions between those groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a variant of these ideas I came up with a while back. The Pax Coincidentia. It's a combination truce and Cold War. The Traditions and Technocracy still struggle, but they deliberately keep their moves low key and coincidental. Vulgar magic and open hostilities are avoided at all costs and both sides will join in on the damage control if that happens. So the fight is more a battle of influence and proxies and red tape.<br /> <br /> There's no pretense that they like each other. They're not trying to hide the struggle from themselves, but minimize its unintended side effects. They've been burned too many times by open conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532379#post1532379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. <b>Good vs. Good</b>: This is the one I hate the most and weirdly what I think Revised wanted to do. Basically, the Technocracy and Traditions both want to make the world a better place for Sleepers and their continued fight against one another is a waste of resources. The Technocrats want to cure all disease and make a utopian future where the environment is pristine and everyone eats while the Traditions want to make a similar magitech Utopian future where prayer does cure cancer and you can visit the stars with astral projection. There's no Enrons or vaccine deniers and it's only really belief the other side is a bunch of evil psychopaths that keep peace from happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also 5:<br /> <br /> <b>Flawed vs Flawed</b>: It's much the same motivations as Good vs Good, but with imperfect actors and the constant temptation to sacrifice ideals in the name of those same ideals. Mages are quick to see the flaws in the other side (real and perceived) and slow to see the same in their own. The Technocracy has legitimate and fatal criticisms of the Traditions (&quot;If we let you have your way, you are going to unleash chaos on the world.&quot;), but they aren't heard. The fact that they are overstating them (&quot;You are deliberately trying to unleash chaos on the world and get people killed&quot;) isn't helping. It's the same in the other direction. The Traditions' valid complaints (&quot;In the name of protecting the people you are ignoring their free will and their dignity&quot;) are harder to hear when they also say (&quot;You are a bunch of tyrants, who want to enslave humanity&quot;). Worst of all, there are Tyrants among the Technocracy and Terrorists among the Traditions and the factions are slow to purge them because they don't want to legitimize the accusations and they don't want to weaken themselves.<br /> <br /> They need reform, they don't have the luxury of reform.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T16:39:41-07:00","id":1532461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532369#post1532369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odd how these threads always end up being about the Technocracy, even when they start out being about the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly what CTP said. The Traditions are only a thing because of the Techies. There is no Trads without the need to oppose the Techies.<br /> <br /> Which is why I think they are doomed. The Techies, for all of its flaws and evil, exist for SOMETHING. The Trads however, exist only for the purpose of DENYING that something. Do the Trads have some greater plan for the masses? No, they can't form a coherent idea about &quot;mass Ascension&quot; that they can all agree with, their only idea is some vague notion of &quot;let them be free to walk their path&quot;, but they can't even agree on a path to be walked by.<br /> <br /> And thus, that's why it is impossible to talk about the Trads without talking about the Techies, because the Trads only exist as a &quot;not-the-techies&quot; faction.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T17:44:01-07:00","id":1532462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532461#post1532461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly what CTP said. The Traditions are only a thing because of the Techies. There is no Trads without the need to oppose the Techies.<br /> <br /> Which is why I think they are doomed. The Techies, for all of its flaws and evil, exist for SOMETHING. The Trads however, exist only for the purpose of DENYING that something. Do the Trads have some greater plan for the masses? No, they can't form a coherent idea about &quot;mass Ascension&quot; that they can all agree with, their only idea is some vague notion of &quot;let them be free to walk their path&quot;, but they can't even agree on a path to be walked by.<br /> <br /> And thus, that's why it is impossible to talk about the Trads without talking about the Techies, because the Trads only exist as a &quot;not-the-techies&quot; faction.<br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something I disagree with. I believe fully the Traditions teach their students that Mass Ascension is possible and there's no need to have &quot;One True Paradigm&quot; where only one kind of magic has to be accepted.<br /> <br /> Everyone can reach Rome their own way.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, is that INTERESTING? Because a substantial number of fans and implied by the &quot;Traditions don't know their foci don't do anything&quot; attitude of Revised, seem to prefer the idea that the Traditions are in an alliance of convenience even decades later.<br /> <br /> Basically, the game refuses to engage with a major source of conflict that would make the Traditions more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T18:19:36-07:00","id":1532465,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Ramnesis;n1532435][QUOTE=CTPhipps;n1532379] 2. <b>Low Contrast</b>: The Technocracy and Traditions are in a state of Cold War. The Traditions have huge chantries and other dimensional palaces while the Technocracy have their Death Stars and Enterprises. Big moves are fairly rare but do happen on occassion. Instead, this is all about the two elites fighting for rulership of humanity. Outcasts like the Hollow Ones may be in a fight for survival but your Tradition determines who you're supporting for when you rule the world. Foci are probably best thought of as tools rather than paradihm as the difference between both sides is just who signs your pay checks.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> There was a variant of these ideas I came up with a while back. The Pax Coincidentia. It's a combination truce and Cold War. The Traditions and Technocracy still struggle, but they deliberately keep their moves low key and coincidental. Vulgar magic and open hostilities are avoided at all costs and both sides will join in on the damage control if that happens. So the fight is more a battle of influence and proxies and red tape.<br /> <br /> There's no pretense that they like each other. They're not trying to hide the struggle from themselves, but minimize its unintended side effects. They've been burned too many times by open conflict.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's also 5:<br /> <br /> <b>Flawed vs Flawed</b>: It's much the same motivations as Good vs Good, but with imperfect actors and the constant temptation to sacrifice ideals in the name of those same ideals. Mages are quick to see the flaws in the other side (real and perceived) and slow to see the same in their own. The Technocracy has legitimate and fatal criticisms of the Traditions (&quot;If we let you have your way, you are going to unleash chaos on the world.&quot;), but they aren't heard. The fact that they are overstating them (&quot;You are deliberately trying to unleash chaos on the world and get people killed&quot;) isn't helping. It's the same in the other direction. The Traditions' valid complaints (&quot;In the name of protecting the people you are ignoring their free will and their dignity&quot;) are harder to hear when they also say (&quot;You are a bunch of tyrants, who want to enslave humanity&quot;). Worst of all, there are Tyrants among the Technocracy and Terrorists among the Traditions and the factions are slow to purge them because they don't want to legitimize the accusations and they don't want to weaken themselves.<br /> <br /> They need reform, they don't have the luxury of reform. </div> </div> </div> This. So much of this. That's it. The &quot;Ascension War&quot; could as well be called &quot;The War of Hubris&quot;.<br /> <br /> I realized that Mages (or &quot;Enlightened Scientist&quot;) are major A-holes just a few years back, in a conversation in this very forum. And I was on the Vampire Masquerade section, not in the MtA. Because sure, we all know that vampires SUCK (ok, that was a low hanging fruit joke, but I just couldn't resist). But there's a reason why they are monsters, and they can't help but to be monsters. They are inhuman beasts after all, that pretend to be human, and tragically some of them even believe in that lie, that they still have some humanity left, but it is just a sick joke. But that's a fate that is imposed upon them, a &quot;curse&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mages however, are fully human... Or are they?<br /> <br /> What's more, the &quot;Awakening&quot; is treated as a major blessing, something to aspire for everybody to go through. Something... Special.<br /> <br /> That's the first problem right over there. Mages are special.<br /> <br /> So, a Mage is not like you and me; we are just peasants, we are just &quot;Sleepers&quot;, we are just part of the ignorant masses living life as sleep-walking zombies, worried about the inflation of potatoes and who our least favorite guy will become the next president or not.<br /> <br /> Mages are a special breed of &quot;elites&quot;. Not necessarily economic or political elites, like the bourgeoisie or the aristocracy, nor even an &quot;informational elite&quot; like I call them, like the priests of old or the media of today. Nor the Warriors that compose the martial elites; those 4 groups are typically the ones that control any given society - merchants of old or &quot;entrepreneurs&quot; of total - economic power, the aristocrats of old or bureocrats of today - political power, the generals and warriors - military power and the priests of old or media today -&quot;cultural&quot; power.<br /> <br /> Mages are more or less, roughly speaking, a representation of intellectuals or the &quot;intelligentsia&quot;. And I have to say that I, personally, begun to loath these &quot;intellectuals&quot;, much like guys like Nietzsche or Socrates did.<br /> <br /> My first realization of the pettiness of the so called &quot;intellectuals&quot; came when I read &quot;The Little Prince&quot; as an adult. I had read it before as a child and as a teen, but as an adult I had a completely different view.<br /> <br /> I love the book ever since I was a child, but one of the passages changed a lot of my perceptions.<br /> <br /> It's when the Little Prince met the &quot;Business Man&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, the Business Man counted stars, because for each one that he counted, since they were all unclaimed, he could be the very first person to claim them, thus that made them his.<br /> <br /> This was a very UNFAIR critique. Look, here we have it, the author of the Little Prince - an artist, therefore a part of the &quot;intellectual community&quot;.<br /> <br /> And his critique is that, the &quot;business man&quot; - aka the entrepreneurs, the pragmatic people that aren't worried about how many angels fit in the head of a pin but that, rather, are worried about &quot;inflation and the next president&quot; and on how to prosper, the critique from an intellectual towards such people is that they are basically &quot;bean counters&quot; - meaning, petty people worried about petty issues, like &quot;counting beans&quot;.<br /> <br /> And this is the CORE VIEW THAT INTELLECTUALS HAVE TOWARDS BUSINESSES. That was the moment that I realized how much jealousy and how much hate the so called &quot;intellectuals&quot; have towards people who are economically successful.<br /> <br /> Because, you see, you have billionaires who don't have a slight clue about Plato or Socrates or Nietzsche or about any of the &quot;deeper&quot; things in life, and who are only worried about money...<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>And that's not fair!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> And Mages are THOSE types of assholes. They are the smart ones, Mages are the wise sages on the top of the mountains, looking at everybody else's stupidity from high above.<br /> <br /> When I first got my hands on a book of MtA, it was so cool, I was a teen and wow, these guys are so heroic, fighting the good fight...<br /> <br /> Then came the Guide to the Technocracy and wow, these guys are misunderstood and flawed heroes, so cool, but we can still fight the good fight and be the heroes of the day.<br /> <br /> But now I see... They are ALL TYRANTS.<br /> <br /> And I used to be one too, and I used to be EXACTLY like that. I was a communist, by the way. Which is why my though pattern was exactly this of &quot;I know what's better for you, better than you!&quot;, but nowadays I see just how condescending and EVIL this way of thinking really is, and I absolutely loath it.<br /> <br /> Particularly because I had a grandfather who was the noblest and kindest and most WISE man I have ever knew, and he was semi illiterate. I had to compare myself towards him and I found myself lacking, and that helped to humble my &quot;tyrannical aspirations&quot; a lot.<br /> <br /> Mages however see themselves as &quot;philosopher kings&quot;; which means that they are the ultimate assholes, they are the ultimate tyrants. Because they LITERALLY embody the notion of &quot;I know what's better for you, better than you&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which is why I keep repeating myself, a victory of the Traditions would not bring a Magitech utopia of peace and freedom, but rather a Magitech with a different kind of dystopia. Because Mages know what's better for the ignorant peasants. What the &quot;ignorant peasants&quot; think or want is irrelevant, since they are basically like the beasts; and that's the core of how all despots think.<br /> <br /> Oh, just as a curiosity, that's how the real world &quot;Order of Hermes&quot; thinks too by the way. The &quot;Corpus Hermeticum&quot;, the collection of books that comprises the &quot;core&quot; of the Hermetic thinking (I'm talking about the real world cult, not the MtA game) makes that explicit about the &quot;mundanes&quot; (the non-initiate), that they are &quot;little better than animals&quot;, since they lack &quot;gnose&quot;, or the &quot;divine knowledge&quot;. I'm not making this up. To the very point that, there's a passage in the Corpus Hermeticum upon which the author is allegedly talking to Hermes Trimeguistus himself, and HT explicitly claims that evil perpetrated towards the &quot;mundanes&quot; is inconsequential and it is not really &quot;evil&quot; because those without the &quot;divine spark&quot; or &quot;gnose&quot; or whatever you wanna call it are like beasts. There are reasons for that reasoning which I won't go into details, but basically is the concept that everything is God and we must remember that we are God yadda yadda yadda and we reincarnate, therefore if you murder millions is of no consequence because they'll reincarnate anyway, and the only thing that matters is that we all remember we are God so that we can return to unity and a bunch of other mambo jambo, but I bring this up just to illustrate how utterly dangerous it is this type of thinking when one believes himself to be &quot;above the Masses&quot;. Which is what Mages do.<br /> <br /> And that's why Mages are so much worse than Vampires. Vampires are egotistical sociopaths; but Mages are so much worse, because Mages as SELF RIGHTEOUS bastards. And when you are righteous, there's no limits to what you can do <br /> <br /> For example: do you guys think that Jihadists view themselves as &quot;terrorists&quot;, let alone as EVIL?<br /> <br /> ABSOLUTELY NOT!!! In their view, they are the warriors of Allah, waging war against the enemies of Allah and agents of Shaitan. Their actions are, therefore, the ULTIMATE GOOD!<br /> <br /> When a medieval Inquisitor was burning a witch, do you think that he thought of himself as an evil bastard? Heck no! He was a pious man fighting the &quot;servants of Satan&quot; and helping to save the souls of his congregation!<br /> <br /> &quot;Evil people doesn't need any reasons to commit evil acts, but only ideology can make good people commit the worst of atrocities&quot;.<br /> <br /> The same apply to the Nazis in Germany and the commies in the USSR and China. These guys believed they were saving the world!<br /> <br /> And when you are self righteous, ANYTHING IS PERMISSABLE and anything becomes automatically &quot;good&quot; because of your &quot;noble cause&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mages are therefore the embodiment of &quot;paving the well to hell with good intentions&quot;. Every single Mage who isn't a psychopath (in which case I have to ask, why haven't you gone dance in the labyrinth of hell with the rest of the Nephandi yet) is self righteous, and thus they ALL see themselves as &quot;heroes&quot;, but the truth is that they are tyrants to whom the only reason as to why they aren't despots is because they haven't seized &quot;the crown&quot;... Yet.<br /> <br /> And that's exactly why I love this game; it's basically &quot;raw human nature&quot; at its core.<br /> <br /> PS: and I love to roleplay my &quot;heroic Mages&quot;... Knowing full well that they are everything I would NEVER want to be.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T18:43:56-07:00","id":1532466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532462#post1532462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's something I disagree with. I believe fully the Traditions teach their students that Mass Ascension is possible and there's no need to have &quot;One True Paradigm&quot; where only one kind of magic has to be accepted.<br /> <br /> Everyone can reach Rome their own way.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, is that INTERESTING? Because a substantial number of fans and implied by the &quot;Traditions don't know their foci don't do anything&quot; attitude of Revised, seem to prefer the idea that the Traditions are in an alliance of convenience even decades later.<br /> <br /> Basically, the game refuses to engage with a major source of conflict that would make the Traditions more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes. I didn't express myself very well. Yes, the Trads hold to this &quot;cherry pick&quot; idea of &quot;Mass Ascension&quot;. I didn't mean that. What I meant is that they don't really know how to do that... They don't have a plan.<br /> <br /> The Techies have a clear plan on how to do that. A fools proof plan, approved by the Ivory Tower and agreed upon every techieboy, while the Union's stamp of quality \ud83d\udc4d\ud83c\udffb<br /> <br /> And it's very simple: stick to the timetable, keep pumping &quot;the powah of da sCience!!!&quot; into the masses and eventually, everybody will Ascend... Perhaps?! Hopefully?! Yeah well...<br /> <br /> But it's a plan, regardless of if we find it stupid or not, but they actually have one and they stick to it, and most importantly, they are GUIDED by it. This gives them a clear cut direction to follow.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Trads plan is... Let the Masses free and then... Then what? Then we will see what happens?<br /> <br /> The Traditions lack a clear focus on what exactly they want to achieve or how to achieve it. And thus, they reduce it all to &quot;Not-the-Technocracy&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;We want something, we don't know what, but whatever it is, is not what the Technocracy have!&quot; Is not a very good overarching goal to follow. Which is why the Trads can only ever exist in opposition to the Union.<br /> <br /> And it's interesting what you brought up here; yes, there is this discussion about &quot;union of convenience&quot; versus &quot;shared unifying view about diversity&quot;. The idea of &quot;unifying in diversity&quot; as a paradox to begin with. You either are unified, or you are diversified.<br /> <br /> But I would say that the Trads try to do BOTH (now, here is some good &quot;Dialectics&quot; for you, embrace the contradictions), and yes, they formed this vision of &quot;no one true single path towards Enlightenment&quot; which is all good and well, but at one hand it weakens any single one of their plethora of visions - for instance, forget about &quot;Hermes Trimeguistus&quot; and the other &quot;Hermetic Masters&quot; teachings about overcoming the Material World to reach the &quot;divine realm of ideas&quot;, and also forget the notion that &quot;reality is just a dream&quot; from the Dreamspeakers, or that &quot;Science is at the eyes of the beholder&quot; from the Etherites, because none of those are &quot;da Truth&quot;, but just a weird sort of &quot;half truths&quot; at best, or incomplete truths.<br /> <br /> But then, at the same time, you now lack a clear cut path. Life is soooooo much easier when you are full of answers instead of full of questions after all. For instance, at school you'll learn that turtles, alligators and serpents are all &quot;reptiles&quot;. And that assurance is so good, and makes the world so simple. And then you go to college to study biology and you learn that, actually.... Just the same applies for atoms. In high school you'll learn that an atom is a bunch of little balls glued together being orbitted by a bunch of other smaller balls, and life is good. And then you go to college to study physics, and you learn that, well, actually....<br /> <br /> I myself, I jokingly say with a phrase that is not mine, that &quot;life was so much easier when I was a teen and I knew the answers to everything&quot;. As I grow older, instead of being a know-it-all like I used to be, now I have nothing but doubts, and I have to admit that life was so much simpler when I used to know it all \ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> The Techies are the ones the &quot;know it all&quot;. They have all the &quot;answers&quot;, while the Trads have nothing but doubts. And this is way the Union is so much better are getting their shit together than the Trads ever will be able to.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Disparates will have more success than the Traditions after all (on the long run) EXACTLY because they ARE in fact, an alliance of convenience. Because the Disparates will happily slaughter one another for the sake of their own absolute and undisputable truth that guide every fiber of my existence - but I can wait to slaughter you AFTER we slaughter those evil Technocrats. But the strength of the Disparates is that they don't compromise their ideals on behalf of some dysfunctional &quot;unity&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T18:49:32-07:00","id":1532467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532462#post1532462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's something I disagree with. I believe fully the Traditions teach their students that Mass Ascension is possible and there's no need to have &quot;One True Paradigm&quot; where only one kind of magic has to be accepted.<br /> <br /> Everyone can reach Rome their own way.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, is that INTERESTING? Because a substantial number of fans and implied by the &quot;Traditions don't know their foci don't do anything&quot; attitude of Revised, seem to prefer the idea that the Traditions are in an alliance of convenience even decades later.<br /> <br /> Basically, the game refuses to engage with a major source of conflict that would make the Traditions more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I see it, the unifying principle behind the Traditions is that they're the advocates for \u201cwe're all doing essentially the same thing!\u201d They <i>started</i> as a loose coalition united only by their opposition to the Order of Reason; but that changed very early on, and they became the \u201cbrushing differences\u201d coalition. That's more of an ideal than a reality; but it's an ideal that they actively work toward. In terms of best points vs. worst points, that's clearly one of their best points. <br /> <br /> The <i>Disparates</i>, by contrast, are a loose alliance that's holding together only because of a shared fear of what's happening with the Technocracy. Where the Traditions are a melting pot, with individual Traditions (and even individual mages) making compromises on their various approaches to Magick in the name of being better able to cooperate with each other, the Disparate Alliance is a \u201csalad bowl\u201d, with each \u201cingredient\u201d working overtime to maintain its own identity while coexisting with the others. Emphasis on \u201ccoexist\u201d, not \u201ccooperate\u201d: for the most part, the Disparates operate on a \u201cstay out of each other's way\u201d basis rather than a \u201cwhat can we do together\u201d basis. <br /> <br /> The Disparates get the \u201cinteresting infighting\u201d thing that you're talking about, leaving the Traditions with the quest for Ascension as their primary story arc. There are some Technocrats and Disparates who pursue Ascension; but they're far more rare, proportionally, than Traditionists who seek Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T19:09:45-07:00","id":1532470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532466#post1532466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, yes. I didn't express myself very well. Yes, the Trads hold to this &quot;cherry pick&quot; idea of &quot;Mass Ascension&quot;. I didn't mean that. What I meant is that they don't really know how to do that... They don't have a plan.<br /> <br /> The Techies have a clear plan on how to do that. A fools proof plan, approved by the Ivory Tower and agreed upon every techieboy, while the Union's stamp of quality \ud83d\udc4d\ud83c\udffb<br /> <br /> And it's very simple: stick to the timetable, keep pumping &quot;the powah of da sCience!!!&quot; into the masses and eventually, everybody will Ascend... Perhaps?! Hopefully?! Yeah well...</div> </div> </div> </div>A minor nitpick here: my view of the first two-and-a-half editions is that they were written almost entirely from the Traditions' perspective. Even MRev was written <i>primarily </i>from the Traditions' perspective, though MRev was the first edition that made a serious effort to consider things from the Technocracy's point of view as well \u2014 though that was clearly a \u201cfirst attempt\u201d sort of thing. As such, there are a bunch of assumptions throughout those first three editions that may not be as absolute as they made them out to be. And one of those assumptions was that all mages pursue Ascension, each in their own way. Things like the philosophies and tactics of the Union were framed in this way, with the Technocracy's Timetable being thought of as their plan for Mass Ascension. <br /> <br /> It isn't, because the Technocracy doesn't think in terms of Ascension, individual <i>or</i> Mass. Their Timetable is set up around the notion of improving the Masses' collective lot in life. They have no intention of helping the Masses <i>Awaken</i>, let alone <i>Ascend</i>. <br /> <br /> But the Traditions don't get that, because Ascension is so central to their way of thinking that they simply can't grasp the idea that someone wouldn't consider it to be all that. <br /> <br /> And for what it's worth, the Disparates are all over the map on the subject of Ascension; but by and large, it's not as high on their list of priorities as it is for the Traditions. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T19:19:19-07:00","id":1532471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532470#post1532470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A minor nitpick here: my view of the first two-and-a-half editions is that they were written almost entirely from the Traditions' perspective. Even MRev was written <i>primarily </i>from the Traditions' perspective, though MRev was the first edition that made a serious effort to consider things from the Technocracy's point of view as well \u2014 though that was clearly a \u201cfirst attempt\u201d sort of thing. As such, there are a bunch of assumptions throughout those first three editions that may not be as absolute as they made them out to be. And one of those assumptions was that all mages pursue Ascension, each in their own way. Things like the philosophies and tactics of the Union were framed in this way, with the Technocracy's Timetable being thought of as their plan for Mass Ascension.<br /> <br /> It isn't, because the Technocracy doesn't think in terms of Ascension, individual <i>or</i> Mass. Their Timetable is set up around the notion of improving the Masses' collective lot in life. They have no intention of helping the Masses <i>Awaken</i>, let alone <i>Ascend</i>.<br /> <br /> But the Traditions don't get that, because Ascension is so central to their way of thinking that they simply can't grasp the idea that someone wouldn't consider it to be all that.<br /> <br /> And for what it's worth, the Disparates are all over the map on the subject of Ascension; but by and large, it's not as high on their list of priorities as it is for the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I stand corrected.<br /> <br /> That does complement my point thou, although in a slightly different manner than I described. The Techiebois know what they want and how they want it. The Trads however just have some vague ideas about what they want and not the slightest clue on how to get it. Hence why there's no way they can win this, and their little enterprise was doomed from the start.<br /> <br /> The Disparates suffer from the opposite problem. Each individual group has their own well perceived goals and how to achieve those, but they lack the ability to properly cooperate. Thus, they too cannot hope to compete to the monolith Union.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I do wonder if the OoH wouldn't have more of a chance by itself alone...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T19:47:23-07:00","id":1532473,"title":"","content":"Since the Order of Hermes provided the \u201cglue\u201d that originally bonded the Traditions together (i.e., a shared language of Magick), I suspect they think of the other Traditions as extensions of themselves. At this stage, I think they'd feel naked without their comrades on the Fragile Path to Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T21:02:45-07:00","id":1532474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532471#post1532471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. I stand corrected.<br /> <br /> That does complement my point thou, although in a slightly different manner than I described. The Techiebois know what they want and how they want it. The Trads however just have some vague ideas about what they want and not the slightest clue on how to get it. Hence why there's no way they can win this, and their little enterprise was doomed from the start.<br /> <br /> The Disparates suffer from the opposite problem. Each individual group has their own well perceived goals and how to achieve those, but they lack the ability to properly cooperate. Thus, they too cannot hope to compete to the monolith Union.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I do wonder if the OoH wouldn't have more of a chance by itself alone...</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I'd argue yes and no there.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy absolutely says, &quot;We know absolutely what we want and how to get there. One man, at the top of the pillar, dictating down how the world works.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Traditions DO know what they want, &quot;We find the man dictating donw how the world work and shoot him in the head.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Traditions aren't a Pattern Avatar but a Dynamic avatar or Questing.<br /> <br /> They don't want to dictate how the world works and control the masses. They want to let the masses choose for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T01:59:38-07:00","id":1532484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532474#post1532474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't want to dictate how the world works and control the masses. They want to let the masses choose for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as the Sleepers chose what the Traditions think they should, yes. But what happens when the Masses choose the Technocracy? Well, obviously, they're not making an informed decision; they're ignorant Sleepers who don't know any better. So the Traditions need to find some way to Awaken them, whether they like it or not, so that the Masses can <i>then</i> choose for themselves.<br /> <br /> Only, by then, there's no going back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T13:05:24-07:00","id":1532520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532484#post1532484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As long as the Sleepers chose what the Traditions think they should, yes. But what happens when the Masses choose the Technocracy? Well, obviously, they're not making an informed decision; they're ignorant Sleepers who don't know any better. So the Traditions need to find some way to Awaken them, whether they like it or not, so that the Masses can <i>then</i> choose for themselves.<br /> <br /> Only, by then, there's no going back.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Traditions were serious about freeing the Sleepers to make their own decisions, one of the things they'd be doing is promulgating subjective reality. That's practically necessary for the sleepers to make informed decisions and its metaphysically necessary for paradigmatic freedom. I don't recall much mention of them doing that. They mostly just push their individual paradigms or syncretic combinations thereof.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't know if this oversight is intentional. It could be that the Traditions claim to want to empower sleepers, but their actions say otherwise. Alternatively, it could be that the writers just didn't think of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T14:15:13-07:00","id":1532525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532484#post1532484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As long as the Sleepers chose what the Traditions think they should, yes. But what happens when the Masses choose the Technocracy? Well, obviously, they're not making an informed decision; they're ignorant Sleepers who don't know any better. So the Traditions need to find some way to Awaken them, whether they like it or not, so that the Masses can <i>then</i> choose for themselves.<br /> <br /> Only, by then, there's no going back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, don't the Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts show the Traditions accept technocracy--just not when it comes with genocide and oppression? I feel like when everyone brings up the &quot;Traditions don't accept science&quot; they ignore these two Traditions exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T14:16:52-07:00","id":1532526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532520#post1532520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Traditions were serious about freeing the Sleepers to make their own decisions, one of the things they'd be doing is promulgating subjective reality. That's practically necessary for the sleepers to make informed decisions and its metaphysically necessary for paradigmatic freedom. I don't recall much mention of them doing that. They mostly just push their individual paradigms or syncretic combinations thereof.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't know if this oversight is intentional. It could be that the Traditions claim to want to empower sleepers, but their actions say otherwise. Alternatively, it could be that the writers just didn't think of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to recall 1 and 2 Edition state that ALL mages know that Paradigm fundamentally is just a tool for studying consensual reality. No one believes there's a difference between God, Technomagic, and Witchcraft at the base.<br /> <br /> It's all will-working.<br /> <br /> Indeed, it was implied understanding that Belief=Reality WAS what triggered Awakening and you couldn't be a mage if you DIDNT know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T14:20:53-07:00","id":1532528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532525#post1532525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, don't the Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts show the Traditions accept technocracy--just not when it comes with genocide and oppression? I feel like when everyone brings up the &quot;Traditions don't accept science&quot; they ignore these two Traditions exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking about the Masses siding with <i>Science</i>; I was talking about the Masses siding with <i>Technocracy</i>. I'm very much aware of the distinction; and if I had meant \u201cScience\u201d, I would have <i>said</i> \u201cScience\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T14:31:58-07:00","id":1532529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532526#post1532526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I seem to recall 1 and 2 Edition state that ALL mages know that Paradigm fundamentally is just a tool for studying consensual reality. No one believes there's a difference between God, Technomagic, and Witchcraft at the base.<br /> <br /> It's all will-working.<br /> <br /> Indeed, it was implied understanding that Belief=Reality WAS what triggered Awakening and you couldn't be a mage if you DIDNT know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; that was 1st and 2nd edition \u2014 the ones that, as I see it, were written from the Traditions' opinion. <br /> <br /> And it's <i>very</i> possible not to know that it's all Willworking. The idea that it's all Willworking was an innovation introduced during the founding of the Traditions \u2014 which means that it's something that's learned, not something that's instinctually known by all mages. <br /> <br /> Even in M20, the idea is that you Awaken when you realize that you have the power to change the world; you don't need to know how it works, or that the way <i>you</i> do it is the same as the way <i>other mages</i> do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T15:51:45-07:00","id":1532530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532520#post1532520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Traditions were serious about freeing the Sleepers to make their own decisions, one of the things they'd be doing is promulgating subjective reality. That's practically necessary for the sleepers to make informed decisions and its metaphysically necessary for paradigmatic freedom. I don't recall much mention of them doing that. They mostly just push their individual paradigms or syncretic combinations thereof.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't know if this oversight is intentional. It could be that the Traditions claim to want to empower sleepers, but their actions say otherwise. Alternatively, it could be that the writers just didn't think of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a somewhat messy point. On the one hand, you'd think that the Traditions <i>would</i> want to promote the \u201csubjective reality\u201d philosophy that they champion among themselves, on the theory that it would make the Consensus more accepting of seemingly conflicting Practices. But doing so has the unfortunate implication of people getting the idea into their head that if they don't like something, the sane response is to recruit a bunch of people to wish it away. My go-to example of this would be Climate Change: don't like it? Get a bunch of people to cancel it, and maybe it will go away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T18:08:59-07:00","id":1532531,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I wouldn't begrudge the Traditions not tolerating the Technocracy when the Technocracy is the ones attacking <i>them</i>.<br /> <br /> If one side is at war with you, both sides are at war.<br /> <br /> Peaceful tolerance of the Technocracy's paradigm is impossible when the paradigm requires your extermination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T18:59:57-07:00","id":1532532,"title":"","content":"\u2026and that came out of left field. Frankly, I don't know how to respond to that, because I'm not even sure what point you're trying to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T20:52:21-07:00","id":1532535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532532#post1532532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026and that came out of left field. Frankly, I don't know how to respond to that, because I'm not even sure what point you're trying to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't a response to your post so much as a statement that the Traditions can't tolerate the Technocracy as an option because the Technocracy is at war with them as their ideology.<br /> <br /> A reminder the Technocracy shot first and always shoots first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T21:29:45-07:00","id":1532539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532525#post1532525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, don't the Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts show the Traditions accept technocracy--just not when it comes with genocide and oppression? I feel like when everyone brings up the &quot;Traditions don't accept science&quot; they ignore these two Traditions exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Etherites and the VAs problem with the Technocracy is NOT about &quot;Genocide and oppression&quot;.<br /> <br /> They were both absolutely fine with &quot;genocide and oppression&quot;, until the Union decided to disavow their precious &quot;truths&quot;. The Etherites didn't leave the Union because of their &quot;authoritarianism&quot; or because of the transatlantic slave trade. They did it because the Union denied the existence of the Ether.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the VAs didn't leave because of the colonization of India, they did it because the Union was unwilling to adjust their timetable for creating Metaspace in the 1950's for the Masses.<br /> <br /> I think you are romanticizing the Trads too much and you're trying to let your personal worldview and personal bias color how you envision this fictional game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T21:45:16-07:00","id":1532541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532526#post1532526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I seem to recall 1 and 2 Edition state that ALL mages know that Paradigm fundamentally is just a tool for studying consensual reality. No one believes there's a difference between God, Technomagic, and Witchcraft at the base.<br /> <br /> It's all will-working.<br /> <br /> Indeed, it was implied understanding that Belief=Reality WAS what triggered Awakening and you couldn't be a mage if you DIDNT know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Believing that &quot;it's all willworking&quot; IS A PARADIGM.<br /> <br /> And one that is NOT shared by everybody, not even by the Trads themselves. You can be sure that there are Dreamspeakers who rather believe that it is all &quot;the will of the spirits&quot; and Choristers who believe it is all &quot;the will of the One&quot;.<br /> <br /> Besides, if one day the masses were to wake up one day with the certainty that &quot;you know what, we live in a rational world which has only one objective reality/truth, and we can find out how it works by analyzing it in a mechanistic manner&quot;, I highly doubt that the Trads would then just say &quot;you know what, we tried, but the people have spoken&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532529#post1532529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah; that was 1st and 2nd edition \u2014 the ones that, as I see it, were written from the Traditions' opinion.<br /> <br /> And it's <i>very</i> possible not to know that it's all Willworking. The idea that it's all Willworking was an innovation introduced during the founding of the Traditions \u2014 which means that it's something that's learned, not something that's instinctually known by all mages.<br /> <br /> Even in M20, the idea is that you Awaken when you realize that you have the power to change the world; you don't need to know how it works, or that the way <i>you</i> do it is the same as the way <i>other mages</i> do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. The Techies don't share this view at all. They believe in one objective truth, one to which you may not know the answers, but it is possible to find them, because they believe in a rational universe that works in a mechanistic way. This is what the Trads can NEVER accept, because it goes against EVERYTHING that they believe. One group believes in a mechanistic world, the other in a subjective one. And the Trads also cannot accept that the Masses have chosen the Technocratic view - because they have. And neither side is even willing to entertain the possibility that the other may be right. Because they are all pricks, both sides are the &quot;wise man&quot; on the top of the mountain, looking down on all others.<br /> <br /> In other worlds, like I always say, they are all condescending &quot;better-than-thou&quot; tyrants.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 03-14-2024, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T00:58:22-07:00","id":1532551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532541#post1532541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Believing that &quot;it's all willworking&quot; IS A PARADIGM.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but it's...right.<br /> <br /> All of the people who believe it's not willworking are just wrong according to the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. The Techies don't share this view at all. They believe in one objective truth, one to which you may not know the answers, but it is possible to find them, because they believe in a rational universe that works in a mechanistic way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that what they believe?<br /> <br /> Because the Technocracy wouldn't need to FORCE that into being the case if it was true; Their goal is to kill or brainwash everyone into believing it and make it true.<br /> <br /> Not because it's true now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T01:58:34-07:00","id":1532553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532525#post1532525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, don't the Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts show the Traditions accept technocracy--just not when it comes with genocide and oppression? I feel like when everyone brings up the &quot;Traditions don't accept science&quot; they ignore these two Traditions exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, moreover scientists are stated to be in many other Trads. The Heremetics especially have scientists in their ranks. There was even a Dreamspeaker who was a geologist in one of the books. The Trads reject the Technocracy's domineering violence not science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T04:41:15-07:00","id":1532556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532553#post1532553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly, moreover scientists are stated to be in many other Trads. The Heremetics especially have scientists in their ranks. There was even a Dreamspeaker who was a geologist in one of the books. The Trads reject the Technocracy's domineering violence not science.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should just keep reading at the topic, just down bellow I already addressed that, and this is false. The Trads don't reject &quot;domineering and violence&quot;. That's a juvenile view of the Traditions, and that's not the reason for the Ascension War","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T04:48:36-07:00","id":1532558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532541#post1532541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Believing that &quot;it's all willworking&quot; IS A PARADIGM.<br /> <br /> And one that is NOT shared by everybody, not even by the Trads themselves. You can be sure that there are Dreamspeakers who rather believe that it is all &quot;the will of the spirits&quot; and Choristers who believe it is all &quot;the will of the One&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532551#post1532551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but it's...right.<br /> <br /> All of the people who believe it's not willworking are just wrong according to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>And to the extent that that matters (which is surprisingly little), it hurts the game; because it promotes an \u201call liars or dupes\u201d mentality about those who don't agree with the Traditions. While that's most obviously the Technocracy, it's not limited to them. The Disparates, for example, fall into a similar \u201cliars or dupes\u201d status if they don't accept the Traditions' \u201cit's all Willworking\u201d paradigm. Which makes it hard to present them as something distinct from the Traditions without also presenting them as inherently inferior to the Traditions. <br /> <br /> But again, the idea that \u201cit's all Willworking\u201d is true is\u2026 largely unimportant, in practical terms. The idea that the Traditions <i>embrace</i> this worldview matters a great deal; and the fact that it's <i>not false</i> is important, in the sense that nobody has disproven it. But it doesn't need to be <i>true</i>, exclusive of other explanations of what Magick could be, in order for the game to work. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532541#post1532541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. The Techies don't share this view at all. They believe in one objective truth, one to which you may not know the answers, but it is possible to find them, because they believe in a rational universe that works in a mechanistic way. This is what the Trads can NEVER accept, because it goes against EVERYTHING that they believe. One group believes in a mechanistic world, the other in a subjective one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a false binary. First, the Techies <i>do</i> accept that what they do involves shaping reality; that's flat out stated in <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b>. And second, the Traditions <i>do</i> accept that there's a component of Reality that's objective; they refer to it as the Earthly Foundations, those things that remain Vulgar even when the Consensus says that they ought to be Coincidental, and vice versa. <br /> <br /> The distinction between Enlightened Science and Willworking isn't a binary choice, but one of emphasis. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532551#post1532551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that what they believe?<br /> <br /> Because the Technocracy wouldn't need to FORCE that into being the case if it was true; Their goal is to kill or brainwash everyone into believing it and make it true.<br /> <br /> Not because it's true now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Half right. Earthly Foundations exist. While they don't constrain the mage beyond the fact that certain things will always* be Vulgar, they <i>do</i> impose a layer of objective truth to reality; and to the extent that Techies actually believe that Reality <i>is</i> objective, this is what they're referring to. <br /> <br /> But Enlightened Scientists <i>also</i> believe that this is a <i>good</i> thing; and yes, that means that they also push for <i>more of it</i>. And to that extent, they <i>do</i> in fact attempt to encourage the Consensus to accept more and more extrapolations of the Earthly Foundations and to spread the notion that all of Reality is objective. <br /> <br /> Note: I said \u201cEnlightened Scientists\u201d here, and not \u201cTechnocrats\u201d; and I also said \u201cencourage the Consensus to accept\u201d, not \u201ckill or brainwash everyone into believing\u201d. This gets back into the \u201cblack and white\u201d vs. \u201cshades of gray\u201d debate, as well as the distinction I recently made between \u201cScience\u201d and \u201cTechnocracy\u201d. Enlightened Science, as I use the term, represents paradigms that promote the \u201cbuild on the Earthly Foundations\u201d notion; Technocracy is a <i>specific implementation</i> of Enlightened Science that uses coercive techniques to do so. You can't be a Technocrat without also being an Enlightened Scientist (which is one thing that distinguishes the Technocracy from <b>Awakening</b>'s Seers of the Throne, but also distinguishes it from the early Order of Reason); but you <i>can</i> be an Enlightened Scientist without being a Technocrat. Navalon exemplifies the latter. <br /> <br /> By contrast, the Traditions look at the Earthly Foundations and think \u201cthat may be <i>what is</i>; but it's not <i>what ought to be</i>\u201d; and then they set about trying to encourage the Consensus to embrace their views of \u201cwhat ought to be\u201d, regardless of whether they conflict with the Earthly Foundations. Some go so far as to search for a way to change the Earthly Foundations themselves; though that sort of thing is probably in the domain of the Archmasters. <br /> <br /> This distinction between trying to build on the Earthly Foundations vs. trying to subvert them is where I draw a line between the Enlightened Science of the Technocracy (and Navalon?) on the one hand, and the Technomancy of the Etherites and VAs on the other hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T04:49:52-07:00","id":1532559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532551#post1532551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but it's...right.<br /> <br /> All of the people who believe it's not willworking are just wrong according to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it is NOT right. It is merely possible.<br /> <br /> You gotta understand, the core books were written from the perspective of the Trads. But it isn't &quot;da Truth&quot;. It's simply one of the possibilities.<br /> <br /> And, even if it was &quot;da Truth&quot;, that would be just a coincidence. Happenstance. There are several belief systems, if one or another happens to be right, it isn't because that group is so much smarter than the rest or because they found out some secret at the Deep Umbra, but simply because they won the lottery of Paradigm.<br /> <br /> And you'll also likewise find many many people who vehemently defends that it is the Technocracy that is right all along, and with strong arguments for it. I had this same discussions over here in these forums.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is that what they believe?<br /> <br /> Because the Technocracy wouldn't need to FORCE that into being the case if it was true; Their goal is to kill or brainwash everyone into believing it and make it true.<br /> <br /> Not because it's true now. </div> </div> </div>That's a misunderstanding of the Technocratic paradigm and their idea of Consensus.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T04:55:58-07:00","id":1532560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532556#post1532556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You should just keep reading at the topic, just down bellow I already addressed that, and this is false. The Trads don't reject &quot;domineering and violence&quot;. That's a juvenile view of the Traditions, and that's not the reason for the Ascension War</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also more central to the heart of this thread than such questions as \u201cis it <i>really</i> all Willworking?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T05:20:17-07:00","id":1532561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532558#post1532558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a false binary. First, the Techies <i>do</i> accept that what they do involves shaping reality; that's flat out stated in <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, but that is not the same as saying that they believe it is simply &quot;willworking&quot;. They do not. They believe that their effects of &quot;shaping reality&quot; are based on mechanistic principles rather than &quot;I do it because I have a piece of God's soul&quot;. This is the core of it.<br /> <br /> Like I always say, WoD have heavy Gnostic elements to it, and Gnosticism preaches that first there was God, than God &quot;died&quot;, sort of, and God's soul got fragmented and countless, infinite pieces, and each piece thus begun to see itself as an individual part rather than just a mere piece of the literal &quot;bigger picture&quot;. And the largest one of those &quot;shards of God&quot; became the Demiurge, who doesn't want the pieces to get back together because the Demiurge doesn't want to give up his own individuality, he/she/it became stuck and self centered, and thus this false &quot;God&quot; created the Material World, which is an illusionary prison for the &quot;shards of God's soul&quot; so that we wouldn't figure it out that we are in fact God, so that we couldn't look into the &quot;spirit mirror&quot; and see God within ourselves.<br /> <br /> That's essentially the entire belief of the Celestial Chorus in the game, well, sort of - they don't have the idea of the Demiurge and there's a few other differences. But you'll find those Gnostic elements throughout all WoD games, so I'm heavily inclined to think that this is probably pointing to the right direction.<br /> <br /> But it is not, however, written in stone, that's just my own personal conjectures, and once again, it is not a &quot;consensus&quot; (not to mistake it for &quot;the Consensus&quot; with capital C).<br /> <br /> The Techies for instance do believe that the world is mechanistic, much like materialists atheists in the real world. They believe that &quot;reality shaping&quot; effects are mechanistic effects, not just the &quot;byproduct of the imagination of the shards of The One&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And second, the Traditions <i>do</i> accept that there's a component of Reality that's objective; they refer to it as the Earthly Foundations, those things that remain Vulgar even when the Consensus says that they ought to be Coincidental, and vice versa. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's not what it is at discussion. <br /> <br /> Even that thou, is not a consensus either. There are those that don't exactly believe in &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot; properly; Dreamspeakers for instance believe that EVERYTHING is a DREAM. EVERYTHING. Not some parts. They don't believe that &quot;reality is sleep-walking&quot; and half of it is material and mechanistic and super duper real objective while the other half is purely imagination; they believe it is ALL SUBJECTIVE. Not all of them, sure, but some do.<br /> <br /> They just have different explanations to what exactly &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot; are rather then &quot;oh this is totally undoubtedly objective truth&quot;.<br /> <br /> It may for example be the &quot;Foundations of the Demiurge&quot; or &quot;the Core code of the Matrix that cannot be changed without breaking it&quot;. <br /> <br /> The truth is, there's no consensus amongst the Trads about what the Earthly Foundations truly are or mean.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T08:03:13-07:00","id":1532577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532561#post1532561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, but that is not the same as saying that they believe it is simply &quot;willworking&quot;. They do not. They believe that their effects of &quot;shaping reality&quot; are based on mechanistic principles rather than &quot;I do it because I have a piece of God's soul&quot;. This is the core of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You won't find me disagreeing on that. I was mainly clarifying the point that their mechanistic universe includes subjective components. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532561#post1532561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I always say, WoD have heavy Gnostic elements to it, and Gnosticism preaches that first there was God, than God &quot;died&quot;, sort of, and God's soul got fragmented and countless, infinite pieces, and each piece thus begun to see itself as an individual part rather than just a mere piece of the literal &quot;bigger picture&quot;. And the largest one of those &quot;shards of God&quot; became the Demiurge, who doesn't want the pieces to get back together because the Demiurge doesn't want to give up his own individuality, he/she/it became stuck and self centered, and thus this false &quot;God&quot; created the Material World, which is an illusionary prison for the &quot;shards of God's soul&quot; so that we wouldn't figure it out that we are in fact God, so that we couldn't look into the &quot;spirit mirror&quot; and see God within ourselves.<br /> <br /> That's essentially the entire belief of the Celestial Chorus in the game, well, sort of - they don't have the idea of the Demiurge and there's a few other differences. But you'll find those Gnostic elements throughout all WoD games, so I'm heavily inclined to think that this is probably pointing to the right direction.<br /> <br /> But it is not, however, written in stone, that's just my own personal conjectures, and once again, it is not a &quot;consensus&quot; (not to mistake it for &quot;the Consensus&quot; with capital C).<br /> <br /> The Techies for instance do believe that the world is mechanistic, much like materialists atheists in the real world. They believe that &quot;reality shaping&quot; effects are mechanistic effects, not just the &quot;byproduct of the imagination of the shards of The One&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You give a good summary of the Chorister paradigm; my only disagreement with you is that I don't consider it as big a part of <b>Mage</b> as you do. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532561#post1532561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The truth is, there's no consensus amongst the Trads about what the Earthly Foundations truly are or mean.</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed. However, there <i>is</i> a consensus that the Earthly Foundations <i>exist</i>; that there are elements of reality that the Consensus can't change. Some view them in a mechanistic way; others view them as the will of greater spiritual entities like the Godhead or the Triat. Some view them in a mechanistic way; or they simply admit that they don't know. But the Earthly Foundations are still an objective truth, even if not one that's fully understood. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T09:33:56-07:00","id":1532578,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that both the malleability of reality and the Earthly Foundations tend to be overstated. This is in large part because on the outside we can make decisions about them clearly, simply, and based on the needs of our games. If I want to say that most basic physical principles are Earthly Foundations, I can make that clear statement. If you want to say that gravity and air are Earthly Foundations and everything else is up for grabs you can. We don't need to figure out the details and we don't need to run experiments to figure that out.<br /> <br /> That's not how it looks like in universe. In universe mages are aware that belief pushes some kind of metaphysical change on reality. They are aware that some things change more easily than others. They likely have a lot of observations on those changes, a few clear trends, and a lot of contradictory information. They have not figured out how far they can push reality. They have not figured out how immovable Earthly Foundations are. They have not figured out why reality is malleable, or what is happening when it shifts.<br /> <br /> The Techs and Trads have theories they push for what is going on and how it functions, but they aren't looking at the same data and they aren't looking through the same lens. This isn't a case of one being right and the other wrong. This is a case where both sides have compelling but incomplete reasons for approaching reality the way they do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T14:06:57-07:00","id":1532607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532559#post1532559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it is NOT right. It is merely possible.<br /> <br /> You gotta understand, the core books were written from the perspective of the Trads. But it isn't &quot;da Truth&quot;. It's simply one of the possibilities.<br /> <br /> And, even if it was &quot;da Truth&quot;, that would be just a coincidence. Happenstance. There are several belief systems, if one or another happens to be right, it isn't because that group is so much smarter than the rest or because they found out some secret at the Deep Umbra, but simply because they won the lottery of Paradigm.<br /> <br /> And you'll also likewise find many many people who vehemently defends that it is the Technocracy that is right all along, and with strong arguments for it. I had this same discussions over here in these forums.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's a misunderstanding of the Technocratic paradigm and their idea of Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear its not just the core books. A lot of books makes it clear that some things are right and some wrong. Some of them literally address the player from an OOC perspective<br /> <br /> Admittedly, i am not sure if this is the view of the m20 writers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T14:13:37-07:00","id":1532609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532578#post1532578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also worth noting that both the malleability of reality and the Earthly Foundations tend to be overstated. This is in large part because on the outside we can make decisions about them clearly, simply, and based on the needs of our games. If I want to say that most basic physical principles are Earthly Foundations, I can make that clear statement. If you want to say that gravity and air are Earthly Foundations and everything else is up for grabs you can. We don't need to figure out the details and we don't need to run experiments to figure that out.<br /> <br /> That's not how it looks like in universe. In universe mages are aware that belief pushes some kind of metaphysical change on reality. They are aware that some things change more easily than others. They likely have a lot of observations on those changes, a few clear trends, and a lot of contradictory information. They have not figured out how far they can push reality. They have not figured out how immovable Earthly Foundations are. They have not figured out why reality is malleable, or what is happening when it shifts.<br /> <br /> The Techs and Trads have theories they push for what is going on and how it functions, but they aren't looking at the same data and they aren't looking through the same lens. This isn't a case of one being right and the other wrong. This is a case where both sides have compelling but incomplete reasons for approaching reality the way they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a good argument that 90% of the arguments in mage are due to the fact that someone, left a decimal point off when describing how reality works to a guy writing down how magic works.<br /> <br /> How Mage actually works: &quot;If you Awaken, you can shape reality with belief.&quot;<br /> <br /> How some people think Mage works: &quot;All reality is shaped by belief, whether sleepers or not.&quot;<br /> <br /> The latter may be more interesting from an EXALTED &quot;this is not our world&quot; perspective but the former is certainly far more easy to parse as a gameline.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't change the Ascension War. It's not that the Technocracy made Faith Healing suddenly not work, it's just it only works if someone is taught magic first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T14:48:44-07:00","id":1532611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532609#post1532609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a good argument that 90% of the arguments in mage are due to the fact that someone, left a decimal point off when describing how reality works to a guy writing down how magic works.<br /> <br /> How Mage actually works: &quot;If you Awaken, you can shape reality with belief.&quot;<br /> <br /> How some people think Mage works: &quot;All reality is shaped by belief, whether sleepers or not.&quot;<br /> <br /> The latter may be more interesting from an EXALTED &quot;this is not our world&quot; perspective but the former is certainly far more easy to parse as a gameline.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't change the Ascension War. It's not that the Technocracy made Faith Healing suddenly not work, it's just it only works if someone is taught magic first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make a slight change<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot; If you Awaken you can consciously shape reality with belief&quot;<br /> &quot;If you are a sleeper you do it unconsiously&quot;<br /> &quot;By the way, the human consensus is just one out of many forces in the universe&quot;<br /> <br /> Now of course i am not certain if the m20 writers actually agree with the third point. Am i the only who dislikes a pure postmodern* or &quot;everything is chaos game?&quot; *(is postmodern the right word here? I am not a philosopher so forgive me if its an erroneous term)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T14:54:06-07:00","id":1532612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532611#post1532611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would make a slight change<br /> <br /> &quot; If you Awaken you can consciously shape reality with belief&quot;<br /> &quot;If you are a sleeper you do it unconsiously&quot;<br /> &quot;By the way, the human consensus is just one out of many forces in the universe&quot;<br /> <br /> Now of course i am not certain if the m20 writers actually agree with the third point. Am i the only who dislikes a pure postmodern* or &quot;everything is chaos game?&quot; *(is postmodern the right word here? I am not a philosopher so forgive me if its an erroneous term)</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, it's mostly a question of how weird you want the world to actually be and whether or not it's the same universe as other games.<br /> <br /> I'd argue even unconsciously, Sleepers are mostly just influencing <i>magic</i>.<br /> <br /> Which is to say Paradox is them reacting by hitting the panic button but that, otherwise, they're not doing anything to determine whether the Earth is round or not.<br /> <br /> That is the most BORING answer for how reality is affected but boring doesn't necessarily mean wrong for the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T15:02:47-07:00","id":1532613,"title":"","content":"The other half of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1492_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1492\" data-vbnamecard=\"1492\">mark</a>'s point, though, is that not everything has to be explainable as Magick; that there are supernatural phenomena in the setting that aren't Magickal in nature, and that it's mage hubris that says otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T15:45:13-07:00","id":1532617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532612#post1532612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like I said, it's mostly a question of how weird you want the world to actually be and whether or not it's the same universe as other games.<br /> <br /> I'd argue even unconsciously, Sleepers are mostly just influencing <i>magic</i>.<br /> <br /> Which is to say Paradox is them reacting by hitting the panic button but that, otherwise, they're not doing anything to determine whether the Earth is round or not.<br /> <br /> That is the most BORING answer for how reality is affected but boring doesn't necessarily mean wrong for the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really do want it to be the same as that of the other settings.<br /> Cosmological constants were, thankfully, always a thing<br /> <br /> I see it as an antivirus. Sleepers are telling it what is and what is not allowed to pass through unharmed. They also, through belief, make my tablet real.<br /> <br /> Canonnically, this is called Mundane magic.<br /> <br /> I am a bit confused, do you agree that it should be like that? You mean boring as in bad, or &quot;Boring but practical??<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532613#post1532613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other half of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1492_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1492\" data-vbnamecard=\"1492\">mark</a>'s point, though, is that not everything has to be explainable as Magick; that there are supernatural phenomena in the setting that aren't Magickal in nature, and that it's mage hubris that says otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some books do agree with precisely that. I am curious, do you like it, or do you prefer it more consensus-oriented? That is, do you, as a player&lt; see the consensus as influencing or defining reality? (I did not have time to read most of the posts so, my apologies, if you already answered)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T16:34:54-07:00","id":1532622,"title":"","content":"The latter. I feel boring but practical benefits Mage versus the idea of going full Grant Morrison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T18:12:58-07:00","id":1532627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532617#post1532617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think some books do agree with precisely that. I am curious, do you like it, or do you prefer it more consensus-oriented? That is, do you, as a player&lt; see the consensus as influencing or defining reality? (I did not have time to read most of the posts so, my apologies, if you already answered)</div> </div> </div> </div>I see the Consensus influencing reality. See my post on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/798518-the-nature-of-the-consensus\">the nature of the Consensus</a> for an in-depth dive into my view on the matter. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T07:42:57-07:00","id":1532649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532609#post1532609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a good argument that 90% of the arguments in mage are due to the fact that someone, left a decimal point off when describing how reality works to a guy writing down how magic works.<br /> <br /> How Mage actually works: &quot;If you Awaken, you can shape reality with belief.&quot;<br /> <br /> How some people think Mage works: &quot;All reality is shaped by belief, whether sleepers or not.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I wouldn't say that. For one there is a recurring premise that the weight of the belief of humanity does alter reality. There aren't rules for how, so I can see the temptation to downgrade this to only changing what mages can accomplish, but that doesn't really mesh with the history of Mage or the accomplishments of the various factions.<br /> <br /> Also, we don't have to limit belief to human belief or will. 2nd edition didn't. It floated the possibility that the spirits have a profound impact on the consensus. And if other metaphysical forces like God or the Triat are pushing things on the world, it's not unreasonable to say they are doing so through their will. It might be stretching the definitions of belief and will, but no more than Mage already does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532609#post1532609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also doesn't change the Ascension War. It's not that the Technocracy made Faith Healing suddenly not work, it's just it only works if someone is taught magic first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also wouldn't go that far. I'd say that in Mage, faith healing and herbology and a number of other techniques did used to work much more than in the modern times, and did used to be usable by sleepers, and that the difference has a lot to do with what the Technocracy pushed into the world. So in an Obi-Wan Kenobi sense, the Technocracy did make faith healing not work, from a certain point of view.<br /> <br /> But that's not the whole story. Faith healing was never as reliable as modern medicine, both because the consensus wasn't as developed then, and because even believers didn't expect it to always work. The Technocracy didn't have to undermine it so they could bring in modern medicine. They mostly drove the the change by focusing on providing a more reliable alternative.<br /> <br /> Or not. We can still depict the Technocracy as malicious enough to undermine healing just because it isn't their own. We aren't forced to take that path, though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532617#post1532617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really do want it to be the same as that of the other settings.<br /> Cosmological constants were, thankfully, always a thing<br /> <br /> I see it as an antivirus. Sleepers are telling it what is and what is not allowed to pass through unharmed. They also, through belief, make my tablet real.<br /> <br /> Canonnically, this is called Mundane magic.<br /> <br /> I am a bit confused, do you agree that it should be like that? You mean boring as in bad, or &quot;Boring but practical??</div> </div> </div> </div>I think where a lot of people have problems with a fully malleable reality is that they don't see guard rails stopping the setting from sliding into utter unrecognizability. On the other hand, some see a tendency for the consensus to reinforce the status quo. For the former, they need to add those guard rails. For the latter, the setting will remain as we expect it barring a major push.<br /> <br /> Notably, because this is a shared setting for use at the gaming table, neither side is wrong. The gaming world usually tends towards the expectations of the people at the table<br /> .<br /> <br /> On another note, the question between Influencing Reality and Defining Reality is actually two partially dependent questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Is the human belief/will the only thing pushing on reality?<br /> <br /> 2) Is all of reality malleable or just some of it?<br /> <br /> I think that's an important distinction because both 'defining' and 'influencing' can have multiple meanings.<br /> <br /> For instance, I tend towards the idea that all of reality is up for grabs, but humanity isn't the only thing doing the grabbing. I'd say reality is <i>defined</i> by belief/will but that's not limited to humans. Another person might say everything is up for grabs but because humanity isn't the sole factor, human belief only <i>influences</i> reality. Different terms, but we mean very similar things. On the other hand, a third person might say much of reality is set and can't be changed at all, so belief/will <i>influence</i> reality. That's the same term as person 2, but with a very different meaning.<br /> <br /> These are also arguments mages have in world, and though they don't have a similar influence on the outcome, the same terminology problems arise. Indeed one of the problems of the Ascension War is that the Technocracy and Traditions use different terms for the same things sometimes and similar terms with different meanings at others.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T15:04:15-07:00","id":1532667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532649#post1532649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I wouldn't say that. For one there is a recurring premise that the weight of the belief of humanity does alter reality. There aren't rules for how, so I can see the temptation to downgrade this to only changing what mages can accomplish, but that doesn't really mesh with the history of Mage or the accomplishments of the various factions.<br /> <br /> Also, we don't have to limit belief to human belief or will. 2nd edition didn't. It floated the possibility that the spirits have a profound impact on the consensus. And if other metaphysical forces like God or the Triat are pushing things on the world, it's not unreasonable to say they are doing so through their will. It might be stretching the definitions of belief and will, but no more than Mage already does.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I also wouldn't go that far. I'd say that in Mage, faith healing and herbology and a number of other techniques did used to work much more than in the modern times, and did used to be usable by sleepers, and that the difference has a lot to do with what the Technocracy pushed into the world. So in an Obi-Wan Kenobi sense, the Technocracy did make faith healing not work, from a certain point of view.<br /> <br /> But that's not the whole story. Faith healing was never as reliable as modern medicine, both because the consensus wasn't as developed then, and because even believers didn't expect it to always work. The Technocracy didn't have to undermine it so they could bring in modern medicine. They mostly drove the the change by focusing on providing a more reliable alternative.<br /> <br /> Or not. We can still depict the Technocracy as malicious enough to undermine healing just because it isn't their own. We aren't forced to take that path, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think where a lot of people have problems with a fully malleable reality is that they don't see guard rails stopping the setting from sliding into utter unrecognizability. On the other hand, some see a tendency for the consensus to reinforce the status quo. For the former, they need to add those guard rails. For the latter, the setting will remain as we expect it barring a major push.<br /> <br /> Notably, because this is a shared setting for use at the gaming table, neither side is wrong. The gaming world usually tends towards the expectations of the people at the table<br /> .<br /> <br /> On another note, the question between Influencing Reality and Defining Reality is actually two partially dependent questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Is the human belief/will the only thing pushing on reality?<br /> <br /> 2) Is all of reality malleable or just some of it?<br /> <br /> I think that's an important distinction because both 'defining' and 'influencing' can have multiple meanings.<br /> <br /> For instance, I tend towards the idea that all of reality is up for grabs, but humanity isn't the only thing doing the grabbing. I'd say reality is <i>defined</i> by belief/will but that's not limited to humans. Another person might say everything is up for grabs but because humanity isn't the sole factor, human belief only <i>influences</i> reality. Different terms, but we mean very similar things. On the other hand, a third person might say much of reality is set and can't be changed at all, so belief/will <i>influence</i> reality. That's the same term as person 2, but with a very different meaning.<br /> <br /> These are also arguments mages have in world, and though they don't have a similar influence on the outcome, the same terminology problems arise. Indeed one of the problems of the Ascension War is that the Technocracy and Traditions use different terms for the same things sometimes and similar terms with different meanings at others.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You are actually right about faith healing. This is not speculation. Its literally how its meant to work. Not just True Faith mind you. There are a variety of Invocations to be found through the gamelines, and, if i am not mistaken, they are not perfect.\\ In particular, Faith Healing, really is not meant to always work. Hell, in sometimes, it simply works by attracting, say, an angel.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they are perfect. But that's not the big issue!<br /> Two words. Ford line. Mass production. The old consensus lacked that .<br /> <br /> And yes , i do think the modern technocracy undermines Faith healing. The books, including i think, the NWO book give a similar example with homeopathy. The idea is<br /> <br /> &quot;If these things are true then what else might be true? If faith works, are demons also real? If homeopathy works are vaccines fake?(And yes, many real life idiots would reach that conclusion<br /> <br /> <br /> I suppose you could argue that if you include, say, Celestines and incarna and deities into the mix, Reality is really malleable. When books talk about cosmological constants they say &quot;these have been in place by whatever forces created/ordered the uniberse.<br /> <br /> I would argue that spirits affect the consensus more directly than a subconsious effect, but, honestly , its just a fine detail. When i say i dislikes a fully malleable reality, what i really mean is &quot;One where humanity is the sole factors defining Everything!<br /> <br /> Which terminology problems are you referring to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T15:57:03-07:00","id":1532671,"title":"","content":"Cosmological Constants, as they were described in MRev, are basically \u201cthe metaphysics of the other gamelines aren't particularly susceptible to the Consensus.\u201d The examples given for Cosmological Constants were things like \u201cthe Triat enforces <b>Werewolf</b>'s cosmology, and something like the Abrahamic God enforces <b>Vampire</b>'s metaphysics; so don't bother trying to get rid of vampires and werewolves by convincing the Masses that they don't exist.\u201d This notion is similar to <b>M20</b>'s Earthly Foundations, save only for the fact that the latter appears to be more focused on maintaining a consistent mundane reality. <br /> <br /> MRev also featured Historical Inertia, which <b>M20</b> belatedly addresses in <b>Victorian Mage</b>, when it takes about what happens when a Territory (that era's term for Reality Zone) gets depopulated: the Territory <i>gradually</i> drifts back toward the Earthly Foundations, but maintains whatever laws of reality the former Consensus imposed on it for a time after the Consensus is removed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T10:12:47-07:00","id":1532703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532671#post1532671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cosmological Constants, as they were described in MRev, are basically \u201cthe metaphysics of the other gamelines aren't particularly susceptible to the Consensus.\u201d The examples given for Cosmological Constants were things like \u201cthe Triat enforces <b>Werewolf</b>'s cosmology, and something like the Abrahamic God enforces <b>Vampire</b>'s metaphysics; so don't bother trying to get rid of vampires and werewolves by convincing the Masses that they don't exist.\u201d This notion is similar to <b>M20</b>'s Earthly Foundations, save only for the fact that the latter appears to be more focused on maintaining a consistent mundane reality.<br /> <br /> MRev also featured Historical Inertia, which <b>M20</b> belatedly addresses in <b>Victorian Mage</b>, when it takes about what happens when a Territory (that era's term for Reality Zone) gets depopulated: the Territory <i>gradually</i> drifts back toward the Earthly Foundations, but maintains whatever laws of reality the former Consensus imposed on it for a time after the Consensus is removed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am certain Mrevised regarding cosmological constants also said &quot;The earth is round, fire was always hot, 2+3= 5. bacteria were probably not made up by committee, etc) Much of this was in the core rules.<br /> <br /> Inertia, in my opinion, is why mages did not get that the Mythic era was ending until it was too late. They could not see a clear cause and effect . Not if things change, say, a century after the trigger has been pushed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T11:04:15-07:00","id":1532813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532703#post1532703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am certain Mrevised regarding cosmological constants also said &quot;The earth is round, fire was always hot, 2+3= 5. bacteria were probably not made up by committee, etc) Much of this was in the core rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't specifically remember those all being cosmological constants, but even so, those are very different statements and they address different things.<br /> <br /> Changing 2+3 to 4 is matter of sense vs nonsense. Either we are redefining the word 'four,' to mean 'five' which is not a reality change, or we are saying something meaningless like &quot;square circle&quot;. It's not really a limit on the power of the Consensus to say it can't do that, just like it's not a limit to say it can't <i>flibble wurble bing</i>.<br /> <br /> Fire being hot is more of a mythic/narrative thing. It's not that we can't think up a world where that doesn't happen, but so much of culture and experience and storytelling is based around fire and the nature of fire. That Cosmological Constant is preserving a form of narrative weight.<br /> <br /> Bacteria as a Cosmological Constant is establishing the explanation as a CC rather than the phenomenon. That is, there's a good case for disease itself being a CC, but bacteria are a modern, largely imperceptible explanation for disease. They don't need to be entrenched as a foundational principle of reality at all and there are plenty of fantasy worlds where diseases are caused by humors or spirits. Not to mention, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> has said on a few occasions, if you can only see something with scientific instruments, it may just be part of the focus rather than part of the Tapestry.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Round World CC is arbitrary. Not only are flat worlds quite common in fiction (just look at Exalted) but Sorcerers Crusade suggests a nonlinear world where the same path doesn't always lead to the same place, and that's an even stranger possibility.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T16:39:16-07:00","id":1533140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532813#post1532813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't specifically remember those all being cosmological constants, but even so, those are very different statements and they address different things.<br /> <br /> Changing 2+3 to 4 is matter of sense vs nonsense. Either we are redefining the word 'four,' to mean 'five' which is not a reality change, or we are saying something meaningless like &quot;square circle&quot;. It's not really a limit on the power of the Consensus to say it can't do that, just like it's not a limit to say it can't <i>flibble wurble bing</i>.<br /> <br /> Fire being hot is more of a mythic/narrative thing. It's not that we can't think up a world where that doesn't happen, but so much of culture and experience and storytelling is based around fire and the nature of fire. That Cosmological Constant is preserving a form of narrative weight.<br /> <br /> Bacteria as a Cosmological Constant is establishing the explanation as a CC rather than the phenomenon. That is, there's a good case for disease itself being a CC, but bacteria are a modern, largely imperceptible explanation for disease. They don't need to be entrenched as a foundational principle of reality at all and there are plenty of fantasy worlds where diseases are caused by humors or spirits. Not to mention, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> has said on a few occasions, if you can only see something with scientific instruments, it may just be part of the focus rather than part of the Tapestry.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Round World CC is arbitrary. Not only are flat worlds quite common in fiction (just look at Exalted) but Sorcerers Crusade suggests a nonlinear world where the same path doesn't always lead to the same place, and that's an even stranger possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we are using slightly different definitions. Is Foundation/CC meant to be something that &quot;whose absence or opposite you can not conceive?&quot; Because this is more like the &quot;beyond&quot; of Oramus in Exalted","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T06:49:57-07:00","id":1533165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1532649#post1532649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stuff + :<br /> .<br /> <br /> On another note, the question between Influencing Reality and Defining Reality is actually two partially dependent questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Is the human belief/will the only thing pushing on reality?<br /> <br /> 2) Is all of reality malleable or just some of it?<br /> <br /> I think that's an important distinction because both 'defining' and 'influencing' can have multiple meanings.<br /> <br /> For instance, I tend towards the idea that all of reality is up for grabs, but humanity isn't the only thing doing the grabbing. I'd say reality is <i>defined</i> by belief/will but that's not limited to humans. Another person might say everything is up for grabs but because humanity isn't the sole factor, human belief only <i>influences</i> reality. Different terms, but we mean very similar things. On the other hand, a third person might say much of reality is set and can't be changed at all, so belief/will <i>influence</i> reality. That's the same term as person 2, but with a very different meaning.<br /> <br /> These are also arguments mages have in world, and though they don't have a similar influence on the outcome, the same terminology problems arise. Indeed one of the problems of the Ascension War is that the Technocracy and Traditions use different terms for the same things sometimes and similar terms with different meanings at others.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am of the exact same mind. Several years ago I posted a topic asking if the Earth was flat before the techies.<br /> <br /> The thing is, what Mages call &quot;Consensus&quot; is simply the HUMAN Consensus.<br /> <br /> WoD is an animistic world. It may or may not be Monotheistic or Gnostic - or even atheistic - on top of that, but if there's one undeniable truth is that it is animistic. That is undeniable, and no amount of &quot;belief&quot; can deny that - it can only deny that fact.<br /> <br /> This means that everything has an associated spirit (call it &quot;dimensional entities&quot; or whatever else you'd like). Rocks, threes and even feelings or ideas have spirits. The spirit of Cobalt, the spirit of Love, the spirit of Wolf, the spirit of Rotten Milk and the spirit of Honest Transactions.<br /> <br /> This means that human will and human Consensus is NOT the only force and the only will at work in the universe.<br /> <br /> &quot;Gravity is an Earth Foundation&quot;. Well, I don't fully agree. I agree with that in the sense that, even if you were able to brainwash every single human into the belief that humans can fly, that still wouldn't happen.<br /> <br /> However however however...<br /> <br /> If you could convince ALL (or at least, the majority) of the &quot;Spirits of Gravity&quot; that &quot;Gravity&quot; only pulls down those that are willing to be pulled down, than this &quot;Earth Foundation&quot; would be under a new COSMOLOGICAL CONSENSUS (as opposed to &quot;Human Consensus&quot;).<br /> <br /> From a practical point of view, that changes nothing; there will never be any way to convince 51% of all Gravity Spirits to change their minds about their very reason to exist, so you CAN safely call it a &quot;Cosmological Constant&quot;, because for all practical effects IT IS CONSTANT, but the fact remains that, this so called &quot;Constant&quot; only remains constant as insofar as there's a will (or a collection of wills) sustaining it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T09:22:03-07:00","id":1533171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533140#post1533140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we are using slightly different definitions. Is Foundation/CC meant to be something that &quot;whose absence or opposite you can not conceive?&quot; Because this is more like the &quot;beyond&quot; of Oramus in Exalted</div> </div> </div> </div>That was part of my point. Those four potential CCs are different kinds of restrictions and/or have different justifications. The mathematical one is a restriction based on the sheer difficulty of envisioning how the world would work if mages could make that change. It's a CC that saves the time and difficulty of explaining why such a change is impossible by any other means.<br /> <br /> The other three CCs were not about the limits of our imagination at all. I brought up how easy it is to envision worlds where they are not true to illustrate that. Instead they are preserving some other aspect of the world that the writers or the ST want to keep static. It's not that fire has to be hot , its that we want Mage to largely exist in a world where fire is hot. It's not that the world has to be round, it is that we want Mage to exist in a where the earth is round... except when we don't.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T10:27:41-07:00","id":1533172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533171#post1533171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was part of my point. Those four potential CCs are different kinds of restrictions and/or have different justifications. The mathematical one is a restriction based on the sheer difficulty of envisioning how the world would work if mages could make that change. It's a CC that saves the time and difficulty of explaining why such a change is impossible by any other means.<br /> <br /> The other three CCs were not about the limits of our imagination at all. I brought up how easy it is to envision worlds where they are not true to illustrate that. Instead they are preserving some other aspect of the world that the writers or the ST want to keep static. It's not that fire has to be hot , its that we want Mage to largely exist in a world where fire is hot. It's not that the world has to be round, it is that we want Mage to exist in a where the earth is round... except when we don't.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah i see. Yes you are right. I should have read it better. By the way, to be clear, do you see the consensus as including non-humans ?( maybe you mentioned it, but i don't really have time to check right now sorry)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> To be honest, i find the opposite as boring. That is, i do like the idea of some things being &quot;true&quot; and having mages trying to prove one thing or another to each tradition only for them to say &quot;well, no because i think the theory should work differently&quot;<br /> <br /> But to be clear, when i say &quot;True&quot; i mean it less &quot;inviolable rules of the universe&quot;<br /> <br /> And more &quot;rules that came to be .. .somehow&quot;<br /> <br /> That is, i expand the definition of CC to include, as Ramnesis says, explanations, but with the caveat that &quot;something&quot; arbitrarily caused them to be.<br /> <br /> So a Hermetic would be less &quot; Enochian is a fragment of the primordial language of the Universe because it is an eternal truth&quot; and more&quot; It is a fragment of the primordial language because someone wrote it&quot; Or if you will :<br /> <br /> &quot;Some early Consensus-makers wrote it into the engine of the Universe. Technically, they could have done differently. Technically, a new Consensus could remove it<br /> Just not a Consensus of &quot;just&quot; humans<br /> <br /> Am i weird for preferring it like that?<br /> <br /> And to go back to the original thread lol : How many people would you say are like the Seers of the Throne in this game?<br /> <br /> That is, how many members* of the Traditions would be evil enough to say&quot; Fuck humanity, i just want to throw fireballs coincidentally once again, let them go back to the dark ages&quot; (Less extremes interpretations that sum up to &quot;I would make things at least marginally worse for the masses if it helped my magick&quot; also count&quot;)<br /> <br /> * individuals i mean. Personally, i put it at around 20% Increasing for the old masters, and decreasing for someone who awoke 5 years ago Am i too cynical?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:21:59-07:00","id":1533188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533172#post1533172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah i see. Yes you are right. I should have read it better. By the way, to be clear, do you see the consensus as including non-humans ?( maybe you mentioned it, but i don't really have time to check right now sorry)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>2nd Edition suggested that spirits do contribute to the consensus, which I found out years ago during an ill conceived attempt to win an argument by quote mining. Since then I've grown more and more fond of the idea. If spirits contribute to the consensus they provide both a natural inertia and a stabilizing force to subjective reality. Not only that, but it makes the Umbra a much more important front in the Ascension War. <br /> <br /> So my general stance is that yes, they do, though not as strongly as humanity does. I also don't have any hard rules on the mechanics of how much they affect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T13:31:35-07:00","id":1533196,"title":"","content":"My view is to define the Consensus specifically as humanity's influence on the nature of reality, instead of being \u201cany and all sentient entities that influence reality\u201d. Which isn't to say that the Consensus is the <i>only</i> thing that influences reality; rather, I want a term that I can use to describe \u201cwhat the people in this town believe\u201d as distinct from \u201cwhat the people in this town, as well as the spirits in this town and whatever other potential influencers that may or may not exist, believe\u201d. For those mages who believe that everything's subjective once you've included all of the influencers, the word for the latter is \u201cReality\u201d; but it's one of those things where the distinction between \u201cwhat is innately true\u201d vs. \u201cwhat is true because that's what the Weaver believes\u201d is moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T13:55:26-07:00","id":1533197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533188#post1533188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2nd Edition suggested that spirits do contribute to the consensus, which I found out years ago during an ill conceived attempt to win an argument by quote mining. Since then I've grown more and more fond of the idea. If spirits contribute to the consensus they provide both a natural inertia and a stabilizing force to subjective reality. Not only that, but it makes the Umbra a much more important front in the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> So my general stance is that yes, they do, though not as strongly as humanity does. I also don't have any hard rules on the mechanics of how much they affect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Revised continued with the same idea . I'd say the general law of &quot;Distance reduces power&quot; should apply. Humans should affect, say, Philadelphia more than Andromeda or for that matter the epiphanies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a><br /> <br /> Pretty much. I mean, what is the difference between a) everything subconsciously affecting reality vs b) humanity doing it subconsciously while the local friendly Maeljin incarna doing it consiously?<br /> Zero, outside of philosophical debates<br /> <br /> I agree with your definition of consensus, The problem is that many players have the more inclusive definition in mind when using the term. I have been in discussions where the actual disagreement was non-existent, but where we did not understand we were talking about something else.<br /> <br /> But to be honest i do prefer the game subtly, very subtly, giving us hints about, say , whether x or y belief in z tradition is wrong or not.<br /> <br /> For instance, according to at least two books &quot;A majority of mages believe that the higher you get in the astral umbra the more you find things originating from there rather than the human mind.<br /> On the other hand, the lower you go, the more you find humanity's personal thoughts.<br /> <br /> Its a good compromises between , say , platonic realism and &quot;everything is chaos&quot;<br /> <br /> OR at least i like it personally","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T14:23:19-07:00","id":1533200,"title":"","content":"Elaborating on this: the mages call the Consensus of humanity \u201cthe Consensus\u201d because that's what they can influence. They don't have any way to influence what Weaver spirits believe, as that's purely the domain of the Weaver (assuming she isn't \u201cmerely\u201d the collective beliefs of the Weaver spirits) , so you have a chicken and egg question about whether the Weaver brought scientific principles into existence or whether they always existed and the Weaver is just championing them. But since both are equally immutable, does it matter?<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T17:06:37-07:00","id":1533218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533200#post1533200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elaborating on this: the mages call the Consensus of humanity \u201cthe Consensus\u201d because that's what they can influence. They don't have any way to influence what Weaver spirits believe, as that's purely the domain of the Weaver (assuming she isn't \u201cmerely\u201d the collective beliefs of the Weaver spirits) , so you have a chicken and egg question about whether the Weaver brought scientific principles into existence or whether they always existed and the Weaver is just championing them. But since both are equally immutable, does it matter?<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It does matter. Technicalities like that are what fuel many theological debates. And that is perfectly appropriate for Mage. By taking other games like Werewolf into consideration, you necessarily have to step down on the basic premise of Mage, at least to a degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T17:18:31-07:00","id":1533219,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the &quot;Was the World Flat Before the Consensus said otherwise?&quot; is pretty much the default, &quot;The idea that reality is defined by belief&quot; rabbit hole writ large.<br /> <br /> And while it's the <b>Boring but Practical</b> answer, it's why I go with only the Awakened affect reality.<br /> <br /> It also reorientates the conflict of mages between one another.<br /> <br /> I don't see any problem with some mages believing this but it also would probably be a sign of Quiet or Marauderdom on the way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T20:54:49-07:00","id":1533228,"title":"","content":"\u201cThe world was flat before the Consensus\u201d isn't a statement about whether or not reality is subjective; it's a statement about whether or not \u201cthe world is round\u201d is an Earthly Foundation/Cosmological Constant: if the Consensus was able to change it, it isn't.<br /> <br /> What answers the question of whether reality is subjective is whether or not the things that the Consensus can't change are the result of some unimaginably powerful entity (such as God, Gaia, or the Weaver) wills it to be so (in which case reality is subjective) or if the things that the Consensus can't change simply are what they are. Now, reality certainly isn't <i>purely</i> objective, because both the Consensus and the Awakened can change it (in the form of Reality Zones in the former case, and in the form of Magickal Effects in the latter case); but it <i>might</i> be purely <i>subjective, </i>if the parts that the Consensus can't change are subjective. <br /> <br /> That said, I don't consider that too be a particularly interesting question, because it doesn't really affect anything that matters. What's more interesting is the question of what the Consensus can and can't do. In the earliest editions of the game, there wasn't much that the Consensus couldn't do; but in M20, the only thing we know for a fact that the Consensus can do is to define where the boundary between Vulgar and Coincidental Magick is; and even that's limited by the Earthly Foundations. In M20, each Awakened is arguably far more powerful than the Consensus, because mages can actually <i>do</i> things; the Consensus can only decide, somewhat, whether or not mages get punished for doing things. <br /> <br /> Let me repeat that: the Consensus can't stop a mage from doing something; it can only punish the mage for doing it. Likewise with Cosmological Constants, or Historical Inertia, or Earthly Foundations; these things don't forbid a mage from doing anything. They merely decide what the mage gets punished for. The only thing that arguably restricts what a mage can do, besides the mage's own Focus, is Countermagic; and neither the Consensus nor the Earthly Foundations do Countermagic. Since even an Arete 1 mage can do Countermagic, that's a remarkably weak Consensus. <br /> <br /> Now, the Consensus <i>might</i> also be able to make some things mundane that would otherwise be Coincidental, meaning that you don't need to make an Arete roll to do it; this is a widely held bit of fanon, and it's essential to any theory that holds that the Consensus can actually do something other than play reality cop. But surprisingly, it's never explicitly confirmed in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T06:44:44-07:00","id":1533249,"title":"","content":"A slight correction to the above: I overlooked one aspect about Reality Zones. In addition to defining whether or not an Effect is Coincidental or Vulgar, it can reduce the difficulty of a Coincidental Effect or increase the difficulty of a Vulgar Effect, by up to 3; and <i>that</i> can be considered \u201chindering Magick\u201d, as increased Difficulty tends to mean fewer successes. In fact, with the rule for Thresholds in place, a high-rank Effect that is defined as Vulgar with a significant difficulty increase could be thought of as not merely \u201cdisliked\u201d by the RZ, but actively <i>forbidden</i>: a Master Effect with +1 Difficulty becomes Difficulty 9 and needs an extra success to succeed. The mechanism of getting there is a bit different; but the result is similar to a limited sort of Countermagic. <br /> <br /> And sometimes a simple house rule can have profound effects. I have a \u201creverse Threshold\u201d house rule that says that if you have enough Difficulty reductions to bring the difficulty below 3, the extra reductions get converted into automatic successes. Applying this to RZs: a one-dot Simple Feat (requiring one success) that's defined as Coincidental with a \u20132 Difficulty reduction will instead automatically succeed; and if that Difficulty reduction is \u20133, the Effect could be a two-dot Simple Feat or a one-dot Standard Feat. Note that this is independent of your Arete; so it's arguable that even Sleepers should be able to take advantage of this. As such, the \u201creverse Threshold\u201d house rule implements a limited way for the Consensus to push low-level Simple and Standard Feats <i>beyond</i> Coincidental, and into the realm of the downright <i>mundane</i>. <br /> <br /> That approach has its limitations: if that's how a RZ can integrate Effects fully, to the point that they're not even considered to be Magick anymore, it can only do so with one- or two-dot Simple Feats or one-dot Standard Feats. Still, that can cover <i>a lot</i> of ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T07:27:52-07:00","id":1533250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533228#post1533228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, the Consensus <i>might</i> also be able to make some things mundane that would otherwise be Coincidental, meaning that you don't need to make an Arete roll to do it; this is a widely held bit of fanon, and it's essential to any theory that holds that the Consensus can actually do something other than play reality cop. But surprisingly, it's never explicitly confirmed in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not explicitly confirmed because it's explicitly made optional. It's one of the three options given at the beginning of M20s reality zones section, along with the Consensus Just Determines Coincidental vs Vulgar, and Technocratic Reality is Default Reality. That's hardly fanon. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you meant that there exists a quasi state between magic and reality where what the mage is doing isn't an Arete roll but is still beyond the capabilities of the sleepers, that is indeed fanon. I don't think its a necessary element of the Consensus doing something other than reality cop, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T09:14:41-07:00","id":1533255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533188#post1533188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2nd Edition suggested that spirits do contribute to the consensus, which I found out years ago during an ill conceived attempt to win an argument by quote mining. Since then I've grown more and more fond of the idea. If spirits contribute to the consensus they provide both a natural inertia and a stabilizing force to subjective reality. Not only that, but it makes the Umbra a much more important front in the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> So my general stance is that yes, they do, though not as strongly as humanity does. I also don't have any hard rules on the mechanics of how much they affect.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, it's in 2ed. I'd say thou that Spirits contribute towards &quot;Consensus&quot; (or at least the Cosmological Consensus) a lot more than humanity does. After all, by this way of defining the universe, fire is hot, water is wet, the Earth is round and gravity pulls things instead of repulsing them because of the Spirits, irregardless of what humans think.<br /> <br /> The so called &quot;Consensus&quot; that is human-made and towards which Techies and Trads fight over would be the &quot;Creation's Leftovers&quot;, or the areas upon which the &quot;Spirits don't hold strong opinions about&quot;.<br /> <br /> I also agree, this turns the Umbra into a much more important and vital battle ground; suddenly creating &quot;Spirits of Bacterias&quot; with Spirit 5 could actually change the Cosmological Consensus upon which diseases are the result of curses, to one upon which they are caused by microorganisms...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T09:34:31-07:00","id":1533256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533196#post1533196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My view is to define the Consensus specifically as humanity's influence on the nature of reality, instead of being \u201cany and all sentient entities that influence reality\u201d. Which isn't to say that the Consensus is the <i>only</i> thing that influences reality; rather, I want a term that I can use to describe \u201cwhat the people in this town believe\u201d as distinct from \u201cwhat the people in this town, as well as the spirits in this town and whatever other potential influencers that may or may not exist, believe\u201d. For those mages who believe that everything's subjective once you've included all of the influencers, the word for the latter is \u201cReality\u201d; but it's one of those things where the distinction between \u201cwhat is innately true\u201d vs. \u201cwhat is true because that's what the Weaver believes\u201d is moot.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can say that with conviction, because Spirits don't actually (or don't necessarily) have free will. They are bound to their roles and their nature. A Fire Spirit cannot decide to be cold, the Weaver cannot decide to no try to instill order. In that sense, spirits are pretty constant.<br /> <br /> So, if the Spirit's &quot;Consensus&quot; is constant, the only variable in the equation are the humans.<br /> <br /> In order to truly change the so called &quot;Earthly Foundations&quot;, or better called &quot;Cosmological Consensus&quot;, you'd have to do like Wyrm and Weaver does, and try to actively promote a sort of &quot;spiritual genocide&quot; at the Umbra level, in order to promote an active change of the spiritual landscape of the Spirit words.<br /> <br /> That &quot;spiritual genocide&quot; don't just include extermination of &quot;undesirable spirits&quot;, but also their replacement by new ones; that could very well be the case of my example on the answer above about diseases being caused by curses vs microorganisms. I'm not saying that this was in fact what happened, but I'm saying that it COULD, this could be introduced as a de facto occuring in any table; not that the Union did it on purpose or that they knew what to do or how to do it, but when they introduced &quot;microorganisms&quot;, spirits representing those were immediately born (or the OoR created them with Dimensional Science 5 even), and unknowingly to the Techies, those new &quot;spirits of microorganisms&quot; started to wage a spirit war in the Umbra against &quot;cursing spirits&quot;, and they got aided by the Union relentless pursuit of curses and faith healing; this stablished a positive feedback loop upon which those new spirits reinforced the work of the Union and the work of the Union reinforced those new spirits, until such a a time where that old &quot;Earthly Foundation&quot; got effectively changed - while at the meanwhile, everybody thought that it was &quot;just&quot; part of the (normal/human) Consensus.<br /> <br /> That's just a possibility mind you, and not set on stone. But it does gives more malleability to the players without screwing the setting (no, a Marauder still won't be able to make the &quot;anti-grav spirits&quot; become dominating in the Umbra).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T09:43:34-07:00","id":1533258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533200#post1533200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elaborating on this: the mages call the Consensus of humanity \u201cthe Consensus\u201d because that's what they can influence. They don't have any way to influence what Weaver spirits believe, as that's purely the domain of the Weaver (assuming she isn't \u201cmerely\u201d the collective beliefs of the Weaver spirits) , so you have a chicken and egg question about whether the Weaver brought scientific principles into existence or whether they always existed and the Weaver is just championing them. But since both are equally immutable, does it matter?<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. At the end of the day, the limit to the (human) Consensus is whatever it isn't set &quot;on stone&quot; by the &quot;Cosmological (spiritual) Consensus&quot;. AKA you can't convince the &quot;Weaver&quot; (or the collective &quot;spirits of order&quot;) to behave chaotically.<br /> <br /> What Mages can influence in the (human) Consensus is whatever is leftover from the &quot;natural spirit order&quot;... Or, let's say, if what the &quot;spirit ecosystem&quot; has laid out for the formation of the world is a &quot;set of laws&quot;, then the (human) Consensus are the little breeches and loopholes and small letters of that code; and the work of the Mages is that of a good lawyer or good accountant... But to become a true &quot;legislator&quot; requires herculean labors (a lawyer can find loopholes in the law, but it's much harder to get the president to sign an executive order)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T09:53:56-07:00","id":1533259,"title":"","content":"In a Werewolf/Mage crossover game, I could see going for that. In a pure Mage game, though, that idea that spirits influence reality should be a belief, not an established fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T10:07:48-07:00","id":1533260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533250#post1533250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not explicitly confirmed because it's explicitly made optional. It's one of the three options given at the beginning of M20s reality zones section, along with the Consensus Just Determines Coincidental vs Vulgar, and Technocratic Reality is Default Reality. That's hardly fanon.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you meant that there exists a quasi state between magic and reality where what the mage is doing isn't an Arete roll but is still beyond the capabilities of the sleepers, that is indeed fanon. I don't think its a necessary element of the Consensus doing something other than reality cop, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, what I meant was that Reality Zones might be able to change what Sleepers are capable of, too. The \u201creverse Threshold\u201d house rule I was just musing about doesn't depend on the dice pool of the person attempting the feat (Arete, in the case of the \u201cmundane Magick\u201d Effects); so I could potentially see even Sleepers being able to perform such Effects: they would get the requisite Automatic Successes just like the Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T10:09:27-07:00","id":1533261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533255#post1533255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is true, it's in 2ed. I'd say thou that Spirits contribute towards &quot;Consensus&quot; (or at least the Cosmological Consensus) a lot more than humanity does. After all, by this way of defining the universe, fire is hot, water is wet, the Earth is round and gravity pulls things instead of repulsing them because of the Spirits, irregardless of what humans think.<br /> <br /> The so called &quot;Consensus&quot; that is human-made and towards which Techies and Trads fight over would be the &quot;Creation's Leftovers&quot;, or the areas upon which the &quot;Spirits don't hold strong opinions about&quot;.<br /> <br /> I also agree, this turns the Umbra into a much more important and vital battle ground; suddenly creating &quot;Spirits of Bacterias&quot; with Spirit 5 could actually change the Cosmological Consensus upon which diseases are the result of curses, to one upon which they are caused by microorganisms...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, although I wouldn't say that mages are fighting over creation's leftovers. The way I'd describe it is that Sleepers and Spirits affect the same Consensus (more or less) and that Spirits do this by believing what they are. Whatever the spirits are, that's what they reinforce.<br /> <br /> But there's a natural feedback between the physical world and spirits that represent or embody part of that world. As the physical world changes, so to do the spirits. This means that the spirits will start off pushing against any changes to physical reality, but over time as they shift in response to the new reality they will start supporting it instead.<br /> <br /> To a point anyways. Spirits are not just influenced by physical reality but metaphysical reality. Spirits associated with some other great force (like the Weaver, since it's been brought up) are influenced into shape by that force. Those forces, then will have a powerful effect on the consensus because of their choirs.<br /> <br /> At least that's a way it could work that covers a lot of the elements I think are necessary. It's a fun idea but it is way more specific than we need for Mage. Really I think Mage works just fine on a foundation of:<br /> <br /> All of reality is up for grabs.<br /> Mages are not the only ones grabbing.<br /> Some things are much, much harder to change than others.<br /> Subjective reality is complicated.<br /> There are lots of fronts in the Ascension War.<br /> <br /> If you have those the setting and storyline make a reasonable amount of sense. There are other foundations that can provide a similar amount of sense, too, these are just my preferred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T10:15:55-07:00","id":1533262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533260#post1533260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, what I meant was that Reality Zones might be able to change what Sleepers are capable of, too. The \u201creverse Threshold\u201d house rule I was just musing about doesn't depend on the dice pool of the person attempting the feat (Arete, in the case of the \u201cmundane Magick\u201d Effects); so I could potentially see even Sleepers being able to perform such Effects: they would get the requisite Automatic Successes just like the Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does make more sense It's certainly a workable way of handling the transition between awakened magic and mundane reality. It also works whether or not there is an underlying baseline reality. I can see a lot of directions this could be taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T13:15:21-07:00","id":1533270,"title":"","content":"Whether or not reality is subjective has to remain ambiguous in order for the premise of Mage to work. Some mages have more open paradigms; others do not. If one group is demonstrably wrong, then one attacks the basic theme of Mage. I think that getting too deep into the mechanics of the Consensus misses this crucial point. Mage should not be bound by the settings of other games. Many of the limits imposed on the Consensus are due to concerns of game balance. Mages should not care about God or Gaia, unless they are involved in their paradigms. By having to establish that God manifested the curse of vampirism or that reality is governed by the Triat, you necessarily soften the game's core theme. The battle for reality is not just about rendering one's preferred type of magic Coincidental in a given area. It is about standing for what you hold. Mechanically defining the influence of the Consensus can dilute what the game is ultimately about; that is, will-workers of vastly different stripes trying to spread their worldviews and attain Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T14:16:25-07:00","id":1533278,"title":"","content":"This is what I meant by Subjective Reality has to be complicated. And I mean it's complicated in the Facebook Relationship sense. <br /> <br /> There has to be a way that the Traditions can think that they are all doing similar things while preferring their specific paradigms. There needs to be a way for the Technocracy to think that it can alter reality while still thinking it is operating off of consistent (or at least semi consistent) principles. <br /> <br /> That sounds difficult, but it is quite common in our world. There are competing views about physics and metaphysics and theology all the time. Sometimes it is obvious to reasonable onlookers which side is right, other times there are compelling arguments on both sides and it takes years to work through who is right. That's because reality is complicated and it is difficult to take it all in at once. A complicated Subjective Reality would provide enough justification for the competing points of view we see.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean it needs to be complicated for the players. We don't have have to have in depth explanations of the Traditions metaphysical arguments or comprehensive charts of the data the Technocracy has gathered. We can simplify it to a short and quick explanation with and cover the rest with an &quot;It's complicated&quot; disclaimer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T23:30:55-07:00","id":1533301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533270#post1533270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether or not reality is subjective has to remain ambiguous in order for the premise of Mage to work. Some mages have more open paradigms; others do not. If one group is demonstrably wrong, then one attacks the basic theme of Mage. I think that getting too deep into the mechanics of the Consensus misses this crucial point. Mage should not be bound by the settings of other games. Many of the limits imposed on the Consensus are due to concerns of game balance. Mages should not care about God or Gaia, unless they are involved in their paradigms. By having to establish that God manifested the curse of vampirism or that reality is governed by the Triat, you necessarily soften the game's core theme. The battle for reality is not just about rendering one's preferred type of magic Coincidental in a given area. It is about standing for what you hold. Mechanically defining the influence of the Consensus can dilute what the game is ultimately about; that is, will-workers of vastly different stripes trying to spread their worldviews and attain Ascension.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Gaia, the Triat or even &quot;God&quot; aren't even a thing in Mage. Well, God is real for some Mages, but not all, but as for Gaia and the Triat, they are never mentioned, so for all purposes you could say they are nonexistent. I just used &quot;Weaver&quot; to exemplify, but I guess that this caused some confusion, but let me clarify that Im not trying to add WtA crossovers. &quot;Spirits of Order&quot; would do just fine, with the main &quot;Spirit of Order&quot; being just one of the countless Incarna that inhabit the Umbra. I just used the word &quot;Weaver&quot; because, you know, words have power (as any good Mage already knows), and thus that immediately invokes the idea of order, but I see now that my spell were perhaps a little bit stronger than it should have been.<br /> <br /> &quot;Spirits&quot; are actually just &quot;trans dimensional entities&quot;, and it is a know fact that those reality abominations from other dimensions distort our own reality by their very presence; that's how they interfere with Consensus, and why they are so dangerous and unpredictable - the worst of which being the so called &quot;Avatars&quot;, those dimensional alien parasites that latches onto those delusional superstitionists of the Traditions (luckily for us Enlightened people, we are immune to that). Regardless, those trans dimensional entities shape the Cosmological Consensus (and are also shaped by our own reality due to Quantum Entanglement).<br /> <br /> That is why it would be far better to detach our core dimension from those alternative universes as much as possible, to prevent those weird parallel worlds from distorting the physical laws of our own universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T00:29:17-07:00","id":1533302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533301#post1533301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Gaia, the Triat or even &quot;God&quot; aren't even a thing in Mage. Well, God is real for some Mages, but not all, but as for Gaia and the Triat, they are never mentioned, so for all purposes you could say they are nonexistent. I just used &quot;Weaver&quot; to exemplify, but I guess that this caused some confusion, but let me clarify that Im not trying to add WtA crossovers. &quot;Spirits of Order&quot; would do just fine, with the main &quot;Spirit of Order&quot; being just one of the countless Incarna that inhabit the Umbra. I just used the word &quot;Weaver&quot; because, you know, words have power (as any good Mage already knows), and thus that immediately invokes the idea of order, but I see now that my spell were perhaps a little bit stronger than it should have been.<br /> <br /> &quot;Spirits&quot; are actually just &quot;trans dimensional entities&quot;, and it is a know fact that those reality abominations from other dimensions distort our own reality by their very presence; that's how they interfere with Consensus, and why they are so dangerous and unpredictable - the worst of which being the so called &quot;Avatars&quot;, those dimensional alien parasites that latches onto those delusional superstitionists of the Traditions (luckily for us Enlightened people, we are immune to that). Regardless, those trans dimensional entities shape the Cosmological Consensus (and are also shaped by our own reality due to Quantum Entanglement).<br /> <br /> That is why it would be far better to detach our core dimension from those alternative universes as much as possible, to prevent those weird parallel worlds from distorting the physical laws of our own universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Triat get mentioned with the Mages.<br /> <br /> Entropy, Stasis, and Dynamism are big things in Mage.<br /> <br /> Except in Mage, the mages view the Wyrm as completely sane (despite Nephandi existing--weird) and just another cosmological constant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T06:20:30-07:00","id":1533310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533302#post1533302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Triat get mentioned with the Mages.<br /> <br /> Entropy, Stasis, and Dynamism are big things in Mage.<br /> <br /> Except in Mage, the mages view the Wyrm as completely sane (despite Nephandi existing--weird) and just another cosmological constant.</div> </div> </div> </div>The principles of Entropy, Stasis, and Dynamism are big things in Mage, the personalities of the Wyrm, the Weaver, and the Wyld less so. A small subset of mages share the Werewolf belief in the specific personification of these principles, but most don't. That's true even among the Nephandi. The Malfeans certainly recognize the Wyrm and work with it and its minions. The rest have other masters, or other &quot;masters,&quot; or no masters at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T10:10:58-07:00","id":1533315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533302#post1533302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Triat get mentioned with the Mages.<br /> <br /> Entropy, Stasis, and Dynamism are big things in Mage.<br /> <br /> Except in Mage, the mages view the Wyrm as completely sane (despite Nephandi existing--weird) and just another cosmological constant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entropy, Stasis and Dynamism are not anthropomorphized forces like they are in Werewolf; they are absolutely NOT the same as Wyrm, Weaver and Wyld. Mage's Entropy isn't a 9 headed beast trying to physically devour the Tellurian; Mage's &quot;Triat&quot; is like the force of Gravity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T12:28:08-07:00","id":1533325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533278#post1533278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what I meant by Subjective Reality has to be complicated. And I mean it's complicated in the Facebook Relationship sense.<br /> <br /> There has to be a way that the Traditions can think that they are all doing similar things while preferring their specific paradigms. There needs to be a way for the Technocracy to think that it can alter reality while still thinking it is operating off of consistent (or at least semi consistent) principles.<br /> <br /> That sounds difficult, but it is quite common in our world. There are competing views about physics and metaphysics and theology all the time. Sometimes it is obvious to reasonable onlookers which side is right, other times there are compelling arguments on both sides and it takes years to work through who is right. That's because reality is complicated and it is difficult to take it all in at once. A complicated Subjective Reality would provide enough justification for the competing points of view we see.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean it needs to be complicated for the players. We don't have have to have in depth explanations of the Traditions metaphysical arguments or comprehensive charts of the data the Technocracy has gathered. We can simplify it to a short and quick explanation with and cover the rest with an &quot;It's complicated&quot; disclaimer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having things be complicated is fine; as you said, it is realistic. I just think that having it be a complicated subjective reality is a step too far. All you really need is the basic spine of the Consensus for the magic system to function. Having it be a complicated reality is fine. Whether or not that reality is subjective or not should be up in the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T21:50:24-07:00","id":1533351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533325#post1533325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having things be complicated is fine; as you said, it is realistic. I just think that having it be a complicated subjective reality is a step too far. All you really need is the basic spine of the Consensus for the magic system to function. Having it be a complicated reality is fine. Whether or not that reality is subjective or not should be up in the air.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. For instance, I fully want &quot;da Truth&quot; of Mage to be fully 100% OBJECTIVE. Not that it IS, mind you, but rather that it is POSSIBLE TO BE. Maybe we are all &quot;fragments of God&quot; living in a fully Gnostic world... But maybe the world really is materialistic and fully mechanicist and the universe follows a simple Evolutionary path, and &quot;Da Science&quot; is actually &quot;Da Truth&quot;. And &quot;Consensus&quot; is just some weird trans-dimensional stuff that we don't fully understand... Yet.<br /> <br /> Or maybe not. But I don't want either way to be set on stone, and I want all options to be on the table. And this needs to be made clear, not just &quot;things are like this, but the techies believe that...&quot;. No. No such thing. There must be one section stating &quot;Cosmology under Divine Revelation&quot;, then another segment with &quot;Cosmology under the Scientific Principle&quot; and &quot;Cosmology under Mystical Insight&quot; and so on, each with their own defining &quot;truths&quot; that are absolutely plausible and coherent.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the game mechanics MUST also reflect that. I see many people scoffing at game mechanics having an effect on how the setting and the cosmology of the setting is perceived by players, but the truth is that game mechanics is almost paramount towards how &quot;da Truth&quot; is perceived. That's one of the reasons why I ditch the old 9 spheres completely in favor of custom tailored &quot;Realms&quot; (custom Spheres) to each individual group. While the Hermetics remain pretty adamant on them, they are pretty much the only ones that adhere to that system in my games; that has a unique effect of turning Magik no longer &quot;translatable&quot; towards different groups - just as a small example of how game mechanics directly impact the setting. Also, if for example you have a set of game mechanics for &quot;Divine&quot; or &quot;Shamanic&quot; &quot;Magic&quot; and another for &quot;Wizardry&quot; (Mystical Insight), then they ABSOLUTELY are not mutually communicable - and this is GOOD.<br /> <br /> This is good because, in effect, it would be much like a Mage nowadays trying to replicate a vampiric Discipline; a Hermetic watching a Chorister could replicate the end result, but it would be a completely new &quot;Spell&quot; that is absolutely unrelated to what the Chorister is doing.<br /> <br /> In the end, it could all still be &quot;all the same thing&quot; and it could be the case that it is all just &quot;willworking&quot; - but the belief makes it so that it is impossible to &quot;translate Magik&quot;. Or not, or it could really be the case that each has a different source for their powers (or perhaps the Hermetic thinks he is doing willworking, but he is actually just a vessel for the Divine, or he's a Psyonic, or maybe he's a weak point in the Quantum Fabric of Space and Time... Or any other reason. But he believes he's practicing willworking or instead he's hacking the universal code or something like it).<br /> <br /> All possibilities fully on the table.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T11:00:47-07:00","id":1533382,"title":"","content":"&quot;People actually have different sources for their powers but for simplicity they're represented the same way mechanically&quot; is what I like to think. You have to have Consensus work on it all regardless, but you can account for this by treating Consensus as a magical effect that interacts with magic but doesn't necessarily come from the same source of it. My Etherite PC does her magic by incorporating magical materials into mundane technology and explains away Paradox as the collective psychic field interfering with the magical components, but that doesn't mean she thinks the alloy invented by the superintelligent lemurs of Lemuria was brought into existence through belief.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as far as how I interpret the Traditions, I like a more idealistic take on them. And I like to treat the Etherites (at least some Etherites) as more legitimately scientific than the Technocracy, which ironically means that they're more willing to accept the existence of the supernatural than the Technocracy because they're not willing to invent pseudoscientific technobabble to make something out to sound scientific. My Etherite doesn't truck with any of this dimensional science nonsense because she knows that's not what a dimension is; it is very clearly the spirit world and she may not understand it but she doesn't need to understand how materials harvested from there work so long as they work in somewhat predictable ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","user":"Citrakayah","date":". 03-30-2024, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T11:05:18-07:00","id":1533383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533382#post1533382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;People actually have different sources for their powers but for simplicity they're represented the same way mechanically&quot; is what I like to think. You have to have Consensus work on it all regardless, but you can account for this by treating Consensus as a magical effect that interacts with magic but doesn't necessarily come from the same source of it. My Etherite PC does her magic by incorporating magical materials into mundane technology and explains away Paradox as the collective psychic field interfering with the magical components, but that doesn't mean she thinks the alloy invented by the superintelligent lemurs of Lemuria was brought into existence through belief.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really?<br /> <br /> Because that seems really....well, problematic. It says that, &quot;Oh yes, White People magic is fundamentally different from Brown People Magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> For me, it should be a game about putting aside differences.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy must be destroyed not because of it's evil, though it has plenty of that, but because it cannot exist with any other paradigms. It is not the enemy of the Traditions.<br /> <br /> It is the enemy of humanity.<br /> <br /> All worlds where there's one paradigm is as bad as the Nephandi because that's not how humanity works. No single paradigm cannot be anything other than nightmarish horrific oppression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-30-2024, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T11:13:56-07:00","id":1533384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533383#post1533383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really?<br /> <br /> Because that seems really....well, problematic. It says that, &quot;Oh yes, White People magic is fundamentally different from Brown People Magic.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think that a black person and a white person can't share the same paradigm? This doesn't say that the power source is dependent on ethnicity, it says it's dependent on paradigm. It's true that to some degree paradigm overlaps with culture and culture overlaps with ethnicity, but: The model of reality the purple paradigm uses is called chaos magic and was invented in England in the 1970s. You want to avoid a world where there's a single paradigm, my take is what you want and you can't actually set aside differences--because if you do, there is only one paradigm, it's just masking itself as inclusive when in reality it is assimilative.<br /> <br /> It's way less problematic to just treat other people's viewpoints as accurate (if not sufficient to explain the sum total of reality). This is just such a weird take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","user":"Citrakayah","date":". 03-30-2024, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T14:34:50-07:00","id":1533394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533384#post1533384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that a black person and a white person can't share the same paradigm? This doesn't say that the power source is dependent on ethnicity, it says it's dependent on paradigm. It's true that to some degree paradigm overlaps with culture and culture overlaps with ethnicity, but: The model of reality the purple paradigm uses is called chaos magic and was invented in England in the 1970s. You want to avoid a world where there's a single paradigm, my take is what you want and you can't actually set aside differences--because if you do, there is only one paradigm, it's just masking itself as inclusive when in reality it is assimilative.<br /> <br /> It's way less problematic to just treat other people's viewpoints as accurate (if not sufficient to explain the sum total of reality). This is just such a weird take.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, when you start with your position as, &quot;fundamentally people from different backgrounds are utterly irreconcilable and operate due to different laws of physics&quot; then you run right into the same issue of Kindred of the East where in an attempt to make the setting more varied and incorporate more cultures than just Western takes, you actually become exclusionist and hostile.<br /> <br /> It also runs into the wall that Mage isn't the Real WorldTM but creating a shared system of fiction to indulge in.<br /> <br /> As for 'White people and Brown people can believe in the same thing', part of the issue is that so much of each Tradition is linked heavily to RL cultural heritage and separating it like they're trying to do with Werewolf seems like a much bigger issue.<br /> <br /> Not saying you're wrong but I sometimes wonder if it wouldn't have been better if Mage had started more with, &quot;Magic is powered by a wholly non-real thing we made up for the game and is unrelated to RL magical practices save as people choose to practice them as their personal religion/identity. Which is to say a Wiccan doesn't get magick from their faith but may be a Wiccan and mage. Same as a Son of Ether and science.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T15:00:24-07:00","id":1533395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533394#post1533394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, when you start with your position as, &quot;fundamentally people from different backgrounds are utterly irreconcilable and operate due to different laws of physics&quot; then you run right into the same issue of Kindred of the East where in an attempt to make the setting more varied and incorporate more cultures than just Western takes, you actually become exclusionist and hostile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kindred of the East said that there was something <i>inherent</i> about people of Asian descent that made them rise as a specific kind of vampire which was not present anywhere else, they collapsed the cultural diversity of all of Asia into &quot;hey they're the same Asian vampire, amirite?,&quot; they gave them a nonsense name, they had everywhere <i>but</i> Asia use the same vampires regardless of local culture, I could go on; Kindred of the East's problem was not actually, &quot;There's more than just Western vampires out there.&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533394#post1533394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also runs into the wall that Mage isn't the Real WorldTM but creating a shared system of fiction to indulge in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage is urban fantasy; it is about our world just with the supernatural thrown in.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533394#post1533394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not saying you're wrong but I sometimes wonder if it wouldn't have been better if Mage had started more with, &quot;Magic is powered by a wholly non-real thing we made up for the game and is unrelated to RL magical practices save as people choose to practice them as their personal religion/identity. Which is to say a Wiccan doesn't get magick from their faith but may be a Wiccan and mage. Same as a Son of Ether and science.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Practically this sort of thing doesn't work out. I challenge you to give <i>one</i> example from fiction of a magic system that had no relation to anything that existed in real life. While I think it's theoretically possible to do, almost any time people try to do this they just end up going for the blandest tropes common to their culture and assuming they're the default.<br /> <br /> Please don't try to erase including other cultures in media and justify it as somehow woke. It's not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T20:05:46-07:00","id":1533402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533382#post1533382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;People actually have different sources for their powers but for simplicity they're represented the same way mechanically&quot; is what I like to think. You have to have Consensus work on it all regardless, but you can account for this by treating Consensus as a magical effect that interacts with magic but doesn't necessarily come from the same source of it. My Etherite PC does her magic by incorporating magical materials into mundane technology and explains away Paradox as the collective psychic field interfering with the magical components, but that doesn't mean she thinks the alloy invented by the superintelligent lemurs of Lemuria was brought into existence through belief.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as far as how I interpret the Traditions, I like a more idealistic take on them. And I like to treat the Etherites (at least some Etherites) as more legitimately scientific than the Technocracy, which ironically means that they're more willing to accept the existence of the supernatural than the Technocracy because they're not willing to invent pseudoscientific technobabble to make something out to sound scientific. My Etherite doesn't truck with any of this dimensional science nonsense because she knows that's not what a dimension is; it is very clearly the spirit world and she may not understand it but she doesn't need to understand how materials harvested from there work so long as they work in somewhat predictable ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing thou, &quot;Spirits&quot; may just as well be beings from other dimensions operating under different laws. It may not just be pure &quot;technobabble&quot;, and the Technocracy may indeed be right.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that they are thou, there's a difference. I'm saying that they may be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T20:22:42-07:00","id":1533403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533383#post1533383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really?<br /> <br /> Because that seems really....well, problematic. It says that, &quot;Oh yes, White People magic is fundamentally different from Brown People Magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> For me, it should be a game about putting aside differences.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy must be destroyed not because of it's evil, though it has plenty of that, but because it cannot exist with any other paradigms. It is not the enemy of the Traditions.<br /> <br /> It is the enemy of humanity.<br /> <br /> All worlds where there's one paradigm is as bad as the Nephandi because that's not how humanity works. No single paradigm cannot be anything other than nightmarish horrific oppression.</div> </div> </div> </div>Errr.... What?<br /> <br /> A game about... Putting aside the differences?<br /> <br /> This is the Ascension WAR. And do you know what War means?<br /> <br /> It means:<br /> <br /> W e<br /> A re<br /> R ight<br /> <br /> Mage is absolutely NOT a game of shiny people holding hands.<br /> <br /> I keep repeating myself, but Mage is a game about pretentious elitists living in Ivory Towers (sometimes literally) who believes that they know better about what's best for everybody else. This is a game of essentially tribal conflict, upon which if you're not from my tribe you're an enemy to be purged and there's no compromise.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is simply the biggest, strongest and most aggressive of all these tribes. But essentially, they are all the same. Again, the so called Traditions were happily slaughtering each other for the exact same reason as the techies did it to the rest: because they could not accept the different.<br /> <br /> It's a very good portrait of human history actually; this grand project that we call &quot;civilization&quot; was built upon the bones of conquered people. Over the entire human history (and pre historic period too), you were either a fellow tribesman or you are to be slaughtered or enslaved. That's actually the law of Nature. Just watch a band of gorillas slaughtering a weaker band and you'll see, or how a lion kills the other to take his territory.<br /> <br /> We are living in an atypical era were we have those rather silly dreams about &quot;world peace&quot; and that we will all live happily ever after united in peace, but then you look at China, Russia, Iran and North Korea to dispel those illusions.<br /> <br /> Mage is a game upon which the differences are the main cause of a bloody and unforgiven shadow war, and the prize is the ultimate control of reality. There's no &quot;putting aside differences&quot;. Even the Traditions do NOT do that, they instead created their own thing upon which they can achieve some sort of unity and create a &quot;bigger tribe&quot; for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T20:30:20-07:00","id":1533404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533402#post1533402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the thing thou, &quot;Spirits&quot; may just as well be beings from other dimensions operating under different laws. It may not just be pure &quot;technobabble&quot;, and the Technocracy may indeed be right.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that they are thou, there's a difference. I'm saying that they may be.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Dimensions&quot; are things like length, width, depth, and time which can be expressed as measurable quantities. &quot;Another dimension,&quot; in physical terms, is basically gibberish. Yes, I am doing the 'physicist complaining about Star Trek' thing despite not actually being a physicist, but the entire schtick of the Technocracy is that they claim to be scientific and it's very clear to anyone who knows about the subjects the Technocracy speaks about that they are <i>not</i>. Plus, even if spirits were just &quot;aliens from other universes,&quot; that wouldn't explain why they don't follow this universe's laws when appearing here, why their universe is so similar to ours, and why they're metaphysically linked to phenomena in our universe.<br /> <br /> It is simply more logical to consider them spirits than consider them aliens. Occam's Razor and all.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533403#post1533403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep repeating myself, but Mage is a game about pretentious elitists living in Ivory Towers (sometimes literally) who believes that they know better about what's best for everybody else. This is a game of essentially tribal conflict, upon which if you're not from my tribe you're an enemy to be purged and there's no compromise.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is simply the biggest, strongest and most aggressive of all these tribes. But essentially, they are all the same. Again, the so called Traditions were happily slaughtering each other for the exact same reason as the techies did it to the rest: because they could not accept the different.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a pretty inaccurate assessment of the Traditions, which didn't always get along with each other but were largely uninterested in purging each other from existence. Your description of human history is similarly bullshit. I would suggest that you actually talk to historians and crack open a few text books rather than... I'm genuinely not sure where you would have gotten that bullshit from. YouTube? Genocide has been the exception rather than the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","user":"Citrakayah","date":". 03-30-2024, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T20:43:03-07:00","id":1533406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533394#post1533394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, when you start with your position as, &quot;fundamentally people from different backgrounds are utterly irreconcilable and operate due to different laws of physics&quot; then you run right into the same issue of Kindred of the East where in an attempt to make the setting more varied and incorporate more cultures than just Western takes, you actually become exclusionist and hostile.<br /> <br /> It also runs into the wall that Mage isn't the Real WorldTM but creating a shared system of fiction to indulge in.<br /> <br /> As for 'White people and Brown people can believe in the same thing', part of the issue is that so much of each Tradition is linked heavily to RL cultural heritage and separating it like they're trying to do with Werewolf seems like a much bigger issue.<br /> <br /> Not saying you're wrong but I sometimes wonder if it wouldn't have been better if Mage had started more with, &quot;Magic is powered by a wholly non-real thing we made up for the game and is unrelated to RL magical practices save as people choose to practice them as their personal religion/identity. Which is to say a Wiccan doesn't get magick from their faith but may be a Wiccan and mage. Same as a Son of Ether and science.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The way Mage was supposed to work was like that. Are you a Shaman? Ok, your powers come from Spirits or from &quot;Spirit Energy&quot; or whatever. Are you a Gnostic Theosophical Chorister? Yeah, you actually ARE God. Ate you a Catholic priest? Then you're blessed by God (or by the Devil). And so on.<br /> <br /> OR NOT.<br /> <br /> This was supposed to be in the open and undefined: yes, this world MAY have Psyonics whose powers come EXCLUSIVELY from their minds, or perhaps &quot;Da Science&quot; is the ultimate truth. Or maybe it's all &quot;Willworking&quot;. Or maybe some do Willworking, some are blessed/cursed by the Devil and some are psyonic mutants. Or they are all self deluded psyonic mutants.<br /> <br /> And of the above (are more) are possible.<br /> <br /> But then the game added mechanics for Avatars and past lives and some other stuff, basically setting on stone that the Hermetics are basically right and all the rest are just self deluded idiots. That's the problem. And there's no amount of technobabble thrown in any number of guides to the Technocracy that can undo that.<br /> <br /> That's why I say that there should be an specific section exclusively about Paradigm, and one that doesn't say &quot;your Magik operates according to your Paradigm&quot;, and much less saying that Techies can never let go of their Instruments &quot;because of Paradigm&quot;. No. It should just describe what each ideology believes, what is their &quot;Truth&quot; and how the universe operates under said Truth. And that Technocrats can never abandon their Instruments because what they do is ACTUALLY SCIENCE. And it should be adamant about what Choristers do is NOT &quot;Magik&quot;, but just &quot;Divine Will&quot;. Then in the section about &quot;Mystical Insight&quot;, you can have a Hermetic master calling them all fools for doing &quot;Willworking&quot; without knowing it, but then in the &quot;Divine Revelation&quot; section, the Chorister master claims that Hermetics are fools for not recognizing that they have being &quot;chosen by a Higher Power&quot;, and so on. The several different and conflicting &quot;Truths&quot; should be exposed to the players, without any being given preferential treatment, and with each one trying to disprove the others, and then the players should decide which path to follow. And &quot;Magik&quot; should be a word used exclusively by groups that adhere to Mystical Insight Paradigms.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T21:08:32-07:00","id":1533407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533406#post1533406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way Mage was supposed to work was like that. Are you a Shaman? Ok, your powers come from Spirits or from &quot;Spirit Energy&quot; or whatever. Are you a Gnostic Theosophical Chorister? Yeah, you actually ARE God. Ate you a Catholic priest? Then you're blessed by God (or by the Devil). And so on.<br /> <br /> OR NOT.<br /> <br /> This was supposed to be in the open and undefined: yes, this world MAY have Psyonics whose powers come EXCLUSIVELY from their minds, or perhaps &quot;Da Science&quot; is the ultimate truth. Or maybe it's all &quot;Willworking&quot;. Or maybe some do Willworking, some are blessed/cursed by the Devil and some are psyonic mutants. Or they are all self deluded psyonic mutants.<br /> <br /> And of the above (are more) are possible.<br /> <br /> But then the game added mechanics for Avatars and past lives and some other stuff, basically setting on stone that the Hermetics are basically right and all the rest are just self deluded idiots. That's the problem. And there's no amount of technobabble thrown in any number of guides to the Technocracy that can undo that.<br /> <br /> That's why I say that there should be an specific section exclusively about Paradigm, and one that doesn't say &quot;your Magik operates according to your Paradigm&quot;, and much less saying that Techies can never let go of their Instruments &quot;because of Paradigm&quot;. No. It should just describe what each ideology believes, what is their &quot;Truth&quot; and how the universe operates under said Truth. And that Technocrats can never abandon their Instruments because what they do is ACTUALLY SCIENCE. And it should be adamant about what Choristers do is NOT &quot;Magik&quot;, but just &quot;Divine Will&quot;. Then in the section about &quot;Mystical Insight&quot;, you can have a Hermetic master calling them all fools for doing &quot;Willworking&quot; without knowing it, but then in the &quot;Divine Revelation&quot; section, the Chorister master claims that Hermetics are fools for not recognizing that they have being &quot;chosen by a Higher Power&quot;, and so on. The several different and conflicting &quot;Truths&quot; should be exposed to the players, without any being given preferential treatment, and with each one trying to disprove the others, and then the players should decide which path to follow. And &quot;Magik&quot; should be a word used exclusively by groups that adhere to Mystical Insight Paradigms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Because I thought the whole &quot;Mages don't know it's all Willworking&quot; was added in subsequent editions and REALLY confused what the Hell people were talking about. The Traditions don't have a coherent philosophy if they're not all on the same page.<br /> <br /> &quot;It doesn't matter if you use A, B, or C since we're all the same. The important thing is our freedom to choose to do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533403#post1533403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Errr.... What?<br /> <br /> A game about... Putting aside the differences?<br /> <br /> This is the Ascension WAR. And do you know what War means?<br /> <br /> It means:<br /> <br /> W e<br /> A re<br /> R ight<br /> <br /> Mage is absolutely NOT a game of shiny people holding hands.<br /> <br /> I keep repeating myself, but Mage is a game about pretentious elitists living in Ivory Towers (sometimes literally) who believes that they know better about what's best for everybody else. This is a game of essentially tribal conflict, upon which if you're not from my tribe you're an enemy to be purged and there's no compromise.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is simply the biggest, strongest and most aggressive of all these tribes. But essentially, they are all the same. Again, the so called Traditions were happily slaughtering each other for the exact same reason as the techies did it to the rest: because they could not accept the different.<br /> <br /> It's a very good portrait of human history actually; this grand project that we call &quot;civilization&quot; was built upon the bones of conquered people. Over the entire human history (and pre historic period too), you were either a fellow tribesman or you are to be slaughtered or enslaved. That's actually the law of Nature. Just watch a band of gorillas slaughtering a weaker band and you'll see, or how a lion kills the other to take his territory.<br /> <br /> We are living in an atypical era were we have those rather silly dreams about &quot;world peace&quot; and that we will all live happily ever after united in peace, but then you look at China, Russia, Iran and North Korea to dispel those illusions.<br /> <br /> Mage is a game upon which the differences are the main cause of a bloody and unforgiven shadow war, and the prize is the ultimate control of reality. There's no &quot;putting aside differences&quot;. Even the Traditions do NOT do that, they instead created their own thing upon which they can achieve some sort of unity and create a &quot;bigger tribe&quot; for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, if you want to make the Technocracy the good guys yeah.<br /> <br /> But the Technocracy has a pogrom and the genocide of all supernaturals as their goal.<br /> <br /> And the Traditions has peaceful coexistence with science and magic as theirs.<br /> <br /> And uh....interesting interpretation of history given that almost all of human history is basically, &quot;War, eventual coexistence because people don't end up going away.&quot;<br /> <br /> The funny thing about Egypt? It's still there, conquered by Greeks or Hysokas or Romans.<br /> <br /> The great lesson of Genghis Khan's Empire was, &quot;Yeah, we eventually became Chinese.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is not usually the one taught by the Enlightenment trying to justify colonialism for obvious reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-31-2024, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T21:14:12-07:00","id":1533408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533395#post1533395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred of the East said that there was something <i>inherent</i> about people of Asian descent that made them rise as a specific kind of vampire which was not present anywhere else, they collapsed the cultural diversity of all of Asia into &quot;hey they're the same Asian vampire, amirite?,&quot; they gave them a nonsense name, they had everywhere <i>but</i> Asia use the same vampires regardless of local culture, I could go on; Kindred of the East's problem was not actually, &quot;There's more than just Western vampires out there.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mage is urban fantasy; it is about our world just with the supernatural thrown in.<br /> <br /> Practically this sort of thing doesn't work out. I challenge you to give <i>one</i> example from fiction of a magic system that had no relation to anything that existed in real life. While I think it's theoretically possible to do, almost any time people try to do this they just end up going for the blandest tropes common to their culture and assuming they're the default.<br /> <br /> Please don't try to erase including other cultures in media and justify it as somehow woke. It's not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point.<br /> <br /> It may have been an impossible task making a magic system for everyone that doesn't favor one sort or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T21:14:12-07:00","id":1533409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533404#post1533404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a pretty inaccurate assessment of the Traditions, which didn't always get along with each other but were largely uninterested in purging each other from existence. Your description of human history is similarly bullshit. I would suggest that you actually talk to historians and crack open a few text books rather than... I'm genuinely not sure where you would have gotten that bullshit from. YouTube? Genocide has been the exception rather than the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Well, I'm glad to know. Quick question thou: what happened to the ancient Egyptians? Ancient Persians?<br /> <br /> How exactly do you think that empires are formed?<br /> <br /> Ever heard about the word &quot;russification&quot;? Yeah, we are hearing a lot about that lately, but the truth is that that's not an exclusively feature of mother Russia.<br /> <br /> Were are the European pagans? Were are the Arabic pagans that worshipped the Moon God? <br /> <br /> Do you know that the UN defines &quot;genocide&quot; not only as the physical extermination of a people, but also as forced cultural assimilation, right?<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bHow exactly do you think that the Han ethnicity became 90% of the people of the most populous nation on Earth? Do you think that they simply birthed faster than all of the other tribes surrounding them?<br /> <br /> Were are the Gauls of France? The Picts of England? The Ainu of Japan?<br /> <br /> Did you know that Genghis Khan's expansion alone killed 10% of the total human population of the world at the time?<br /> <br /> Tell me, what happened when a Viking incursion reached a Monastery in Europe?<br /> <br /> I don't know what kind of history books you have being reading, but the ones I know aren't about the history of the unicorns.<br /> <br /> Did you also know that, according to archeological evidence, when humanity discovered/invented farming around 10.000 years ago, the life expectancy of all humans dropped by 10 years, and that the main cause of deaths at that period became due to VIOLENT CONFLICTS? Because, as soon as we went from nomadic hunter-gatherers to sedentary or semi-sedentary farmers, we started to gather around villages, and those were ripe for the taking for other groups to steal their food (and possibly, their women too).<br /> <br /> Do you even know what happens during a war? We have all these fancy &quot;rules of engagement&quot; in the West, but just go to Ukraine and you'll see what REAL WAR means.<br /> <br /> Real war means that your children are not safe, and your mother, daughter, sisters, they may all end up raped and either killed or turned into sex slaves. And the males may be killed or turned into slaves. That's what has happened throughout the entire human history.<br /> <br /> A quick question: do you know how many genocides &quot;Alexander the Great&quot; perpetrated? You do know that he didn't just &quot;conquered&quot; the Greeks, but that in fact several city-states that resisted, he burned them to the ground and slaughtered them all. You did know that, right?<br /> <br /> Do you know how many genocides Julius Caesar perpetrated?<br /> <br /> Do you know how many genocides the first emperor of China perpetrated in order to &quot;Unify&quot; China?<br /> <br /> Do you know how many genocides happened time and time again whenever a Daimyo in Japan waged war against another?<br /> <br /> Did you know that, there was an Emperor in China that proclaimed himself as the Second Coming of Christ, and hundreds of millions of Chinese died in the following civil war?<br /> <br /> By the way, every time China collapses, hundreds of millions die in civil wars.<br /> <br /> Did you know that, during the 3 centuries of Islamic expansion over India, 300 MILLIONS of Indians were slaughtered by the Muslims?<br /> <br /> Speaking of India, do you how how many Kingdoms were erased from the Earth over its long history?<br /> <br /> How many millions have the Aztecs ripped the hearts of at the top of their pyramids over the centuries? Do you know?<br /> <br /> We certainly don't read the same history books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T21:53:22-07:00","id":1533411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533407#post1533407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? Because I thought the whole &quot;Mages don't know it's all Willworking&quot; was added in subsequent editions and REALLY confused what the Hell people were talking about. The Traditions don't have a coherent philosophy if they're not all on the same page.<br /> <br /> &quot;It doesn't matter if you use A, B, or C since we're all the same. The important thing is our freedom to choose to do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, if you want to make the Technocracy the good guys yeah.<br /> <br /> But the Technocracy has a pogrom and the genocide of all supernaturals as their goal.<br /> <br /> And the Traditions has peaceful coexistence with science and magic as theirs.<br /> <br /> And uh....interesting interpretation of history given that almost all of human history is basically, &quot;War, eventual coexistence because people don't end up going away.&quot;<br /> <br /> The funny thing about Egypt? It's still there, conquered by Greeks or Hysokas or Romans.<br /> <br /> The great lesson of Genghis Khan's Empire was, &quot;Yeah, we eventually became Chinese.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is not usually the one taught by the Enlightenment trying to justify colonialism for obvious reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Try telling to a Ukrainian that they can cohexist with the Russians... As long as they speak Russian and bow to Tzar Putin.<br /> <br /> That's the thing, when we think about &quot;genocide&quot; we automatically think about the gas chambers in Auschwitz, but that's just the most extreme version of it and it's not what encompass the entire definition of it.<br /> <br /> For instance, China is placing the Muslim Uyghurs in concentration camps, but they aren't physically eliminating them... Well, not all of them. Instead, they are &quot;re-educating&quot; them into &quot;how to be a good Chinese&quot;. That's genocide.<br /> <br /> Go ask a Finn about what their history books teach regarding the many several Russian invasions, begining in the 19 century when the Tzar decided that being a faithful subject was not enough, you had to be &quot;Russian&quot;. Let's see what they tell you.<br /> <br /> Sure, &quot;people don't go away&quot;. Which is why everything related to the culture of the Gauls is the stuff of history books. Once they got conquered by the Romans under Julius Caesar, around 2 millions were slaughtered in the &quot;conquest&quot;, a few millions more were sold as slaves to the Romans (and their women turned into sex slaves), and the rest were forced to worship the Roman Gods and speak Latin.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Egyptians&quot; of today are NOT the ancient Egyptians. They are ARABS. They are culturally as related to the ancient Egyptians as you and me both are culturally related to the Zulus.<br /> <br /> The Iranians of today are genetically descendants of the ancient Persians, but everything about the Persian culture has being lost ever since they were conquered by the Caliphate.<br /> <br /> Imagine if you, as a westerner like me, got invaded by China, forced to speak Chinese and eat as they eat and think as they think (or else). Imagine being forced to worship Xi Jinping as the &quot;Big Brother&quot; and to only ever open your mouth to talk about the government to give praises - since we love to trash our governments. That's basically what every single conquered people ever had to endure, and that when they were &quot;lucky&quot; enough to not being killed or enslaved.<br /> <br /> Go ask any Irish about how much they have always loved their &quot;cohexistance&quot; with the Brits, that should be a funny exercise. And hey, let's not forget, the Irish were forced to forgo their ancient Celtic languages and adopt English too. And even today, as English speakers and as an independent and prosperous nation, go ask an Irish how much their people loved being enslaved and subjugated by the Brits.<br /> <br /> Or ask a Pole how fun their history has been for the last 4 centuries. What a great time they have been having by been &quot;cohexisting&quot; sometimes with the Germans and sometimes with the Russians.<br /> <br /> Or ask a Korean about how much fun they have been having &quot;cohexisting&quot; with both the Chinese and the Japanese for the last 1.000 years.<br /> <br /> Or ask a Kurd TODAY how much fun they are having by &quot;cohexisting&quot; as a second class subjugated people under the Turk fist. Or how the Armenians, Greeks, Serbs and Arabs loved to &quot;cohexist&quot; for the last 4 to 6 centuries with the Ottomans.<br /> <br /> I won't even mention the native Americans in this because that would be a low blown, but since I'm Brazilian I pretty much have to, specially because one of our neighbors is Paraguay, and in there, half of their population still speaks the native language of Tupi-Guarani. Pretty much every where else, they were forced to speak Spanish (or Portuguese in here). That must have been a fun &quot;cohexistence&quot;, if by &quot;cohexistence&quot; you mean working to death into the silver mines.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the natives, did you know that, when the Portuguese got into Brazil, they got embroiled into the middle of a war of extermination between the Tupi-Guaranis and the Tupinambas? Yeah, the Tupi-Guaranis group, coming from the north, had been exterminating the Tupinambas for over 4 centuries previous to the Portuguese arrival. In fact, the natives would come to the Portuguese, French and Dutch to form alliances, in the hopes to use the Europeans in THEIR wars against each other over here. When the Portuguese arrived, the Tupi-Guaranis had already removed the Tupinambas from over 60% of the territory. Something like that.<br /> <br /> And, Cortez only managed to destroy the Aztecs because he amassed an army of 50.000 natives who HATED the Aztecs (and after centuries of wars to capture slaves to be sacrificed, I can't blamed them). So, actually, it were other natives that destroyed the Aztecs, under the leadership of Cortez.<br /> <br /> Anyway. Sure, &quot;assimilation&quot; happens. Sometimes, it's even pacific, or not as bloody.<br /> <br /> Most of the times thou, &quot;assimilation&quot; happens at the tip of the spear. It's &quot;convert or else&quot;. That has always been the norm. For instance, the Vikings decided to convert to Christianity. Just like the Indonesians converted to Islam.<br /> <br /> But the Persians, Egyptians, North Africans and all the way into the Indian sub continent, were forced to convert to Islam, after countless cases of mass slaughters and mass enslavement. Just like the natives in the Americas were forced into Christianism. In Africa, the big African empires had their foundations based on the subjugation of weaker peoples and their mass enslavement.<br /> <br /> Like I said, when we invented agriculture 10.000 years ago, we begun to slaughter each other at unprecedented rates.<br /> <br /> Until 1945, humanity lived in a world of &quot;might makes right&quot; and that's it.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, we live in an atypical era brought by the &quot;Pax Americana&quot; and because of that we have those strange ideas of &quot;world peace&quot; that simply are disconnected from the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T06:14:22-07:00","id":1533414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533409#post1533409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly do you think that empires are formed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Violent conquest, obviously, but honestly you're shooting your own argument in the foot here because the historic norm for empires was to try and extract wealth from the periphery and direct it to the core without really bothering about forcing cultural assimilation--forcing cultural assimilation provokes unrest and requires you to completely restructure the society, and it is simply easier to co-opt the local power structure and have them send resources to the metropole. Empires are fundamentally lazy. And obviously you don't want to exterminate the entire population of a conquered area if you're an empire because you need them to extract wealth. Empires still did genocide but it wasn't the <i>norm</i> and this notion of eternal conflict of your kin group versus all others is simply bullshit; citing a bunch of anecdotes (some of which are wrong; the Triple Alliance didn't embark on wars to capture sacrifices; that was internal propaganda for why they couldn't subdue the Tlaxcala easily; in reality they wanted to expand their tributaries) won't really help you.<br /> <br /> And to bring this back to Mage, it's why the Technocracy is kind of bizarre historically; most groups don't have any interest in forcing everyone to adhere to a single orthodoxy. Even if you had a Traditions wizard-king (and you did not), do you think he cares if the peasants do Verbenae healing rituals? No, because he's not in it for the peasants believing the Hermetic paradigm, he's in it to <i>get paid</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","user":"Citrakayah","date":". 03-31-2024, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T08:55:56-07:00","id":1533419,"title":"","content":"Empires often exemplify the slogan &quot;Nothing succeeds like success.&quot; European intellectuals have long loathed the USA because it has been successful. Because we've had a two hundred and forty some year run of democracy (with the trend being towards greater inclusion over the long duree), we make non democratic seem burdensome (non democratic systems are burdens, but America's flawed democracy make that to obvious to hide). Because of our prosperity, America is accused of encouraging materialism and consumerism. Because America strongly values individual freedom and fulfillment, we are blamed for individualism and a lack of willingness by the masses to sacrifice their lives for the goals and dreams of the elites.<br /> <br /> Much of this is silly. People would kick back against being used anyway. But America, flaws and all, makes it obviously the way to go. I reject the notion that America is an Empire in any but an esoteric &quot;dammed if you do, dammed if you don't&quot; way. But like a successful Empire, America's &quot;success&quot; breeds both imitators and converts. This wildly embitters European intellectuals and their wannabes.<br /> <br /> If you are offering hard tack and water of dubious cleanliness at a high price, and I come by with luscious burgers, fries, and sodas, clean, fresh, and cheap, I'm likely to put you out of business. You might resent this.<br /> <br /> If your culture places many burdens on the young, especially young women, and a few days travel away is a different culture your young people can join, which offers far better opportunities for far less sacrifice, you might find your young people leaving for greener pastures. In present day India, many small scale societies, that have endured since before Summer and Ur, are fading away. Falling apart as their young people leave for a solid chance at a better life. Bizarre as it may seem America, which has never had any power in India, is accused of IMPERIALISM because of this. But it's simply people chasing a better opportunity.<br /> <br /> Once, long ago, the Technocrats offered a better tomorrow and a better today as well. They still think they do. The Desparates don't understand that they (in most cases) offer nothing. The Trads, flawed as they are, do still offer something. This will be called Empire whether or not that makes any sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 03-31-2024, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T09:36:32-07:00","id":1533420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533414#post1533414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Violent conquest, obviously, but honestly you're shooting your own argument in the foot here because the historic norm for empires was to try and extract wealth from the periphery and direct it to the core without really bothering about forcing cultural assimilation--forcing cultural assimilation provokes unrest and requires you to completely restructure the society, and it is simply easier to co-opt the local power structure and have them send resources to the metropole. Empires are fundamentally lazy. And obviously you don't want to exterminate the entire population of a conquered area if you're an empire because you need them to extract wealth. Empires still did genocide but it wasn't the <i>norm</i> and this notion of eternal conflict of your kin group versus all others is simply bullshit; citing a bunch of anecdotes (some of which are wrong; the Triple Alliance didn't embark on wars to capture sacrifices; that was internal propaganda for why they couldn't subdue the Tlaxcala easily; in reality they wanted to expand their tributaries) won't really help you.<br /> <br /> And to bring this back to Mage, it's why the Technocracy is kind of bizarre historically; most groups don't have any interest in forcing everyone to adhere to a single orthodoxy. Even if you had a Traditions wizard-king (and you did not), do you think he cares if the peasants do Verbenae healing rituals? No, because he's not in it for the peasants believing the Hermetic paradigm, he's in it to <i>get paid</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Technocracy is a fictional entity. Other than that, Mages as people aren't after the logical things that nations are after, meaning wealth and power. So, they don't operate under normal conditions of &quot;international relations&quot; that the ruling bodies of nations work under. What they are after is the ultimate control of reality, upon which it does make sense to go after the complete extermination of all opposition, since anything less means they can't accomplish their goal.<br /> <br /> About the Empires yes, the idea was to extract wealth from the periphery to the core. Empires were also always and all of them built on slavery. Every single one without exceptions. What most empires did however was a sort of &quot;divide and conquer&quot; option. Ally with some &quot;tribes&quot; (smaller nations, sometimes even on the tribal level) and use those to defeat the stronger ones, turning the &quot;allies&quot; into &quot;vassals&quot; (tributaries) and the defeated enemies into slaves (effective genocide). That's what Julius Caesar did with the Gauls for example, that's what the Spaniards did with the natives and many other countless examples. Greeks, Persians, Egyptians, every single Empire ever did this. And all of them had countless slaves. Sometimes, the slaves would be their own people too. But every single human group practiced slavery throughout the entire human history","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T10:25:05-07:00","id":1533421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533420#post1533420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Technocracy is a fictional entity. Other than that, Mages as people aren't after the logical things that nations are after, meaning wealth and power. So, they don't operate under normal conditions of &quot;international relations&quot; that the ruling bodies of nations work under. What they are after is the ultimate control of reality, upon which it does make sense to go after the complete extermination of all opposition, since anything less means they can't accomplish their goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>This presumes that all mage factions believe in Consensus Reality (they <i>don't</i>) and that those who do want ultimate control of reality... which I don't think they all do. Ultimately they don't really <i>need</i> it, after all; Horizon shows that it's possible to create a place where all paradigms function. The Traditions are a stable alliance that's lasted centuries despite having differing paradigms and the Disparate Alliance is a ton of Crafts which have banded together as well. The Traditions <i>did</i> manage to accept each other, and can even accept Technocratic defectors so long as they don't try to murder everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T12:30:51-07:00","id":1533427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533395#post1533395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindred of the East said that there was something <i>inherent</i> about people of Asian descent that made them rise as a specific kind of vampire which was not present anywhere else, they collapsed the cultural diversity of all of Asia into &quot;hey they're the same Asian vampire, amirite?,&quot; they gave them a nonsense name, they had everywhere <i>but</i> Asia use the same vampires regardless of local culture, I could go on; Kindred of the East's problem was not actually, &quot;There's more than just Western vampires out there.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mage is urban fantasy; it is about our world just with the supernatural thrown in.<br /> <br /> Practically this sort of thing doesn't work out. I challenge you to give <i>one</i> example from fiction of a magic system that had no relation to anything that existed in real life. While I think it's theoretically possible to do, almost any time people try to do this they just end up going for the blandest tropes common to their culture and assuming they're the default.<br /> <br /> Please don't try to erase including other cultures in media and justify it as somehow woke. It's not.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mage books never described the game as urban fantasy. Furthermore, urban fantasy is not about our world with supernatural elements thrown in; it is about our world with fantastical elements thrown in. The presentation is what matters. A book with supernatural elements can be mundane realism.<br /> <br /> Other than that, though, you are pretty much spot on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T14:58:04-07:00","id":1533432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533403#post1533403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A game about... Putting aside the differences?</div> </div> </div> </div>It absolutely can be. I know as I wrote and developed sections of M20 books that suggest that very thing. It's not the default, and it damn sure ain't easy, but it is one possible way to run Mage, absolutely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533403#post1533403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I keep repeating myself, but Mage is a game about pretentious elitists living in Ivory Towers (sometimes literally) who believes that they know better about what's best for everybody else. This is a game of essentially tribal conflict, upon which if you're not from my tribe you're an enemy to be purged and there's no compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can also be that, sure. And this view is given the preponderance of the word count (especially pre-M20)<br /> <br /> But Mage is about a *lot* of things, and trying to pigeonhole it into simply being about bloodthirsty hubris-ridden power mongers misses a whole lot of the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533403#post1533403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a very good portrait of human history actually; this grand project that we call &quot;civilization&quot; was built upon the bones of conquered people. Over the entire human history (and pre historic period too), you were either a fellow tribesman or you are to be slaughtered or enslaved. That's actually the law of Nature. Just watch a band of gorillas slaughtering a weaker band and you'll see, or how a lion kills the other to take his territory.<br /> <br /> We are living in an atypical era were we have those rather silly dreams about &quot;world peace&quot; and that we will all live happily ever after united in peace, but then you look at China, Russia, Iran and North Korea to dispel those illusions.<br /> <br /> Mage is a game upon which the differences are the main cause of a bloody and unforgiven shadow war, and the prize is the ultimate control of reality. There's no &quot;putting aside differences&quot;. Even the Traditions do NOT do that, they instead created their own thing upon which they can achieve some sort of unity and create a &quot;bigger tribe&quot; for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the words in the game don't always bear this out. And yes, we know humanity is (and has been for most of its existence) kinda terrible. However rebellion against that terrible status quo is another of the many things Mage is and can be about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-31T20:52:11-07:00","id":1533441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533315#post1533315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Entropy, Stasis and Dynamism are not anthropomorphized forces like they are in Werewolf; they are absolutely NOT the same as Wyrm, Weaver and Wyld. Mage's Entropy isn't a 9 headed beast trying to physically devour the Tellurian; Mage's &quot;Triat&quot; is like the force of Gravity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Previous editions equated Stasis, Dynamism, and Entropy with Weaver, Wyld, and Wyrm; M20 explicitly doesn't. But even those mages who believe in the Triat split hairs and view them as anthropomorphized representatives of the Metaphysical Trinity, as opposed to the Metaphysical Trinity being attributes of the Triat. <br /> <br /> And there <i>are</i> indications that Entropy is broken, in setting: a Euthanatos Archmaster has been working to fix it. That <i>might</i> be a reference to the Wyrm; but if so, it's oblique and not very important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T09:29:38-07:00","id":1533490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533325#post1533325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having things be complicated is fine; as you said, it is realistic. I just think that having it be a complicated subjective reality is a step too far. All you really need is the basic spine of the Consensus for the magic system to function. Having it be a complicated reality is fine. Whether or not that reality is subjective or not should be up in the air.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is getting into an issue of terminology. I use the terms Consensus Reality and Subjective Reality interchangeably. Any reality where the Consensus partially but not fully changes reality, then, is a complicated subjective reality. As is any reality where the Consensus has complicated rules. As is any reality where the Consensus has unlimited reach but has to compete with other forces.<br /> <br /> Really, the only scenario where the Consensus exists but reality is not subjective is if mundane reality is 100% set and the Consensus only affects what mages themselves can do. We can keep that possibility open, yes, but it's one of the less meaningful options for the setting. That is, it isn't consistent with the history, motivation, tactics, or ideals of the major mage factions. It doesn't make it possible for the Traditions and Technocracy to have good justifications for their metaphysics, it just makes them both wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-02T12:00:55-07:00","id":1533497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533490#post1533490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is getting into an issue of terminology. I use the terms Consensus Reality and Subjective Reality interchangeably. Any reality where the Consensus partially but not fully changes reality, then, is a complicated subjective reality. As is any reality where the Consensus has complicated rules. As is any reality where the Consensus has unlimited reach but has to compete with other forces.<br /> <br /> Really, the only scenario where the Consensus exists but reality is not subjective is if mundane reality is 100% set and the Consensus only affects what mages themselves can do. We can keep that possibility open, yes, but it's one of the less meaningful options for the setting. That is, it isn't consistent with the history, motivation, tactics, or ideals of the major mage factions. It doesn't make it possible for the Traditions and Technocracy to have good justifications for their metaphysics, it just makes them both wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see what you are getting at, but I would say that a reality wherein the Consensus partially changes reality is partially subjective and partially objective. If there are some things that the Consensus cannot influence, then that reality is at least in part objective. Also, a reality that is subjective actually just renders both the Traditions and the Technocracy wrong. There is a difference between wanting reality to conform to a given model and actually thinking that reality conforms to a given model. In a reality that is totally subjective, you cannot actually have the philosophical conflict that is at the core of Mage. Instead, you just have a game that is about rendering certain types of magic Coincidental and other types of magic Vulgar. The war becomes more pragmatic and political rather than ideological in nature. The Technocracy can be used as an example here. The Technocracy has been portrayed as thinking that the universe is mechanistic in nature, and they have also been portrayed as thinking that Enlightened Science is a more useful method will-working than mystical types of will-working. Each of these portrayals can lead to a different image of the Technocracy. In the former portrayal, the Technocracy are earnest, and actually think that their cosmology accurately models reality. In the latter portrayal, the Technocracy does not necessarily have any ideological commitment to their cosmology, and may even recognize that it is not objectively correct, but they think that it would be the best reality for humanity to live in. These are two distinct lines of reasoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T07:11:18-07:00","id":1533512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533497#post1533497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see what you are getting at, but I would say that a reality wherein the Consensus partially changes reality is partially subjective and partially objective. If there are some things that the Consensus cannot influence, then that reality is at least in part objective.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why its a terminology difference. I would add, though, that it also depends on why the Consensus can't change the other parts. If there are other entities also pushing reality into shape, entities which are not absolute, then their effects are still part of subjective reality.<br /> <br /> I'll also add, even if we use absolute Earthly Foundations at the table for convenience, that doesn't mean they are actually absolute in universe. That's letting gaming abstractions become the reality of the game world and that usually doesn't work well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, a reality that is subjective actually just renders both the Traditions and the Technocracy wrong. There is a difference between wanting reality to conform to a given model and actually thinking that reality conforms to a given model. In a reality that is totally subjective, you cannot actually have the philosophical conflict that is at the core of Mage. Instead, you just have a game that is about rendering certain types of magic Coincidental and other types of magic Vulgar. The war becomes more pragmatic and political rather than ideological in nature. </div> </div> </div>Mage generally presents the idea that physical reality is malleable. Moral reality is never stated as such. In fact, everyone in Mage acts like they consider morality as largely objective. That is, they disagree about what the right thing is, but they don't think the other side can <i>become</i> right if they convince enough people. The moral and philosophical part of the Ascension War can continue regardless. It is the strategy of the war that depends on a complicated reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Technocracy has been portrayed as thinking that the universe is mechanistic in nature, and they have also been portrayed as thinking that Enlightened Science is a more useful method will-working than mystical types of will-working. Each of these portrayals can lead to a different image of the Technocracy. In the former portrayal, the Technocracy are earnest, and actually think that their cosmology accurately models reality. In the latter portrayal, the Technocracy does not necessarily have any ideological commitment to their cosmology, and may even recognize that it is not objectively correct, but they think that it would be the best reality for humanity to live in. These are two distinct lines of reasoning. </div> </div> </div>Those both will exist even in a part subjective, part objective reality, as you put it. And more besides. As long as reality is complicated enough that mages don't know what is actually happening (even if they think they do) we can have these differences of opinion make sense.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T11:53:35-07:00","id":1533523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533512#post1533512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why its a terminology difference. I would add, though, that it also depends on why the Consensus can't change the other parts. If there are other entities also pushing reality into shape, entities which are not absolute, then their effects are still part of subjective reality.<br /> <br /> I'll also add, even if we use absolute Earthly Foundations at the table for convenience, that doesn't mean they are actually absolute in universe. That's letting gaming abstractions become the reality of the game world and that usually doesn't work well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mage generally presents the idea that physical reality is malleable. Moral reality is never stated as such. In fact, everyone in Mage acts like they consider morality as largely objective. That is, they disagree about what the right thing is, but they don't think the other side can <i>become</i> right if they convince enough people. The moral and philosophical part of the Ascension War can continue regardless. It is the strategy of the war that depends on a complicated reality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Those both will exist even in a part subjective, part objective reality, as you put it. And more besides. As long as reality is complicated enough that mages don't know what is actually happening (even if they think they do) we can have these differences of opinion make sense.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot take much issue with any of the points that you presented, they seem quite reasonable. It does seem like the issue here is mostly terminology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-03T18:29:23-07:00","id":1533548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533512#post1533512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why its a terminology difference. I would add, though, that it also depends on why the Consensus can't change the other parts. If there are other entities also pushing reality into shape, entities which are not absolute, then their effects are still part of subjective reality.<br /> <br /> I'll also add, even if we use absolute Earthly Foundations at the table for convenience, that doesn't mean they are actually absolute in universe. That's letting gaming abstractions become the reality of the game world and that usually doesn't work well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me emphasize a point here: just because the Consensus can't change an Earthly Foundation, that doesn't mean that a <i>mage</i> can't, if only temporarily. In fact, given enough ranks in appropriate Spheres, there's nothing that a mage <i>can't</i> change. In <i>that</i> sense, the world of <b>Mage</b> <i>always</i> includes a subjective element, even in the extreme case of the Earthly Foundations covering <i>everything</i>, and the Consensus being powerless to change <i>anything</i> \u2014 which isn't anywhere close to the default for the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533512#post1533512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage generally presents the idea that physical reality is malleable. Moral reality is never stated as such. In fact, everyone in Mage acts like they consider morality as largely objective. That is, they disagree about what the right thing is, but they don't think the other side can <i>become</i> right if they convince enough people. The moral and philosophical part of the Ascension War can continue regardless. It is the strategy of the war that depends on a complicated reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something which I find very ironic, in the sense that it's the exact opposite of what you'd expect from the real world. Here, the laws of physics are absolute and nobody seriously doubts that; but the fundamental nature of <i>moral</i> reality is hotly debated, with moral relativists arguing that morals are a social construct and can be changed by changing society, whole moral absolutists argue things like morality coming from God it being intrinsic to nature. It seems weird that there are no moral relativists in <b>Mage</b>. <br /> <br /> Though I don't even know how a <i>mage</i> would go about changing moral reality; none of the existing Spheres seem to cover it, with the possible exception of Telos from <b>Ascension</b>. <br /> <br /> But getting back to the subject of the thread: <i>this</i>, the conflict over what's moral and what isn't, is the thing that <i>really</i> matters in the Ascension War; the question of the nature of physical reality pales in importance in comparison. Its only <i>real</i> importance is whether anyone <i>knows</i> its true nature and lies about it \u2014 because deception is one of those things that we vote as morally wrong. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530343-how-do-you-do-your-traditions-good-bad-or-hypocritical?p=1533512#post1533512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those both will exist even in a part subjective, part objective reality, as you put it. And more besides. As long as reality is complicated enough that mages don't know what is actually happening (even if they think they do) we can have these differences of opinion make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}